window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS=(window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101 | Grade 5 Genesis Bloodline Diamond Rice","paragraphs":["The next morning, Dexter woke up before his 5:00 AM alarm.","He stared at the ceiling, debating whether to sleep for another ten minutes until the alarm rang, but he shook his head and chuckled.","’If I sleep again, even the alarm won’t be able to wake me.’","He knew himself too well; if he closed his eyes again, he wouldn’t be getting up until noon.","He stretched and yawned. ’ Alright. Today is an exciting day. Lots of things to do.’","He dragged himself out of bed to start his morning routine. However, when he stepped into the bathroom to bath, he found the shower drain completely clogged.","Dexter sighed, pulling on a pair of cleaning gloves. He reached into the drain and pulled out a massive clump of hair with three different colors.","Silver, amber, and dark strands all tangled together.","His expression went completely deadpan. He obviously couldn’t tell the girls not to wash their hair, but the sheer volume of it was ridiculous. He shook his head, packed the hair into a plastic bag, tied it shut, and tossed it into the waste bin.","After cleaning up the bathroom and arranging the rooms, his mind drifted back to the three Bloodline Evolution Stones resting in his storage ring.","He had forgotten about them long enough. It was time to figure out how to give them to the girls.","His eyes lit up.","He could mix the bloodline stones into the food.","As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he had the accumulated knowledge and culinary techniques of masters far beyond his years.","If he could extract the raw essence from the stones and infuse them into a meal, the girls would absorb the bloodlines naturally without ever knowing they had consumed a priceless treasure.","Dexter closed his eyes, sifting rapidly through the vast library of Foodsmith memories embedded in his mind.","He searched for methods of extracting essence from solid spiritual objects, cross-referencing techniques for dissolving mana-dense materials into edible form.","One method surfaced above all others.","His Emperor Void Flame.","The 9th Heavenly Flame possessed unique properties that could gently melt and strip the pure essence from a Bloodline Evolution Stone without destroying or degrading its core properties.","The extracted essence could then be seamlessly blended into a spiritual meal, binding with the ingredients on a molecular level.","’ Now, that’s a solid plan.’","Dexter’s grin widened as the full plan crystallized in his mind.","He would use the Diamond Rice, combined with the Heavenly Treasures he still had in storage, and the fresh ingredients he had purchased from the market.","Together, he would formulate a perfect Grade-Five meal. A rice-based dish so refined that the bloodline essence would be completely undetectable, absorbed effortlessly by the girls’ bodies as they ate.","He had considered using the stones on himself. But a Bloodline Evolution Stone could only be used once per person. If he took one, his Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline would advance a single grade, but not game-changing.","More importantly, he only had three stones for three girls. If he took one for himself, one girl would be left out, he didn’t think it would be fair.","Dexter retrieved the three shimmering crystals from his storage ring.","Then summoned a thin, controlled thread of his Emperor Void Flame—a warm white fire flickered gently above his fingertips unlike the violent crimson of his combat flames.","With precision control of a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he wrapped the white flames around the first stone.","The crystal began to glow.","Slowly, the outer shell of the stone liquefied, releasing a shimmering, vapor that rose into the air like distilled starlight.","Dexter guided the vapor with his mana, channeling it directly into the pot of cooking Diamond Rice.","The rice grains absorbed the essence instantly, their crystalline structures glowing faintly before returning to normal.","To the naked eye, nothing had changed. But Dexter’s Gastronomy body could sense the transformation as the bloodline essence blended perfectly with the grain.","He repeated the process with the second and third stones, infusing each one into a separate portion of the meal.","Then he added the Heavenly Treasures: thin slices of Origin Sun Fruit, crushed Star Essence threads of Millennium Blood Ginseng and various others.","The Diamond Rice absorbed everything, the grains swelling with concentrated energy.","The kitchen filled with an aroma so rich, that Dexter himself had to suppress the urge to grab a spoon and dig in.","The fragrance wassweet, savory, earthy, and faintly celestial, with a warmth that seemed to seep into the walls themselves.","By 7 o’clock, the meal was complete.","════════════════════","[Name: Celestial Bloodline Genesis Rice]","[Grade: 5 Arcane Meal]","════════════════════","[Description:","A legendary rice dish crafted from Diamond Rice and a collection of rare Heavenly Treasures, refined through the Emperor Void Flame. Every crystal-like grain contains perfectly balanced life essence, nourishing the body from the cellular level while awakening its hidden potential.]","[Effects]","• Permanently increases Physical Strength by 20%.","• Greatly enhances the body’s natural healing ability, increasing recovery speed by 300%.","• Removes accumulated toxins and impurities from the body.","• Greatly restores stamina, vitality, and mana.","[Hidden Effect]","• Randomly awakens one compatible bloodline from the sealed Bloodline Essence contained within the meal.","• If the user already possesses a bloodline, there is a chance for it to evolve instead of awakening a new one.","═══════════════════","Over the past few days, Dexter and the girls had fallen into an unspoken morning routine.","He would cook from 5 until 7am. During that time, Lyra and Selene would wake up, go to the bathroom, brush their teeth, bathe, and freshen up on their own.","Once they were done, Dexter would go to their room to help Mira with her morning routine.","Afterward, all four of them would eat breakfast together.","This morning, Dexter had made one small adjustment. He had opened the kitchen window to ventilate the cooking smoke, but he had also closed the door connecting the kitchen to the hallway.","He knew from experience that if Lyra caught even a faint whiff of the Diamond Rice cooking, she would materialize in the kitchen like a hungry ghost, and he wouldn’t be able to finish plating the food.","So the door stayed closed. The window stayed open. And the aroma drifted outside into the morning air instead.","Dexter washed his hands at the kitchen sink, preparing to go to the girls’ room to help Mira.","He dried his hands on a towel and was about to step into the hallway when—","\"BANG!\"","A loud, violent crash echoed through the house.","Dexter froze.","\"CRACK!\"","Another one? It was followed by shattering of soemthing.","’ What just happened right now?’","His body tensed and he surged forward, rushing toward the girls’ bedroom, but as he reached the hallway, he realized the sound wasn’t coming from the bedroom.","It was coming from the bathroom.","Dexter sprinted to the bathroom door and threw it open.","He was stunned by what he saw.","Mira was sitting in her wheelchair, half-naked.","Her shirt had been removed, leaving her upper body exposed but her spectral arma hovering behind her covered her exposed skin. But that wasn’t what made Dexter stunned.","It was the massive crack on the bathroom wall with chunks of plaster and tile scattered across the wet floor.","Not to mention the toilet had also been shattered, as if someone had gripped it with inhuman force and squeezed.","The shower head had been ripped clean off its mount, the metal pipe bent at an ugly angle.","Dexter stood in the doorway, stunned."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102 | Please Feed Me","paragraphs":["\"What did you do?\"","Mira’s head hung low, her hair hanging forward to cover her face as she stared at the ground ad though it was the most interesting thing in the world.","She looked like a child who had broken something expensive and was waiting for the scolding. Her spectral arms had retracted slightly, curling behind her shoulders as if trying to hide.","Dexter exhaled slowly through his nose.","He understood immediately what had happened. Mira had tried to take care of herself. She had wanted to be independent, to handle her own morning routine without needing his help.","But her control over the spectral arms was still crude. She had probably gripped the shower head too hard, yanked it off the wall, panicked, and lashed out, destroying the toilet and punching a hole through the wall in the process.","Dexter rolled his eyes then stepped into the bathroom carefully, avoiding the broken ceramic.","\"Since you’re not really proficient with your mana arms yet,\" he said, his voice calm and even, \"let me be the one to take care of you until you are. For now, don’t enter the bathroom without my permission.\"","He didn’t scold her but what he said seemed to have more effect.","Mira blinked her eyes.","’He didn’t complain?’","She expected more but it turned out Dexter wasn’t really mad.","However, she didn’t look up or argue. She simply sat there with her ears burning red.","Dexter turned to assess the damage. He walked to the kitchen, grabbed a wooden stool, and carried it back to the bathroom. He climbed up, retrieved the mangled shower head from the floor, and examined the broken metal pipe.","\"Whoosh!\"","He immediately summoned a thin thread of Emperor Void Flame, wrapping it carefully around the severed joint, fusing the pipe and shower head back together as if they had never been broken.","Satisfied, he stepped down from the stool and turned to Mira.","She was still unusually quiet.","Dexter washed her hair carefully, lathering shampoo into her scalp and rinsing it with warm water from the repaired shower. He scrubbed her shoulders, her arms, her back and her legs with a soft sponge without a single change in expression.","But one could only imagine the insane struggle coursing through his veins.","Especially since his bloodline advanced to Ancient grade, he was becoming more and more active.","Thankfully, the pain managed to keep the dragon from rising. Otherwise, Mira wouldn’t be the only embarrassed one.","He supporting her weight against his chest as he washed the rest of her body.","Throughout the entire process, Mira said nothing.","Not a single mocking word or observations. Nor even clever jabs about him being gay or something.","Dexter found it both amusing and oddly cute.","Mira always had something to say. Always. The fact that she was completely quiet meant she was genuinely embarrassed.","He dried her off with a fresh towel, patted her skin dry, and dressed her with a purple sundress covered in small white flowers.","Mira’s eyes immediately snapped open when she saw it.","She gritted her teeth and glared at him.","Dexter shrugged innocently. \"What?\"","Mira continued to glare, her crimson eyes narrowing to slits. Then she let out a sharp snort.","\"Hmph!\"","Dexter smirked and dressed her in the flower sundress, adjusting the straps over her shoulders. He brushed her damp hair until it fell neatly over her shoulders, then wheeled her out to the kitchen.","Lyra and Selene were already seated at the dining table. Lyra’s eyes were locked onto the covered pot on the stove with the focus of a predator tracking prey.","Selene sat beside her, eyes closed, her echolocation painting a perfect picture of the kitchen around her.","Dexter served the meal.","He ladled the glowing, star-flecked Diamond Rice into four bowls.","The rice looked and smelled exactly like the premium Arcane meals he had made last night.","He placed a bowl in front of Selene. Her hand reached out instinctively, finding the spoon without hesitation.","He placed three bowls in front of Lyra. She didn’t even wait for him to sit down before grabbing her spoon.","Finally, he placed a bowl in front of Mira. She looked at it, then at him, and then summoned her spectral arms.","One arm reached for the fork.","This time, her grip was noticeably steadier than the night before.","Dexter sat down with his own portion and began eating.","The four of them ate in silence.","Dexter glanced at each of the girls as they ate. He couldn’t wait to see what they would become.","The food was, as always, nothing short of extraordinary.","The moment the girls took their first bites, their eyes widened in unison.","Mira’s spoon, froze halfway to her mouth.","\"How much Diamond Rice do you actually have?\" she asked, her crimson eyes narrowing with suspicion. She had assumed the previous meal was a rare, one-time luxury. The fact that Dexter was serving it again meant he either had a secret supplier or an impossibly deep storage.","Dexter shrugged casually. \"Why do you ask? Do you want to cook for us?\"","Mira glared at him, recognizing the jab instantly. She turned her head away and resumed feeding herself, her spectral arm trembling as it guided the fork toward her lips.","But after two more bites, the overwhelming taste of the meal broke through her pride.","The Diamond Rice seemed to melt on her tongue, each grain releasing a burst of warm, savory energy that spread through her damaged meridians like sunlight through cracks in a wall.","Her spectral arm faltered, the fork hovering uselessly in the air as her concentration wavered.","She glanced at the arm and then at Dexter.","She hated herself for what she was about to say as she gritted her teeth but eventually said it.","\"Please feed me,\" she murmured, her voice so small it was barely audible.","Dexter’s grin could have lit up the entire bungalow. \"Of course, my lady.\"","Mira pursed her lips so tightly they turned white, a deep flush crawling up her neck. She almost regretted asking. But the aroma wafting from the bowl was simply too tantalizing that it overrode her stubborn pride."]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103 | Ewwwww!","paragraphs":["Dexter’s grin could have lit up the entire bungalow. \"Of course, my lady.\"","Dexter picked up her fork, scooped a portion of the glowing rice, and guided it to her lips. Mira opened her mouth without protesting, closing her eyes as the warmth spread through her body once more.","From that point on, the girls ate silently.","Each one was entirely consumed by the food before them, as if it were the most delicious thing they had ever tasted in their entire lives.","Lyra finished her three portions in under three minutes, breaking her personal record. Selene finished hers in five. Even Mira, being fed by Dexter, finished in ten.","Dexter stared at the empty bowls, his expression slightly stunned. \"You girls were faster than usual today.\"","He shook his head in disbelief as the girls reached for their water glasses, drinking lots of water to wash down the rich meal.","’ Thank you.’","The soft, melodic voice of Lyra drifted into Dexter’s mind like a gentle breeze. She was looking down at her empty bowl, her cheeks faintly pink, but her gratitude was genuine and warm.","Dexter smiled and projected a gentle thought back. ’ You’re welcome.’","\"Thank you,\" Selene muttered aloud. Her voice was barely louder than a mosquito’s whisper, but Dexter’s enhanced hearing caught every syllable clearly. He nodded at her with a soft smile.","Selene didn’t leave the table.","While Lyra and Mira eventually moved to the living room, Selene remained seated in her chair, her pale eyes closed.","But Dexter could feel her Echolocation talent was focused entirely on him.","He glanced at her curiously, wondering what she wanted.","’ Does she want to hold my arm again?’","The memory of her clinging to him like a kitten on heat the previous afternoon made him smile goofily.","But right now, she didn’t say anything and was simply sitting there, as though listening to him move.","Dexter dried his hands and turned to face the living room before speaking.","\"I need to go out this afternoon,\" he announced. \"But I’ll make lunch for you girls first before I leave.\"","Mira who was in the living room frowned slightly.","But didnr say anything.","Lyra, however, spoke. Once she saw the text written by the ai glasses.","She looked up with her dark eyes.","’You’ve been going out too much lately,’ she projected into Dexter’s mind, her mental voice carrying a rare edge of displeasure.","Selene’s eyes snapped open as her head tilted toward Dexter, her expression unreadable.","Dexter held up a reassuring hand. \"It’s just a spar. I made a bet with someone. If I win, I get rich.\"","Mira’s eyes flickered open. \"And if you lose?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"I gain nothing, and I lose nothing.\"","Mira frowned, her brow creasing. \"If you win, you gain something. If you lose, you lose nothing.\" She paused. \"That doesn’t sound right.\"","Dexter didn’t elaborate. He simply smiled and turned back to the sink.","Mira didn’t press the issue. In truth, she didn’t particularly care where Dexter went or what he did.","Her mind was occupied by something she hadn’t told anyone.","Last night, her right index finger had moved and it wasn’t fake.","She had spent three years experiencing phantom sensations, false flickers of hope that her nerves were repairing, only to be crushed every time.","She didn’t plan to tell Dexter nor had she told Lyra or Selene. The Grand Cosmos Scripture and the Arcane meals were working.","Her nerves were slowly repairing themselves.","She couldn’t wait for the day she could move on her own again, but until then, she would keep this small, precious hope locked inside her heart.","***","Dexter was deep in thought as he dried the last plate.","The bloodline essence hidden in the Diamond Rice would begin taking effect soon. With any luck, the girls would awaken their new bloodlines before the day was over.","Dexter picked up the trash bin and headed for the front door. \"I’m taking out the trash,\" he announced to no one in particular. \"I’ll be right back.\"","He stepped outside into the cool morning air. The neighborhood was quiet, most residents already at work. A few birds chirped from the power lines above.","As he carried the trash bin toward the curb, his eyes caught movement across the street, opposite their house.","An elderly woman was kneeling in her front garden, carefully watering a row of colorful flowers with a battered watering can.","Dexter paused as he recognized her instantly.","It was the woman he had seen this yesterday morning.","And also the same old woman who Tessa said had bet against him returning.","He smiled wryly and raised his hand in a friendly wave.","The old woman glanced up, looked at him for exactly one second smiled and then turned back to her flowers.","Dexter rubbed his nose. \"Tough crowd.\"","He was about to set the trash bin down by the curb when he felt something wet on his left foot. He looked down.","Foul, grayish water was dripping from the bottom of the trash bag, pooling directly on his bare left foot. The liquid had leaked from a torn hole in the trash bag inside and was now seeping on his leg.","\"Ewwwww!\"","Dexter recoiled violently, his face twisting in disgust. He shoved the trash bag into the bin, grabbed the garden hose from the side of the house, and turned it on full blast.","\"Whooosh!\"","He directed the cold water at his foot, scrubbing furiously with his other foot.","\"Oh, that is disgusting. That is so disgusting—\"","As he was hosing down his foot, a familiar voice drifted down from above.","\"That must have been terrifying for you.\"","Dexter raised his head and he saw a young girl opposite him.","Tessa was sitting on top of the tall brick wall that divided his compound from hers. Her legs dangled casually over the edge, her red hair tied back with a strip of cloth, her green eyes watching him with amusement.","Dexter stared up at her, water still spraying against his foot."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104 | Meeting Henry!","paragraphs":["Tess looked down at him with amusement in her eyes as she looked at his feet.","\"That must have been disgusting...\"","\"Yeah,\" Dexter muttered flatly, still hosing down his foot. \"It was.\"","\"Good morning,\" Tessa said cheerfully as she smiled at him.","Dexter sighed. \"Good morning.\"","Tessa blinked her eyes and flicked her long hair to the back.","Dexter turned off the tap and grabbed a rag from the hook on the wall, drying his leg.","\"So why are you once again on my wall?\" he asked, raising an eyebrow. \"If you wanted to greet me, you could just come to the front gate like a normal person.\"","Tessa shrugged, swinging her legs. \"This is more comfortable. And it’s a shortcut.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","He shook his foot a few times to flick off the remaining droplets, then looked back up at the girl perched on his wall like a gargoyle.","\"Shouldn’t you be in school?\"","She blinked.","\"School?\"","For a second she looked genuinely confused before lightly smacking her forehead.","\"Oh...\"","\"We’re on break.\"","Dexter narrowed his eyes.","Something about that answer sounded suspicious.","She looked like she was making it up on the spot.","Maybe she skipped school, but it wasn’t really any of his business.","Tessa tilted her head, her nostrils flaring slightly. Her expression shifted from amused to genuinely curious.","\"Were you cooking this morning?\"","Dexter paused. He knew immediately she was referring to the meal he had prepared for the girls.","The kitchen window had been open to ventilate the smoke, while the door was locked for Lyra not to smell it.","The aroma of that particular dish was potent enough to travel a considerable distance.","He thought for a moment, then nodded slowly. \"Yeah. Why?\"","Tessa’s eyes immediately lit up like two green fireworks. \"Really? I didn’t know you were such a good cook!\"","Dexter shrugged. \"Well. Don’t judge a book by its cover.\"","Tessa smiled in excitement. \"Can I have some? It smells really, really nice. Please? Can I have some? Please?\"","Dexter blinked at the rapid-fire begging. He shook his head. \"Not a chance. It’s all finished.\"","Tessa’s expression collapsed into the most devastating puppy-dog eyes Dexter had ever seen.","Her green eyes widened and her lower lip pushed out in an exaggerated pout as it trembled as though she was about to cry.","\"Pretty please? Please, please, please, please, please—\"","Dexter lips curled. ’ How can ’please’ be pretty?’","\"Fine!\" Dexter held up both hands in surrender.","\"Fine. All right.\"","He had originally left a small portion in the pot for Lyra, knowing full well that she would be hungry.","But seeing Tessa begging on his wall reminded him of the pastries he had purchased from her family’s bakery for the girls.","He had forgotten it when the girls rejected his jewelries, just remembering right now.","He could give the girls the pastries as an afternoon treat instead, and give Tessa the little bit of rice left.","It wasn’t truly a full portion, just the scraped remnants clinging to the bottom of the pot that was maybe half a plate at most.","He looked up at Tessa. \"It’s only a little bit. Are you sure you’d want something so small?\"","Tessa nodded vigorously, her red ponytail bouncing. \"Yes! It’s just smells really good this morning through your window. I tried to respect your space, I really did, but the aroma was tooooo tempting. I had no choice but to come over. My feet just brought me here on their own.\"","Dexter chuckled. It sounded more like a compliment than an excuse, making his ego rise a bit.","\"Alright alright. I will get it for you.\"","He shook his head with a faint smile and walked back inside.","He entered the kitchen, scraped the bottom of the pot carefully, and managed to gather a modest portion onto a small plate.","He covered it with a clean plate to keep the warmth in, then walked back outside.","The moment Tessa saw the plate, her eyes sparkled.","She immediately leapt off the wall, landing silently on his side of the compound as she snatched the plate from his hands with the speed of a hawk.","She lifted the upper plate, brought the plate to her nose, and inhaled deeply. Her eyes fluttered shut.","\"Ah...\" she sighed, her voice dripping with contentment. \"It truly smells heavenly.\"","Then her eyes snapped open. She looked at Dexter sharply and suspiciously.","\"Are you an Arcane Chef?\"","Dexter’s blinked his eyes.","How had she guessed so quickly?","He shrugged, his face expressionless.","\"Maybe.\"","Tessa’s eyes narrowed slightly, studying him as a brilliant idea popped up in her head. Her eyes twinkled mischievously.","\"All right. Maybe I have a business plan for you.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Business plan?\"","Before Tessa could respond, she suddenly turned her head toward her family’s compound and cupped her hands around her mouth.","\"Hey! Come meet our neighbor!\"","She seem to have forgotten something but she immediately corrected herself. \"D-ad! Come meet Dexter.\"","Dexter stared at her. \"You’re talking to your dad?\"","From the other side of the wall, a deep voice called back. \"Tessa. Don’t just climb into another person’s compound through their fence. It’s rude and disrespectful.\"","Tessa rolled her eyes. Then she turned back to Dexter, her expression brightening again. \"Dexter, come meet my d-ad!\"","Dexter thought he might have heard some hesitation in her tone. He blinked slowly then sighed as he walked through his front gate to his neighbors place.","Halfway there, the gate on the other side swung open, and a man stepped out.","He was tall, almost exactly Dexter’s height, but broader with thick shoulders and muscular arms.","His large muscle was visible beneath the rolled sleeves of a simple baker’s apron.","He looked to be in his early forties as he smiled and extended his hand toward Dexter.","\"Dexter, right? I’m Henry, Tessa’s father.\"","Dexter shook his hand.The grip was firm and strong.","He replied with a respectful smile. \"I’m Dexter.\""]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105 | Henry And Tessa","paragraphs":["The moment their hands clasped, Dexter felt it as he registered the mans strength.","Peak Superhuman Realm.","Dexter maintained his composure, but he was internally surprised.","This baker was actually a Peak Superhuman expert and he was running a bakery.","\"So,\" Henry said, his voice deep and steady. \"You’re the young man who married the three girls from the Calloway, Vance, and Frost families.\"","Dexter rubbed the back of his head in mild embarrassment. Seemed like everyone had associated him with the three families.","\"Yes, that’s correct.\"","Henry’s slowly nodded his head and held Dexter’s gaze for a long moment, then released his hand.","\"Good grip,\" he remarked mildly.","\"I also heard about what happened during the monster outbreak,\" he said quietly. \"And also about the highway incident.\"","Dexter’s expression remained neutral. \"News travels fast.\"","\"In this neighborhood, yes.\" Henry studied him for another moment. Then he nodded, seemingly arriving at some private conclusion. \"If you need help, you’re welcome here anytime, Dexter. Any friend of my daughter’s is a friend of ours.\"","He extended his hand again. Dexter shook it.","\"Thatsbwyiye nice of you. Thank you. I will take my leave now.\"","Henry clapped him on the shoulder.","Dexter waved goodbye. \"Take care.\"","\"You too,\" Henry replied, watching as Dexter turned and walked back through his front gate.","Dexter disappeared into his compound, and Henry remained standing on the sidewalk for a few long seconds.","His warm smile slowly faded as his expression hardened.","He slipped his hands into his pockets, glanced once more at Dexter’s closed gate, then turned to look at the wall where Tessa was jumping over to their side.","He didn’t say anything and simply turned then walked back into his own home.","***","The Wren family home was deceptively ordinary from the outside, with a few potted flowers on the front porch and fresh paint on the walls.","But the moment Henry stepped through the front door, the illusion of normalcy faltered.","The interior was almost entirely empty.","There were no paintings on the walls, no family pictures, or decorations or even bookshelves or tables.","There was just two simple wooden chairs facing a small television set in the center of a empty living room, with a single center table between them.","It was as though no one was living in the house.","Henry entered the house and saw Tessa sitting on one of the two chairs.","She was staring at the plate of rice in her hand, her fork frozen mid-air.","Henry squinted at her. \"Should you be eating that?\"","Tessa rolled her eyes. \"Relax. If they wanted to send someone, they wouldn’t send him. F-Rank affinity, no backing, no connections. I think he’d be more worried about his wives than try troubling us.\"","She took another bite, chewing thoughtfully.","\"Moreover, why would people from Imperius Continent plant an assassin like him? It wouldn’t make sense.\"","Henry gazed at Tessa, then at the food in her hand, then shook his head slowly. \"We have to be careful, Tessa. I, old lady Jane and the rest are here to protect you but we can’t afford to let them ever find us.\"","Tessa shot her ’father’ a sharp glare. \"Watch your tone. I’m blending in. That’s what we’re supposed to do, isn’t it? I’m not making any trouble.\"","She paused, then tilted her head with an indifferent look. \"If you wanted to keep a low profile, why did you open a bakery in the first place? That doesn’t exactly scream ’invisible.’\"","Henry opened his mouth. Then closed it. He had no reply for that.","\"Just be careful, my lady.\" he said quietly after a long silence. \"Until you finish awakening your bloodline, there’s nothing much you can do to protect yourself if something goes wrong.\"","Tessa pouted, her cheeks puffing out like an angry chipmunk. \"You’re annoying.\"","She snatched the plate off the table, stomped toward her room, and kicked the door shut behind her with a bang sound.","Henry stood alone in the empty living room, staring at the closed door. He let out a slow, heavy breath and rubbed his temples with calloused fingers.","But his eyes suddenly flashed as he checked his arms. His skin suddenly trembled as draconic scales ripped out of his skin and then retracted back.","\"It’s almost time.\"","***","Back in his bungalow, Dexter prepared for the afternoon sparring session.","The training facility where the bet would take place was located deeper in the city and a considerable distance from the outer district.","He needed to leave soon if he wanted to arrive on time.","The girls were still meditating.","Lyra was on the couch, her eyes closed.","Mira was at the window, cultivating in silence. Selene was in the bedroom, equally absorbed.","Dexter moved quietly through the kitchen. He pulled the pastries he had bought from Tessa out of the microwave and considered where to put them.","He knew that if he placed them in front of Lyra, she would devour them in seconds, regardless of whether she had just eaten a full meal.","Instead, he decided to text her later in the afternoon when she got hungry. That way, the pastries would serve their intended purpose as a snack rather than an extension of breakfast.","He heated the pastries briefly with his Emperor Void Flame.","The white flames infused the dough with a subtle warmth that would never fade, even after a full day, the pastries would remain perfectly hot and fresh, as if they had just come out of the oven.","It was one of the many convenient side effects of cooking with a Heavenly Flame.","He did the same with the lunch he had prepared.","Even though he had used ordinary market ingredients rather than Heavenly Treasures, the meal had still condensed into a Grade-One Arcane dish.","His Great Grandmaster Foodsmith skills had become so refined that even basic ingredients, when combined with his mana and flame, produced meals with tangible restorative properties.","He packed the lunch into covered containers and set them on the counter where the girls could easily find them.","Cleaned himself up, took care of Mira without her permission and then spoke to the girls.","\"I’m heading out for the sparring session,\" he announced.","Lyra opened one eye, looked at him, and simply nodded before closing it again. A moment later, her soft, melodic voice echoed in his mind.","’Good Luck!’"]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106 | He’s Your Husband Afterall","paragraphs":["Lyra opened one eye, looked at him, and simply nodded before closing it again. A moment later, her soft, melodic voice echoed in his mind.","’Good luck.’","Dexter smiled warmly and projected his thoughts back. ’ Thank you.’","Mira didn’t react and Selene was in the room.","But Dexter could feel Selene’s echolocation pulses focused on him,","He turned toward the front door, slipped on his shoes, and reached for the handle.","\"Knock. Knock. Knock.\"","Dexter paused, his hand hovering over the knob. He frowned, wondering who it could be.","’ Oh shit. The beds.’","The beds he had bought yesterday and for the girls, the delivery must have arrived.","Dexter opened the front door to find two delivery workers in matching uniforms standing on his porch. One of them held out a clipboard.","\"Are you Dexter Ashford?\"","\"Yes.\"","The worker extended the clipboard and a pen. \"Sign here, please.\"","Dexter scribbled his signature and stepped aside, gesturing them in.","Originally, he had only ordered two beds. But at the last minute before placing the order, he had changed his mind.","Instead of two, he had purchased four, one for each of the girls.","The expense had drained nearly all his money but Dexter was expecting payment from the Hero Association so he wasn’t quite worried.","More importantly, every investment he made in his wives would return a hundredfold through the system.","So it was a win-win situation.","Dexter guided the workers through the hallway.","First, he directed them to the girls’ bedroom.","\"You remove the original beds and the three new ones here side by side.\"","Then he led them to his own small room for the fourth.","The workers nodded and got to work, carrying the heavy mattress frames and bed components through the narrow hallway.","Mira, who had been cultivating silently by the living room window, furrowed her brows.","Across the room, both Lyra and Selene wore similarly troubled expressions, their brows knit in irritation.","Dexter saw this and immediately knew the noise might have been disturbing for them.","Dexter scratched the back of his head, feeling a pang of guilt for disrupting their cultivation.","He walked over to the girls and spoke in an apologetic tone.","\"I’m sorry about the noise. I just wanted to make your sleeping arrangements more comfortable. You girls have been sharing two merged beds, and I know that can’t be good for your backs. With these new beds, everything should be properly set up, and you’ll be able to rest comfortably.\"","Mira’s eyes snapped open. \"We never complained.\"","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"You never needed to. I just can’t bear you three being uncomfortable when it’s within my power to change it.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the room immediately went still.","[Mira + 3 Affection]","[Lyra + 7 Affection]","[Selene + 10 Affection]","Mira’s lips twitched and her crimson eyes flickered with warmth.","She immediately closed her eyes, lowered her head, and snorted softly, pretending to concentrate on her cultivation.","But the faint pink tinge creeping up her neck betrayed her.","Lyra’s eyes had snapped open as well.","The families that had married them off had treated them as burdens. The world had treated them as broken relics.","But Dexter... Dexter kept on trying his utmost to make them comfortable.","No matter his intentions, he was obviously doing this from his heart.","’Thank you,’Lyra’s soft voice echoed in Dexter’s mind.","Dexter smiled. ’You’re welcome.’","Selene hadn’t moved. Her pale eyes remained closed, and her face expressionless.","But inside, the cracks around her frosted heart continued to increase.","Dexter smiled faintly.","\"They just need about thirty to forty minutes to finish setting everything up. I’m sorry for the inconvenience and the noise.\"","The girls nodded.","Before returning to supervise the workers,","Dexter glanced at Mira’s neck. The Type-5 Protective Amulet rested against her collarbone making him sigh in relief.","He had temporarily lowered the Type-5 House Protection Barrier so the delivery workers could enter the property. That meant, for the next forty minutes, the house was theoretically vulnerable.","But the Protective Amulet on Mira’s neck was more than capable of shielding all three girls if someone managed to slip past the lowered barrier.","And Dexter himself remained on high alert.","If anyone so much as twitched in the wrong direction, he would know.","***","35 minutes later, the workers were done.","Three fluffy, queen-sized beds now occupied the girls’ bedroom, each fitted with fresh sheets, thick comforters, and soft pillows.","The fourth bed, a similarly plush mattress sat in Dexter’s small room.","Dexter touched and admired his new bed. The mattress was incredibly soft, with cloud-like surface that seemed to swallow you whole the moment you lay down.","\"So nice!\"","He couldn’t help but smile.","Then he quickly cleared his throat and straightened his posture.","’A man shouldn’t behave like a woman, giggling over a fluffy bed.’","Hw quickly stood up and chided himself. He should have bought a harder, firmer mattress for himself. Something masculine.","But the bed was just so... fluffy.","After the workers left, he walked back to the living room.","\"You can go in and check the beds now,\" he told the girls. \"If you want to rest or close your eyes for a bit, the room is ready.\"","All three nodded.","But none of them moved.","They remained exactly where they were.","Dexter shrugged. Patience was part of the process.","After settling the remaining logistics around the house, he turned to the girls.","\"I’m heading to the city for the spar,\" he announced.","’Good luck,’Lyra’s voice echoed in his mind immediately.","\"Good luck,\" Selene murmured softly.","Dexter smiled. \"Thank you.\"","Mira, as usual, said nothing.","Dexter opened the front door, stepped out, and pulled it shut behind him.","\"I’ll be back soon,\" he called through the closed door.","***","Inside the silent living room, Mira frowned at the closed door as Dexter’s footsteps faded down the street.","Lyra caught sight of Mira’s worried expression and smiled.","’If you’re worried about him, why didn’t you tell him not to go?’ Her voice echoed gently in Mira’s mind.","Mira’s head snapped toward Lyra, her crimson eyes narrowing.","But her face quickly hardened into her usual mask of cold indifference.","\"He’s a man,\" Mira said flatly, \"Of course he’ll do whatever he wants regardless of what anyone says.\"","’He’s also your husband,’ Lyra’s voice teased, the mental tone laced with a playful, almost mischievous edge. ’He would listen to you if you told him to stay.’"]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107 | Simon & The Strange Sister","paragraphs":["\"He’s also your husband,\" Lyra’s voice teased, the mental tone laced with a playful, mischievous edge. ’He would listen to you if you told him to stay.’","Mira’s eyes narrowed sharply as she glared at the seemingly tranquil Lyra on the couch.","She opened her mouth to retort, but found she had no immediate comeback.","Lyra’s lips curled into a faint, knowing smile. Her dark eyes remained closed, but beneath that calm exterior, a spark of her old self, the rumored \"Shadow Saintess\" with two faces, was starting to reveal itself.","There was a certain ’madness’ in her quiet amusement, a subtle shift from the broken, withdrawn girl she had been just days ago.","Mira scoffed, turned her head away, and forcefully closed her eyes, plunging herself back into cultivation to escape the telepath’s teasing.","***","Meanwhile, Dexter had booked a taxi heading deeper into the city. He settled into the back seat and gave the driver the name of the district.","A few minutes later, the taxi slowed down as two more passengers hailed it from the curb.","The car stopped, and a young man and a young woman climbed in. The woman took the front passenger seat, while the young man squeezed into the back beside Dexter.","As the taxi pulled back onto the road, Dexter frowned slightly. His enhanced senses automatically scanned the new arrivals.","’Superhuman Realm.’","The man beside him was at the Second or Third Stage of the Superhuman Realm.","The woman in the front seat was even stronge, radiating the unmistakable pressure of a Peak Superhuman.","’ When did Superhuman experts become so much?’","Dexter was genuinely surprised.","Ever since he had entered the Superhuman Realm himself, he was realizing just how many powerful experts hid in plain sight in this city.","To find two of them sharing a random public taxi was quite a coincidence.","The car drove in silence for a while before the woman in the front turned her head slightly, addressing the young man in the back.","\"Are you prepared for the tournament?\" she asked in a cold voice.","The young man straightened his posture. \"Yes, sister. I am prepared.\"","The woman snorted. \"That’s what you said last time before you lost to Colin. Just make sure not to lose this time. Don’t lose our family’s face again.\"","The young man scratched his head, looking a bit sheepish, but then his gaze hardened. \"Don’t worry, sister. I’ll try my best.\"","The woman’s expression darkened. \"Try your best? You best isn’t enough. Try your hardest. If you lose this time, it’s not just about losing face. Our parents will be disappointed. And more importantly, I will be disappointed in you.\"","Dexter tuned out the rest of their conversation, turning his gaze to the city skyline rolling past the window.","’ Tournament ?’","He hadn’t heard anything about a tournament happening in the city, but it wasn’t really his concern.","About five minutes later, the young man suddenly turned to face Dexter.","\"This weather is quite nice, isn’t it?\" the young man asked with a bright, friendly tone.","Dexter didn’t respond immediately. He glanced to his side, realizing the young man who looked to be about his own age was trying to make small talk.","\"Yeah,\" Dexter replied neutrally. \"It is.\"","The young man smiled, extending his hand. \"Hi, my name is Simon.\"","Dexter looked at the outstretched hand, then at the young man’s face.","Simon was wearing a wide, somewhat foolish grin, his eyes bright with a naive, harmless energy.","Dexter blinked, then eventually took the hand and shook it.","\"I’m Dexter.\"","\"Dexter,\" Simon repeated, his smile widening.","\"That’s quite a unique name.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"My parents were jokesters.\"","Simon chuckled at the rhyme. \"Are you heading to the Titan Training Center too?\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yeah. I assume you’re going there too?\"","\"Yeah! There’s a city-wide tournament being hosted there today,\" Simon explained enthusiastically. \"I’m trying to win the tournament and gain some reputation in the city.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Alright. Good luck with that.\"","\"Are you also going for the tournament?\" Simon asked, leaning in slightly.","Dexter shook his head. \"No, I’m just going there for a friendly spar with someone.\"","\"Oh, alright!\" Simon said cheerfully, not pressing for details. \"I hope you win your spar.\"","Dexter offered a small nod. \"I hope you win your tournament too.\"","Simon beamed.","Ten minutes later, the taxi pulled to a stop in front of a massive, building.","The building was enormous, with reinforced walls as a large, metallic archway loomed over the entrance.","’Titan Elite Training Facility’","The three of them stepped out of the taxi and approached the main gate.","Simon and his sister produced their Hero Identification cards, which the guards scanned.","\"Go in.\"","The guards spoke.","The two people headed inside the gate.","The moment Dexter was out of earshot, Simon’s sister grabbed her brother by the arm and yanked him to the side.","\"Simon, why are you being friendly with everyone?\" she hissed. \"You don’t know his intentions! He might be trying to get close to our family, or to me, through you.\"","Simon shook his head, his expression baffled. \"We entered the vehicle before us. He was already sitting in the back when we hailed it. How would he have known we were going to be in the same taxi?\"","\"Moreover, how could he know exactly where your car would break down? How could he know we would be hailing this exact taxi? Sister, you’re being way too paranoid.\"","The sister shook her head.","His sister’s lips curled into a thin, disapproving line. \"And you’re being way too carefree. It’s better to be paranoid than to be taken advantage of. You can greet him or talk to him, but don’t get too close.\"","Simon sighed but eventually nodded in reluctant agreement.","As they finished their conversation and approached the gate, they caught the tail end of Dexter’s interaction with the guard. Dexter casually pulled out a sleek, golden identification card and handed it over.","The guard’s demeanor transformed instantly. He snapped to attention, saluting sharply.","\"Good morning, Mr. Dexter! You can head inside immediately.\"","Simon and his sister froze in their tracks.","A gold license card. That was the highest tier of identification issued by the Hero Association.","It meant the holder was a Gold-rank registered hero, a status reserved for those whose evaluated potential placed them in the top ten of the entire city.","But Dexter didn’t wait for them to react.","He simply pocketed his card, nodded to the guard, and strode through the gate, heading directly toward the location he had been given for his sparring session.","\"Why would I bother getting close to you? Don’t tell me you’re the Storm Empress.\"","Dexter’s lips curled into a mocking smile when his enhanced hearing overheard Simon and his sisters conversation.","Lyra opened one eye, looked at him, and simply nodded before closing it again. A moment later, her soft, melodic voice echoed in his mind.","’Good luck.’","Dexter smiled warmly and projected his thoughts back. ’ Thank you.’","Mira didn’t react and Selene was in the room.","But Dexter could feel Selene’s echolocation pulses focused on him,","He turned toward the front door, slipped on his shoes, and reached for the handle.","\"Knock. Knock. Knock.\"","Dexter paused, his hand hovering over the knob. He frowned, wondering who it could be.","’ Oh shit. The beds.’","The beds he had bought yesterday and for the girls, the delivery must have arrived.","Dexter opened the front door to find two delivery workers in matching uniforms standing on his porch. One of them held out a clipboard.","\"Are you Dexter Ashford?\"","\"Yes.\"","The worker extended the clipboard and a pen. \"Sign here, please.\"","Dexter scribbled his signature and stepped aside, gesturing them in.","Originally, he had only ordered two beds. But at the last minute before placing the order, he had changed his mind.","Instead of two, he had purchased four, one for each of the girls.","The expense had drained nearly all his money but Dexter was expecting payment from the Hero Association so he wasn’t quite worried.","More importantly, every investment he made in his wives would return a hundredfold through the system.","So it was a win-win situation.","Dexter guided the workers through the hallway.","First, he directed them to the girls’ bedroom.","\"You remove the original beds and the three new ones here side by side.\"","Then he led them to his own small room for the fourth.","The workers nodded and got to work, carrying the heavy mattress frames and bed components through the narrow hallway.","Mira, who had been cultivating silently by the living room window, furrowed her brows.","Across the room, both Lyra and Selene wore similarly troubled expressions, their brows knit in irritation.","Dexter saw this and immediately knew the noise might have been disturbing for them.","Dexter scratched the back of his head, feeling a pang of guilt for disrupting their cultivation.","He walked over to the girls and spoke in an apologetic tone.","\"I’m sorry about the noise. I just wanted to make your sleeping arrangements more comfortable. You girls have been sharing two merged beds, and I know that can’t be good for your backs. With these new beds, everything should be properly set up, and you’ll be able to rest comfortably.\"","Mira’s eyes snapped open. \"We never complained.\"","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"You never needed to. I just can’t bear you three being uncomfortable when it’s within my power to change it.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the room immediately went still.","[Mira + 3 Affection]","[Lyra + 7 Affection]","[Selene + 10 Affection]","Mira’s lips twitched and her crimson eyes flickered with warmth.","She immediately closed her eyes, lowered her head, and snorted softly, pretending to concentrate on her cultivation.","But the faint pink tinge creeping up her neck betrayed her.","Lyra’s eyes had snapped open as well.","The families that had married them off had treated them as burdens. The world had treated them as broken relics.","But Dexter... Dexter kept on trying his utmost to make them comfortable.","No matter his intentions, he was obviously doing this from his heart.","’Thank you,’Lyra’s soft voice echoed in Dexter’s mind.","Dexter smiled. ’You’re welcome.’","Selene hadn’t moved. Her pale eyes remained closed, and her face expressionless.","But inside, the cracks around her frosted heart continued to increase.","Dexter smiled faintly.","\"They just need about thirty to forty minutes to finish setting everything up. I’m sorry for the inconvenience and the noise.\"","The girls nodded.","Before returning to supervise the workers,","Dexter glanced at Mira’s neck. The Type-5 Protective Amulet rested against her collarbone making him sigh in relief.","He had temporarily lowered the Type-5 House Protection Barrier so the delivery workers could enter the property. That meant, for the next forty minutes, the house was theoretically vulnerable.","But the Protective Amulet on Mira’s neck was more than capable of shielding all three girls if someone managed to slip past the lowered barrier.","And Dexter himself remained on high alert.","If anyone so much as twitched in the wrong direction, he would know.","***","35 minutes later, the workers were done.","Three fluffy, queen-sized beds now occupied the girls’ bedroom, each fitted with fresh sheets, thick comforters, and soft pillows.","The fourth bed, a similarly plush mattress sat in Dexter’s small room.","Dexter touched and admired his new bed. The mattress was incredibly soft, with cloud-like surface that seemed to swallow you whole the moment you lay down.","\"So nice!\"","He couldn’t help but smile.","Then he quickly cleared his throat and straightened his posture.","’A man shouldn’t behave like a woman, giggling over a fluffy bed.’","Hw quickly stood up and chided himself. He should have bought a harder, firmer mattress for himself. Something masculine.","But the bed was just so... fluffy.","After the workers left, he walked back to the living room.","\"You can go in and check the beds now,\" he told the girls. \"If you want to rest or close your eyes for a bit, the room is ready.\"","All three nodded.","But none of them moved.","They remained exactly where they were.","Dexter shrugged. Patience was part of the process.","After settling the remaining logistics around the house, he turned to the girls.","\"I’m heading to the city for the spar,\" he announced.","’Good luck,’Lyra’s voice echoed in his mind immediately.","\"Good luck,\" Selene murmured softly.","Dexter smiled. \"Thank you.\"","Mira, as usual, said nothing.","Dexter opened the front door, stepped out, and pulled it shut behind him.","\"I’ll be back soon,\" he called through the closed door.","***","Inside the silent living room, Mira frowned at the closed door as Dexter’s footsteps faded down the street.","Lyra caught sight of Mira’s worried expression and smiled.","’If you’re worried about him, why didn’t you tell him not to go?’ Her voice echoed gently in Mira’s mind.","Mira’s head snapped toward Lyra, her crimson eyes narrowing.","But her face quickly hardened into her usual mask of cold indifference.","\"He’s a man,\" Mira said flatly, \"Of course he’ll do whatever he wants regardless of what anyone says.\"","’He’s also your husband,’ Lyra’s voice teased, the mental tone laced with a playful, almost mischievous edge. ’He would listen to you if you told him to stay.’"]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108 | Don’t Hold Back","paragraphs":["Dexter arrived before a massive twenty-story building.","While it wasn’t the tallest structure he had ever seen, it was incredibly wide, stretching across the landscape.","[A/N: I was about to say \"Stretching across the landscape like Bonnie Blues legs but it might not be appropriate lol]","There were dozens of entrances, sliding glass doors as people went in and came out of it.","He stopped at the main entrance and looked around. The violet haired girl had told him she would meet him here.","He scanned the crowds of heroes coming and going, but didn’t see her.","Then, he heard his name.","\"Dexter.\"","The voice was soft like a whisper, yet it reached his ears with perfect clarity. He turned around.","Lexa was standing two hundred meters away across the busy place.","Before Dexter could even raise an eyebrow, she took a single step forward.","In the blink of an eye, the two-hundred-meter distance vanished. She blurred through the crowd without disturbing a single person, reappearing just five meters away from him.","She then slowed her pace, walking the remaining distance at a casual, unhurried stroll.","\"Let’s go in,\" she said simply, stepping past him.","Dexter blinked. He had almost forgotten he was dealing with an Ultra-rank expert.","To someone at that level, crossing two hundred meters was no different from taking a single step. They could appear anywhere their eyes could see in an instant.","As she walked past him, Dexter noticed something else. She wasn’t wearing her dark cloak today.","Instead, she was dressed in a fashionable crop top and fitted jeans, her violet hair pulled back into a neat, stylish ponytail.","She looked like she was heading out for a casual afternoon of shopping or attending a fashion show, not preparing for a soaring session at all.","Dexter stared at her back for a second, then blinked.","It was painfully obvious she didn’t take their upcoming spar seriously.","The violet-eyed girl smiled faintly as they entered the building together.","Inside, the main hall was enormous. There were tens of receptionists stationed behind a massive, curved counter, efficiently handling a constant stream of heroes booking training facilities.","Lexa walked up to a receptionist whose station had just opened up.","\"We want to book a sparring arena,\" she said.","The receptionist, a polite young woman, smiled and nodded. \"Yes, we have several available. Which tier would you like to book? We have Ordinary, Standard, Deluxe, Premium, or the Presidential suite.\"","\"Deluxe will be okay,\" Lexa responded casually.","The clerk nodded and typed on her terminal. \"Alright, that will be $5,000 per hour. Please scan your card to pay here.\"","Lexa pulled out her phone and scanned the QR code on the counter. The payment of $5,000 went through in an instant.","The clerk produced a sleek, black access pass and handed it over. \"Here is the pass to Arena 512. You can find it in the Deluxe section down the east corridor. Good luck.\"","Lexa took the pass and started walking. Dexter followed closely behind.","They moved past the Ordinary and Standard sections. The building’s interior was designed like a massive indoor sports complex.","Through reinforced glass walls, Dexter could see various open arenas, much like indoor boxing rings where heroes were already sparring with each other.","The sounds of clashing weapons, explosive impacts, and cheering spectators echoed through the vast halls.","They continued walking until they crossed the threshold into the Deluxe section, where the atmosphere grew noticeably quieter.","They reached the door marked Arena 512.","She tapped the key card against the scanner, and the heavy steel doors slid open with a soft hiss revealing the room to them.","’Damn!’","Dexter was stunned as he entered the room.","The room beyond was enormous. The entire chamber was an arena in itself, built for serious combat.","The walls were forged from graded reinforced pure steel, designed to absorb and dissipate the shockwaves of high-level battles so that combatants could go all out without damaging the surroundings or alerting the outside world.","Along one wall, a row of advanced measuring equipment was mounted.","It could record and track impact force, reaction speed, mana output, and a dozen other combat metrics.","Adjacent to those, a collection of gymming and running equipment lined the far corner.","Dexter’s eyes lingered on a set of dumbbells resting on a reinforced rack.","The smallest one was labeled 5,000 kg. The next was 10,000 kg. The largest read 200,000 kg.","He wasn’t particularly surprised. Superhuman-level heroes reached these levels of physical strength as a baseline.","Dexter himself wasn’t certain of his exact lifting limit, but he knew with certainty that it exceeded 15,000 kilograms by a comfortable margin.","Beyond the combat area was a private bathroom occupied one side, complete with a shower and changing area.","In the opposite corner, a relaxation zone with leather sofa, wall-mounted television, a mini fridge, and a fully stocked minibar.","\"This is actually nice,\" he murmured, rolling his shoulders.","This was a place where he could go all out.","Every technique, every ability, every ounce of his strength could be unleashed here without restraint.","He could polish his combat skills, refine his patterns, and push himself to his absolute limits without holding back.","No wonder heroes flocked to these facilities.","As Dexter was still taking in the room, the violet-eyed girl dropped her bag near the wall and walked to the center of the arena, then turned to face him.","She tilted her head slightly, her ponytail swaying with the motion as she asked.","\"Are you ready?\"","Dexter turned toward her.","He glanced at her crop top, her jeans and the nice boots she was wearing.","\"Aren’t you going to change or something?\"","The girl smirked. \"There’s no need for that, It will be over in less than 3 moves.\"","Dexter stared at her.","’ Actually calling me weak?’","He shook his head slowly, then walked to the center of the arena to face her.","The girl closed her eyes as the mana radiating from her body began to shift and compress.","Layer by layer, her energy diminished, compressing inward like a collapsing star until it stabilized at a far more manageable level.","Superhuman Realm, Third Stage.","She opened her violet eyes. \"Done. Are you ready?\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109 | Draconic Might!","paragraphs":["She opened her violet eyes. \"Done. Are you ready?\"","Dexter blinked in surprise.","She was actually able to precisely control her energy, suppressing her cultivation from Ultra-rank all the way down to a third level of the Superhuman Realm.","Dexter nodded. \"All right. I’m ready.\"","The girl’s expression turned serious as she said with indifference.","\"I would advise you to take this seriously, because I will. This will determine whether you have the strength to keep the key.\"","Dexter frowned. \"I thought we talked about this. I’m not giving you the key.\"","The girl smiled coldy.","\"When did the weak have the rights to give orders?\"","A chuckle rang out from her mouth. \"If you were the same strength as I am, I would have left it with you willingly. But you’re simply too weak for your opinion to matter.\"","She paused, letting the words sink in.","\"Taking the key from you is as easy as snatching lollipop from a baby. Instead, I decided to amuse my self with this duel. Let’s see whether you have the strength to keep it.\"","Dexter’s expression hardened.","He had been treating this spar as a friendly exchange, a chance to test his abilities against a stronger opponent.","But she was actually threatening to snatch the key by force if he couldn’t stop her.","His gaze turned cold.","\"Since you’ve reduced your strength,\" he said, his voice turned flat and dangerous, \"I hope you don’t hold back. Because I won’t either.\"","The girl’s lips curled upward. \"Good.\"","\"Can I know the name of the person I’m going to defeat?\" Dexter asked.","The girl’s smile widened.","\"My name is Violette.\"","The instant the last syllable left her lips, she blurred.","\"BOOM!\"","The air around the place she had been staying previously suddenly exploded by the sheer amount of speed.","One moment she was standing twenty meters away. The next, she was directly in front of Dexter as her fist shrieked through the air, punching directly at Dexter’s chest with all the strength of a level 3 Superhuman expert!","Her fist moved with the speed of a bullet train as it slammed into him Like a sledge hammer.","\"BOOM!\"","A massive explosion erupted from the point of impact as shockwaves blasted outward in every direction, the force of her movement catching up with her in a devastating secondary detonation.","The steel walls trembled slightly as the shockwave from the punch slammed into it.","However, despite all of these impressive feat, Dexter didn’t move a single muscle.","He stood exactly where he had been, hands in his pockets as Violett’s fist collided against with chest.","His body had absorbed the full force of the blow and transferred it straight down through his legs into the ground beneath him.","Violette’s eyes widened in shock as she stared at Dexter.","It felt as though she had punched a punched a mountain instead of a human being!","The impact had traveled back up her own arm, vibrating through her bones, making her uncomfortable.","Dexter indifferently looked down at the fist still pressed against his chest, then he raised his gaze to Violette’s face.","\"Is that it?\" he asked indifferently.","Violette’s face changed drastically. She flashed backward in an instant, putting five meters of distance between them in a snap.","Violett’s expression turned extremely serious as she started at Dexter as though she was seeing him for the first time.","Her brow furrowed deeply.","*What the hell was that?*","What kind of Third Stage Superhuman had a body this dense?","She couldn’t believe Dexter’s body was that ridiculous.","Dexter smirked.","The Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture, Demon Tempering Body and the Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline had forged his physique into something terrifying.","Dexter tilted his head, a faint, dismissive sound escaping his lips. \"Do you want to try again?\"","Violette’s eyes turned cold.","\"You truly wish to die.\"","Her pride wouldn’t allow her to accept what had just happened.","\"Bang!\"","She vanished again, reappearing behind Dexter in a blur that would have been invisible to anyone without enhanced senses.","Her waist twisted as she unleashed a vicious kick directly at the back of his neck.","\"Bang!\"","The kick connected. Dexter’s neck tilted an inch but he remained standing and unmoved like a mountain!","Even at this point, he still hadn’t taken his hands out of his pockets!","It was truly insane!","Dexter slowly turned his head, the motion itself pushing Violette’s foot back, forcing her to retract the kick","He looked at her over his shoulder, his expression completely unbothered.","\"I didn’t think Ultra-rank expert would be this weak.\"","\"You—!\"","Her face twisted anger and her violet eyes blazed with fury as she retreated backward, her fists clenching at her sides.","She had bragged two seconds ago she would defeat him in three moves.","Right now, she had struck twice and yet her opponent had barely moved!","As an ultra rank expert, her body should naturally be stronger than a Superhuman rank brat. Even if she surpressed her strength, there’s no way to surpress durability.","But yet, her body was actually weaker than a Third Stage Superhuman.","Someone she had told that he was too weak.","The humiliation burned through her veins like magma.","\"Draconic Body!\"","She growled as she activated her talent.","\"ROOOOOOOOAAAR!\"","Instantly, a phantom image of a golden dragon erupted from her body as it roared like a true ancient beast.","\"Down!\"","Violette stomped her feet as she burst forward with speed. The golden dragon behind her surged ahead of her, its massive maw opening wide as it descended upon Dexter along with Violett’s fist.","Dexter raised an eyebrow. The pressure emanating from the dragon was intense.","He couldn’t tell if it was a bloodline technique or an innate talent, because the energy waves it radiated blended seamlessly with Violette’s own mana signature.","But even after seeing this, he simply let out an indifferent snort.","\"Reckless struggle.\"","He only took out one of his hands out of his pockets and punched out with the second fist.","\"KA-BOOM!\"","The explosion was deafening as a massive shockwave erupted like a thunderclap detonating inside a sealed chamber.","The steel walls groaned as they absorbed the brunt of the force as the wind trembled viciously.","Violette’s eyes widened when she saw she didn’t even manage to push Dexter an inch backward!","\"Die!\"","She roared in fury and punched again.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter matched it.","She immediately released a barrage of punches.","\"Bang!\" \"Bang!\" \"Bang!\"","Their fists became blurs.","Each collision sent another thunderous shockwave rippling through the arena.","The steel walls rang with each impact as the ground beneath their feet groaned and trembled.","Every punch Violette threw was equally matched by Dexter.","She struck faster even faster, her fist looking like a machine gun shooting out rapid bullets of fists.","But Dexter was no different, he matched her punches and also matched her speed!","His expression didn’t change a single bit and he didn’t move a single inch.","What does it meant to be invincible in the same realm!?","Violette suddenly flipped backwards as ash roared.","\"Divine Dragon Might!\"","Violette’s left eyes shone as it transformed into a pure golden eye of a dragon.","Her fingernails elongated into curved claws as her canine teeth extended into fangs.","She had activated her bloodline.","Her energy surged, her strength exploded upward, and the golden dragon coiling around her body doubled in size.","\"ROOOOOOAR!\""]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110 | Take Me Out For Lunch","paragraphs":["\"Divine Dragon Might!\"","Violette’s left eyes shone as it transformed into a pure golden eye of a dragon.","Her fingernails elongated into curved claws as her canine teeth extended into fangs.","She had activated her bloodline.","Her energy surged, her strength exploded upward, and the golden dragon coiling around her body doubled in size.","\"ROOOOOOAR!\"","Violette flashed suddenly vanished, reappearing behind Dexter and launched a devastating downward kick.","Dexter sidestepped effortlessly. The kick slammed into the ground.","\"BOOM!\"","The floor trembled violently but didn’t explode down the steel been made of special material.","Violette spun and released another kick, this time a horizontal sweep aimed at Dexter’s midsection.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter raised his arm and received the kick on his forearm.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter was actually forced to take a step backward. But it was actually just a single step!","But Dexter simply smiled.","\"It’s quite impressive you manage to push me backward,\" he said calmly, \"But in the same realm, I am invincible.\"","The instant the words left his mouth, his body flashed as he picked out with intense speed.","\"Boom!\"","The wind shrieked as his fist tore through the air as he punched directly at Violette’s chest.","In that instant, Violett’s face changed drastically and she quickly brought up her hand in x shape manner to block.","The phantom image of a dragon around her suddenly wrapped its wings around Violette to protect her.","\"BOOM!\" \"CRACK—\"","The golden barrier made of wings immediately shattered like it was made of glass as it slammed directly against Violett’s crossed arms.","\"KA-BOOM!\"","Her arms was forcefully pressed against her chest as her shirt exploded from the force revealing sport bra holding two massive breasts.","\"Whoosh!\"","Like a leaf in an hurricane, she was blasted backwards with an extreme force.","She slammed into the far steel wall with a deafening ’bang’ as she bounced back and landed on the ground.","Dexter slowly pulled his fist back, a small smile on his face. He looked across the arena at her crumpled form.","\"Are you convinced?\"","Violette looked up at him, panting heavily.","Her golden dragon eye still blazed. Her claws were still extended. Her chest rose up and down rapidly, and a thin line of blood traced from the corner of her lip.","Fury!","A deep surge of anger ripped through her like a hurricane.","Suddenly, a pressure wave of pressure spread out of her like head.","Her suppressed energy shattered its restraints, climbing from Third Stage Superhuman to Fourth... Fifth... Sixth... Ninth... Twelfth...","The barrier between realms cracked.","\"Ultra Realm.\"","The moment her energy touched the Ultra Realm threshold, Dexter’s face changed.","’ She’s really angry over a spar and willing to go all out?’","Dexter’s gaze hardened. He began channeling mana into his bloodline, preparing to activate Scorching Fury—","Then, just as suddenly as it had erupted, the pressure stopped.","Violette closed her eyes and ghe golden dragon pupil in her left eye retreated, the color fading back to violet. Her claws retracted, shrinking back into normal fingernails. Her fangs withdrew. The golden dragon coiling around her body dissolved into sparkling motes of light that scattered and faded.","She stood there, expressionless, staring at Dexter for a long, silent moment.","Then, without a single word, she turned, walked to the side of the arena, picked up her bag, and headed toward the restroom.","Dexter blinked.","He stared at the closed restroom door, stunned.","Then he shook his head and let out a quiet laugh.","\"Like granddaughter, like grandfather,\" he muttered to himself.","It was exactly the same thing her grandfather had done.","When Dexter had won their bet, learning the Grand Cosmos Scripture in a single day, the old man had simply walked away without saying a word.","Now the granddaughter was doing the exact same thing. Beaten in a spar, her pride stinging, she had retreated to the washroom without uttering a single word.","Dexter shrugged. He would let her compose herself. Pride was a fragile thing, and he had just shattered hers rather thoroughly.","He looked down.","His right boot had exploded during the fight, most likely from the accumulated shockwaves of their fist exchanges.","The leather had torn apart, the sole had separated, and his sock was poking through a hole at the front of the boot.","Dexter face-palmed with his free hand.","\"Seriously?\"","He shook his head, kicked off the remnants of the destroyed boot, and limped slightly as he walked to the sideline to wait for Violette.","Luckily, a pair of disposable sandals sat neatly arranged on a shelf near the relaxation zone—courtesy of the training center, presumably for combatants whose footwear hadn’t survived their sparring sessions.","Dexter slipped them on. They were slightly tighter than his size, the thin rubber pressing uncomfortably against his toes, but they were infinitely better than walking barefoot through the city.","He limped back to the arena and waited.","Five minutes passed, ten. No sign of Violette.","’What’s she doing in there?’","Dexter frowned and crossed his arms, staring at the closed restroom door with impatience. He had won the spar and he wanted the money she owned him.","He had no intention of standing around all afternoon waiting for a sore loser to finish sulking in the bathroom.","He frowned and was prepared to go knock.","The restroom door clicked open.","Violette stepped out.","She had changed into a fresh outfit, a simple white blouse and dark slacks, her violet hair now loose and falling past her shoulders.","Her expression was carefully composed, the mask of cold indifference firmly back in place.","She looked at Dexter. She seemed to want to speak, but hesitated, her tongue darting out to wet her lips. Then, finally, she spoke.","\"How about lunch?\"","Dexter shook his head immediately. \"No. I just want to get home.\"","Violette hissed softly through her teeth. \"If you want your money, I’d suggest you come with me.\"","Dexter frowned, his eyes narrowing. \"You’re holding the bet hostage over dinner?\"","Violette shrugged, a hint of smugness returning. \"You won already. The money is yours. The least you could do is fulfill one of my wishes before I hand it over.\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111 | Country Bumpkin","paragraphs":["Violette shrugged, a hint of her earlier smugness returning. \"You won already. The money is yours. The least you could do is fulfill one of my wishes before I hand it over.\"","Dexter stared at her for a long while as he frowned. He thought for a bit then eventually agreed. It wouldn’t hurt to just take her to lunch and leave after.","\"Alright. What restaurant?\"","\"I know a place close to here,\" Violette said, already walking toward the exit. \"Let’s go.\"","Dexter followed her out of the Titan Training Facility entirely.","The afternoon air was warm against his skin as it reached its highest intensity.","Violette confidently led the way. Her earlier fury seemingly dissolved, or at least deeply slightly reduced.","\"There’s an Arcane restaurant nearby,\" she said over her shoulder. \"Best one in the district.\"","***","The restaurant was called House Of Daily Gourmets.","The building was incredible. They mixed traditional along with modern architecture, making it look really nice.","The entrance was framed by two enormous stone lions, their eyes set with tiny mana gems that flickered with ambient light.","Despite the restaurant’s size, it was packed.","The main dining hall was filled to the brim with heroes, businessmen, wealthy civilians, and what appeared to be several minor nobles.","Waiters moved between tables with practiced grace, carrying steaming dishes that filled the air with a complex, mouthwatering aroma.","Yet despite the crowd, the restaurant was so spacious that there were still plenty of empty tables available.","Violette walked in as if she owned the place. She selected a table near the window and Dexter sat down opposite her.","A waiter appeared almost instantly. He was a young man in a black uniform with a cloth napkin draped over his forearm.","\"Good evening. Welcome to House Of Daily Gourmets. Are you ready to order, or would you like a moment to review the menu?\"","Violette didn’t even glance at the menu. \"I’ll have the Grade Two Stamina Recovery Set. Dragon-Tail Steak with Moon-Herb Sauce.\"","The waiter nodded and turned to Dexter, presenting a leather-bound menu with a subtle bow.","Dexter opened it.","His eyes nearly popped out of his skull.","The menu was organized by grade.","Grade One meals occupied the first page, with prices ranging from 3,000 to 8,000 dollars per plate.","Grade Two meals started on the second page, with prices between 12,000 and 50,000 dollars. Grade Three meals which was the highest the restaurant offered actually began at 80,000 dollars and climbed to a staggering 150,000.","Dexter stared at the numbers.","A Grade Two meal, similar in quality to the simple rice dishes he casually cooked for his wives every morning, cost 12,000 dollars per plate here. And that was the cheap end. The higher-end Grade Two dishes ran up to 50,000.","’ What the hell!’","The simple meals he cooked at home were Grade One at minimum, even with ordinary ingredients.","With Diamond Rice and Heavenly Treasures, he was producing Grade Four meals that didn’t even exist on this restaurant’s menu.","If a Grade Two meal here cost 50,000 dollars per plate, what would a Grade Four meal be worth?","’ What would a Grade Five meal be worth?’","The numbers went through his mind like he was a number calculator.","One could even see dollars sigh in his eyes!","If he opened a restaurant, serving even Grade Two or Grade Three meals to the public, he could generate astronomical income. Tens of thousands of dollars per plate. Hundreds of thousands per day. Millions per month.","And that was just the beginning. As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, his capabilities far exceeded anything this restaurant could produce.","He was in a class of his own. There were only three Grandmaster Foodsmiths registered in the entire city, and none of them could reliably produce Grade Four meals. He could do it with his eyes closed.","A restaurant, his own establishment. A place where his Foodsmith skills could generate consistent, massive revenue, revenue that could be reinvested into his wives to gain 10,000 times returns!","The more he thought about it, the more excited he became. His eyes practically glowing with fire.","Across the table, Violette noticed the brightness in Dexter’s eyes.","Her lips curled upward in a small smile.","She mistook his excitement for the naive wonder of a young man experiencing fine Arcane Meal for the first time.","In her mind, she was looking at a country bumpkin who had never set foot in a restaurant this expensive.","The resentment she felt from losing to him eased slightly.","’ So he’s strong,’ she thought to herself, taking a sip of water.","’ Strong but poor. Interesting combination.’","\"You’ve never been to an Arcane restaurant before, have you?\" she asked, a trace of condescension in her voice.","Dexter pondered and realized he truly hadn’t seen an arcane restaurant before. He shook his head. \"No.\"","Violette’s internal diagnosis of \"country bumpkin\" was confirmed. She smiled warmly—the first genuinely warm expression she had shown him all day.","\"You should try their food. It’s really quite good.\"","Dexter nodded absently, still mentally calculating potential restaurant revenue streams.","He selected a Grade One meal from the menu.","*Grade One Iron-boar Steak: Premium monster beef steak served with mana-infused wild rice and fire-roasted vegetables. Restores physical stamina, slightly strengthens muscle fibers, and accelerates recovery from physical exertion. Ideal for post-training consumption.*","Price: 5,000 dollars.","Dexter ordered because he wanted to taste it.","He wanted to compare a professional restaurant’s Grade One meal against his own cooking to see where he stood. To understand the gap between his Foodsmith skills and the commercial market.","The waiter collected the menus and disappeared into the kitchen.","Dexter leaned back in his chair, his eyes drifting across the restaurant.","The atmosphere was refined but not stuffy. Soft instrumental music played from hidden speakers.","The clinking of fine china and the murmur of polite conversation created a comfortable, ambient noise.","Violette sat across from him, her posture elegant, her violet eyes watching him with quiet, assessing interest.","\"You handled yourself well in the arena,\" she said after a moment, her tone carefully neutral.","Dexter looked at her. \"You don’t sound happy about it.\"","\"I’m not,\" she admitted without hesitation. \"I reduced my strength to Third Stage Superhuman and still lost. That shouldn’t have been possible.\"","\"You told me not to hold back, I didn’t.\"","Violette’s jaw tightened slightly. \"Your body... it’s not normal. No Third Stage Superhuman should be that durable. What cultivation technique are you practicing?\"","Dexter smiled enigmatically. \"A man should have his secrets.\"","Violette studied him for a long moment, then let out a soft, reluctant huff. \"Fine. Keep your secrets.\"","The waiter returned, carrying two large, covered plates balanced expertly on one arm.","He placed the first plate in front of Violette—her Grade Two Dragon-Tail Steak, the meat glistening with a shimmering moon-herb sauce that radiated faint, silvery mana. The aroma was rich and complex, carrying hints of wild game and aromatic herbs.","Then he placed Dexter’s plate in front of him. The Grade One Iron-boat Steak Set.","The steak was thick and perfectly seared, resting on a bed of mana-infused wild rice alongside fire-roasted vegetables.","The meat had a faint, reddish glow the telltale sign of monster beast beef, which contained trace amounts of ambient mana.","The presentation was clean and professional.","Dexter blinked his eyes. ’Looks nice but I want to eat, not soak my eyes in designs.’","Dexter muttered as he saw the design on his food and the small portions given to him."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112 | Mysterious Faction","paragraphs":["In just ten seconds, Dexter had completely deconstructed the meal.","With the refined palate of a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he analyzed everything about the dish.","The precise blend of herbs in the seasoning, and the method of mana infusion. He could taste every ingredient, trace every step of the cooking process, and identify every single flaw.","In just a few seconds, he recognized so many flaws.","The mana infusion method wasn’t done right.","The seasoning was slightly too heavy on one side, masking the natural umami of the meat.","The fire-roasted vegetables were slightly over-charred, introducing a bitter taste that clashed with the steak’s savory nature.","For an ordinary person, the meal was decent and even enjoyable. But for someone like Dexter, it was far from perfect.","’ Disappointing .’","Although he was extremely disappointed by the food he was never one to waste food.","His Chaos Flame Demon bloodline and his metabolism, burned through the calories and mana with quickly. He finished the entire plate in under two minutes.","Violette stared at him, stunned by his speed of eating.","She had barely finished a quarter of her own steak and this guy had eaten all of it.","Her lips tugged slightly. ’ Truly a country bumpkin.’","Dexter set down his fork and leaned back. \"So,\" he said, meeting her violet eyes. \"Are you going to tell me anything about the necklace?\"","Violette’s expression flickered as she pondered.","Then, instead of answering his question, she asked one of her own.","\"What do you know about the powers controlling this place?\"","Dexter frowned. \"The powers controlling this place?\"","\"Do you mean the Nine main families of Stargate City?\"","Violets sneered with disdain and arrogance in her tone. \"What Nine main families? They are merely frogs playing house in a well. I’m talking about the three main associations?\"","’ Did she just compare the seven main families as frogs in the well ?’ Dexter’s pupils constricted violently and he knew Violette status might be even more astonishing than he thought.","Dexter considered her question for a moment. \"There’s the Hero Association, the Geneticists Association that manufactures genetic serums, and the Federation.\"","Violette raised an eyebrow. \"Any other powers?\"","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"I know there are likely other powers operating behind the scenes, but I’ve never heard of them.\"","Violette nodded again. \"There’s a reason you’ve never heard of them. The Hero Association is the strongest, having the support of the federation, and they make sure the news about other associations is suppressed.\"","Dexter’s frown deepened. \"So what does that have to do with the necklace?\"","Violette grinned darkly.","\"The necklace is a sort of key,\" she said quietly.","\"The key is only given to the successor of one of those hidden factions you’re taking about. If you wear the necklace, you automatically become the next generation leader of a hidden faction.\"","Dexter’s face changed.","’Leader?’","Becoming the next-generation leader of a hidden faction? How was that possible?","Had that old man actually given him the key to leading a mysterious organization just because he had won a bet about learning a cultivation technique?","Not to mention that it was a mysterious faction, if he was caught, the Hero Association would definitely not let him off.","Violette smirked, watching the realization dawn on his face. \"So now, do you know how much trouble you’re in?\"","\"If word gets out, not only would you be hunted by opposite factions, but by the Hero Association also.\"","She suddenly leaned forward slightly. \"Why don’t you give me the necklace? And just like that—\"","\"Snap!\"","\"Your trouble disappears. Simple.\"","Dexter blinked and for a brief moment, he truly considered giving her the necklace right there.","Afterall he still had to take care of three wives. And now, he somehow became the next generation leader of some mysterious organization?","He could bare take care of his girls and himself. If his identity was revealed, he would place the girls in danger. They were his investments afterall.","But then, another thought came to his head.","What if she was lying?","He had only ever heard of the Hero Association, the Geneticists Association, and the government.","Those were the acknowledged powers of the continent. The idea that there were other, hidden factions was plausible, but the notion that he would casually meet an old man, win a bet, and receive a token of leadership for one of these secret organizations?","It was simply too absurd.","And if there was one thing Dexter had learned from living with Mira, it was how to recognize when someone was trying to be manipulative.","His gaze focused as he sneered at Violette. \"I know your tricks. And I won’t fall for them.\"","Violette stared at him, genuinely stunned.","Then, slowly, she smirked. She didn’t try to correct him not did she argue. She simply let his dismissal stand as a knowing amusement danced in her violet eyes.","\"Alright. I won’t say much regarding this matter any longer.\"","\"What academy are you attending?\" she asked suddenly, shifting topics entirely. \"What university?\"","Dexter frowned. \"University? Why would I need to go to a university?\"","Violette’s brow creased. \"Are you not planning anything for your future?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"I’m not planning to attend any university.\"","Violette appeared even more stunned than before. She opened her mouth, then closed it.","Her frown deepened into something approaching genuine concern.","\"If you’re not planning to attend an Ultra University,\" she said slowly, \"then the key would be useless to you anyway. You should really hand it over to me.\"","Dexter’s ears pricked up. \"Ultra University? What’s that?\"","Violette hesitated as she studied his face, searching for any sign that he was joking.","When she found none, her expression shifted changed into something between disbelief and pity.","She opened her mouth to speak, but then closed it. A faint, cryptic smile replaced her frown.","\"The key would eventually...\" She paused, shaking her head. \"I have no idea why Grandfather gave you the key instead of giving me. But I’m pretty sure you will regret his choice very soon.\"","Her face lightened up as she smiled making her face look even prettier. She had a smile that could actually dim the surroding noise as she smiled at him.","But Dexter’s brows were scrunched up into a frown instead.","Violette let out a quite giggle and offhandedly raised her hand and called the waiter."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113 | Mister Wayne, Young Leader Michael","paragraphs":["Dexter remained frowning as Violette called the waiter and started the process of payment.","’ Ultra University.’","He had never heard of such a thing. He had heard of Hero University, of course.","He had finished secondary school but never attended one. Hero Universities were for the wealthy.","Dexter didn’t need a certificate as his path became clear when he got the system.","Become a licensed hunter, raid dungeons, use the Slaughter Extraction System to grow stronger with every kill, earn money, and spoil his wives, making them grow even stronger.","As for the Hero university, it was unnecessary for that route.","But an Ultra University? That classification of academy was entirely new to him.","He was intensely curious, but Violette didn’t seem to want to explain as she paid the waiter, stood up, and wanted to leave.","Before she could take a single step, a voice suddenly spoke out from behind her.","\"Violette?\"","The voice was masculine, wounded, confident, and was quite gruff.","A young man stepped out from between the tables.","The young man was tall and had a chiseled jaw that looked as though it had been carved from marble.","His tailored suit perfectly complemented his broad shoulders and fit body.","Every detail of his appearance was neat, from the crisp knot of his tie to the mirror-like shine of his shoes.","He looked like a model who’d just walked out of a magazine.","A charming smile spread across his face as he approached.","\"Violette,\" he repeated, his smile widening. \"I thought I recognized you from across the room. I figured my eyes were playing tricks on me, but... it’s actually you.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and observed the exchange.","The moment the man appeared, Violette’s face turned indifferent.","\"Wayne,\" she said flatly. \"I’m leaving.\"","She moved to walk past him, but Wayne shifted effortlessly into her path. It didn’t look aggressive but natural instead.","\"No, no,\" he said, his smile never wavering. \"You can’t leave just like that. I’ve been trying to get in touch with you for the past month. Please... don’t leave on my account.\"","Violette’s gaze turned cold as she stared at the young man.","The young man’s attention drifted to Dexter.","A subtle frown came across his face as his eyes landed on Dexter.","Dexter was dressed plainly and ordinary, like those construction workers. His eyes drifted to his feet, and the arrogance in Wayne’s face increased.","Dexter looked ordinary. Perhaps a little handsome, but nothing that explained why someone of Violette’s standing would be dining with him in a restaurant like this.","The frown disappeared like it had never appeared in the first place as he revealed a fake smile and stretched his hand out.","\"I’m Wayne,\" he said pleasantly. \"And who are you?\"","Dexter glanced at the offered hand before shifting his gaze to Violette.","She hadn’t said a word, but he caught the faint flicker in her violet eyes.","Dexter looked back at Wayne’s outstretched hand, stood up, and replied curtly.","\"Hey, I’m leaving.\"","He gave Violette a brief nod then without a second thought, walked past Wayne without another word.","Dexter didn’t want to get tangled into whatever was happening between the two. They might be exes and might have had a relationship with each other; everything would simply be messy if he gets involved. So he decided to walk away instead.","His sandals made muffled flip-flop sounds as he exited the restaurant, and moments later, he was gone.","Wayne remained motionless, his hand still suspended awkwardly in the air.","For the briefest instant, his smile cracked, and his brown eyes turned pure red.","Wayne was an Ultra-Rank Hero.","Every superhuman hero who met him would immediately show respect without being needed to be told.","Power was respect in this world, it was simply the natural order of things.","Yet this ordinary-looking man hadn’t merely failed to show him respect.","He had dismissed him entirely.","A faint killing intent leaked out as his gaze hardened.","Then Wayne inhaled slowly.","His composure returned until his polished smile settled back into place.","Violette, seeing the exchange, chuckled lightly as she reached for her handbag.","\"If there’s nothing else,\" she said coolly, \"I’ll be leaving.\"","She slung the bag over her shoulder and headed for the exit.","This time Wayne didn’t block her.","Instead, he fell into step beside her, matching her pace.","\"You should really get in touch with Young Leader Michael,\" he said casually, but there was a hidden force in his tone.","\"He’s been trying to reach you. Just as I have, he has something he wants to tell you. Something he believes you might actually be willing to hear.\"","Violette suddenly stopped.","Around them, the restaurant carried on as normally and yet, the space between Violette and Wayne had gone deathly cold.","Then she turned.","Her violet eyes met his.","The cold within them could have frozen an ocean.","\"It seems Michael has been lenient towards you. Speak to me that way and you will not just lose your tongue. And as for Young Leader Michael, tell him that if we ever choose to ally with another faction, it certainly won’t be with Blood Crown.\"","She stared at Wayne, whose face had drained a bit of color, then smiled.","Without waiting for a response, she turned and walked away.","Wayne stood where he was, watching her disappear through the restaurant doors.","He was still smiling but his face was slightly pale from fear. However, the fear and the fake smile vanished.","A streak of crimson veins bulged along the side of his neck, up to the edge of his eyes, before it slowly receded as pure killing intent flashed within his eyes.","His gaze instantly became savage and bloodthirsty. It was terrifying.","It lasted only a heartbeat before he managed to compose himself.","Throughout the entire exchange, another young man had stood quietly behind Wayne.","He hadn’t spoken nor had he moved a muscle to draw attention to himself.","Only after Violette disappeared completely did he finally break the silence.","\"Mister Wayne...\"","He hesitated.","\"I don’t understand why Young Leader Michael is so determined to form an alliance with them.\"","Wayne slowly turned.","His gaze settled on the young man with the crushing weight of a collapsing mountain.","The temperature around them seemed to drop as if the killing intent he had suppressed moments earlier still lingered in the air.","The young man’s face instantly lost all color.","Sweat formed across his forehead as he lowered his head, his earlier curiosity evaporating without a trace.","Wayne opened his mouth and spoke in a calm but terrifying tone.","\"You presume to question Young Leader Michael’s decisions?\"","The young man hurriedly shook his head.","\"I... I wouldn’t dare.\"","Wayne’s expression remained impassive.","\"Then learn to keep your mouth shut.\"","His face slowly calmed as he continued.","\"The thoughts of Young Leader Michael are beyond people like us. Simply do your job and nothing more.","\"...Yes, Mister Wayne.\"","The young man’s head faced the ground even more, and his entire body trembled with fear and respect.","Only after the restaurant gradually returned to normal did Wayne glance once more toward the exit Violette had taken.","A faint smile that didn’t reach his eyes slowly curved across his lips.","\"So...\"","he murmured to himself,","\"You’ve really chosen your side.\""]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114 | $1,000,000","paragraphs":["As he exited onto the street, he overheard several patrons talking excitedly about a tournament happening at the Titan Training Center.","He the suddenly remembered about Simon and his strange sister.","’That must be the tournament Simon had mentioned. Maybe he would win?’","To him, Simon was too kind-hearted but he also knew kindheartedness doesn’t mean he isn’t a demon in combat.","He decided against going back to watch. Instead, he hailed a taxi. The green taxi stopped and after giving his home district, the driver with accent nodded his head and then took off... just like his mom.","***","The taxi had been driving for about 2 minutes when Dexter’s phone buzzed.","He pulled it out and glanced at the screen.","[Credit Alert: $200,000 deposited into your account]","He stared at the notification. Violette had actually kept her promise and sent part of the money.","Before he could fully process the number, a second notification appeared.","[Credit Alert: $870,000 deposited into your account.]","Dexter’s eyes widened.","$200,000 plus $870,000.","One million and seventy thousand dollars.","’ I’m a freaking millionaire!’","Dexter’s mind trembled as he felt extremely giddy. He was an actual millionaire in less than a day!","A massive grin split across his face, almost reaching his ears.","It was so wide that even the taxi driver who offhandedly glanced at him through the rear mirror almost had a heart heart!","Fortunately, he had holy water in his car.","’ Should be easy to tie the kid up and exorcise him.’","Dexter didn’t car what the driver thought. This was his first time having so much money. He had never in his life come into contact with such massive digits.","Except when using a calculator.","His mind immediately shifted into overdrive as he pulled up his phone’s browser and started searching.","What should he buy first? How should he spend the money? Buying a few things shouldn’t take all his money right?","He started to look on the internet what he could buy for the girls, big mistake. There was lots and lots of items on the internet.","So he settled on fashion clothing, shoes, boots, newer version wheel chair for Mira, newer phone model for Lyra and newer AI Contact Lens for Selene.","Then a thought struck him. He was in a taxi, why couldn’t he just purchase a vehicle instead of simply using a taxi. Then transporting the girls and items woukd be even easier. bulletproof SUV.","As he thought about this, he couldn’t keep the thought lying down. It’s a million dollar right? Buying a car shouldn’t take much from his money!","After pondering he decided to get a bulletproof SUV.","He was not going to repeat the highway incident where the taxi driver got sniped in the skull.","The driver who was at the front suddenly got goosebumps and he immediately made the cross sign over his chest. ’ This boy might be really possessed!’","Dexter suddenly leaned forward and spoke.","\"Change of plans, take me to Valerium car dealership at Raestrum District.\"","The driver nodded and adjusted his route.","Five minutes later, the taxi pulled up in front of a massive car dealership. The showroom floor stretched across an enormous, brightly lit space, filled with rows of gleaming vehicles of types and luxury.","Dexter stepped out of the taxi and walked inside. The moment he crossed into the building, a salesman in a tailored suit materialized at his side like he had just teleported.","\"Good evening, sir! Welcome to Valerium Motors. How can I assist you today?\"","Dexter smiled like the rich millionaire that he was.","\"I need an SUV,\" he said. \"Preferably bulletproof. Bulletproof glass, reinforced chassis, the works.\"","The salesman’s eyes brightened. \"Of course, sir. We have an excellent selection of armored SUVs. Right this way.\"","He led Dexter through the showroom to a section where several rugged, imposing vehicles were parked.","Each one was black or dark grey, with thick, reinforced doors and windows.","\"This is our latest model,\" the salesman said, gesturing proudly at a sleek, modern SUV.","\"This year’s edition. Reinforced vibranium-alloy frame, mana-infused bulletproof glass rated to withstand Superhuman-level impacts, self-sealing tires, and a built-in mana shield generator. Retail price: $350,000.\"","Dexter’s heart jumped. 350k just for a car? His entire fortune would be gone just by purchasing three!","Dexter pretended to observe the vehicle truly in fact, he was looking for ways to reject this vehicle and maybe can el his whole plan of buying anything at all.","But as he examined the vehicle, he noticed that it was quite beautiful. But was Modern, aggressive and really looked like a manly vehicle.","But It was too flashy.","If he drove this thing through his neighborhood, every pair of eyes on the street would track it and people would know he got into some money.","If he saw the vehicle the next morning, then that simply mean pigs could fly.","Dexter looked at the salesman and shook his head.","\"This,\" he said. \"It’s too flashy. Don’t you have old models, preferably one that is perfect to assist with someone with wheelchair?\"","The salesman’s smile faltered slightly. \"I’m sorry, sir? You want a reinforced car that is perfect for transporting someone in a wheelchair and make things easier?\"","Dexter nodded and added. \"Don’t forget not flashy either. I need something that looks ordinary on the outside but is reinforced underneath.\"","The salesman blinked, he recovered as he smiled professional. \"I understand completely, sir. Follow me.\"","Dexter thought the salesman might tell him they don’t have, giving him a perfect excuse to withdraw from this purchase.","But seeing the confident expression on the young man’s face, Dexter decided to go with him.","The young man led Dexter across the showroom floor, to a quieter section at the back. Here, the vehicles were older body styles, muted colors, and ordinary in every way. Outside, they wouldn’t earn a second glance on any street.","\"This is our Reliability Line,\" the salesman explained. \"Older exterior designs, but we retrofit the internals with the same military-grade reinforcement packages as our newest models. Same protection but less attention.\"","Dexter’s eyes scanned the row and settled on a dark grey SUV. It looked perfectly ordinary!","The kind of vehicle you’d see in a grocery store parking lot and immediately forget.","Dexter when forward to open the door and he was surprised.","The door was easily three times heavier than a standard car door. The windows was also bulletproof and the interior was minimalist and wide too.","\"What’s the spec on this one?\" Dexter asked, sliding into the driver’s seat.","\"Excellent choice, sir,\" the salesman said, brightening. \"This is the Vanguard V4. Reinforced vibranium-steel alloy chassis, hidden beneath standard exterior paneling. Ballistic resistant bulletproof glass rated to withstand Peak Superhuman-level impacts. Self-sealing run-flat tires.\"","\"Built-in mana shield generator with a six-hour sustained output. EMP-resistant electronics. And a 600-horsepower mana-hybrid engine that runs on both standard fuel and Nexus Cores.\"","He walked to the rear of the vehicle and pressed a button on the key fob.","The tailgate rose automatically.","Then, with a soft mechanical hum, the floor folded outward as a compact hydraulic ramp extended smoothly to the ground.","\"The rear cabin has been completely reconfigured,\" the salesman continued. \"The third-row seats have been removed to create a dedicated wheelchair bay. It features an automatic restraint system that locks the chair securely to the floor, during sudden maneuvers.\"","He stepped aside, allowing Dexter to look inside.","The interior was surprisingly spacious.","A wheelchair could roll straight up the ramp without needing to be lifted. Once inside, it would lock into place automatically, leaving enough room for another passenger to sit comfortably beside it.","The roof had been raised slightly to provide extra headroom, and the side doors opened nearly ninety degrees, making transfers effortless if they were ever necessary.","\"Despite the modifications,\" the salesman added with a smile, \"from the outside, it still looks like an ordinary family SUV.\"","It was perfect to transport Mira with the vehicle!","\"So how much is it?\"","The salesman smiled.","\"Including the reinforcement package and accessibility conversion, the total comes to $280,000 sir.\"","Dexter almost went mad right there it was simply too expensive.","However, the mind was willing, but the flesh was unruly.","He ran his hand over the steering wheel. It was really really comfortable.","He looked at the salesman. \"I’ll take it.\"","The salesman’s face lit up like a sunrise. \"Fantastic, sir! If you can provide your Hero license, I’ll start the paperwork immediately.\"","The moment the young man saw the gold card, his face changed and what supposed to take thirty minutes was finished in ten.","Within ten minutes, Dexter had transferred the funds, signed the registration documents, and was handed a pair of keys.","He slid into the driver’s seat, adjusted the mirrors, and twisted the key.","\"Vroooom!\"","The way the engine purred made Dexter feel like it was totally worth it.","He pulled out of the dealership onto the city street."]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115 | Neuro-link Wheelchair","paragraphs":["The Vanguard V4 drove really smoothly and purred when you wanted it to.","The steering was responsive, the suspension smooth, and the cabin was soundproofed too.","Dexter entered onto the highway, his mind already shifting to his next destination.","Mira’s wheelchair and then a boutique with decent clothing and maybe flowery dress for Mira. He loved them on her, owning perfectly well she doesn’t like it. Her puffed up checks when she’s angry always reminds him of a angry chipmunk with red hair.","The standard hospital-issue wheelchair she had been using since their wedding was getting olds so he needed to change them.","Now that Mira had awakened her Spectral Arms, she was already attempting to move herself, but the old wheelchair’s wheels were stiff, requiring extra strength and precision.","He alredy found he was looking for earlier.","It was a tech boutique store (Arctech) next called Hexatech Innovations.","They specializing in arcane technology that mix modern engineering with arcane craftsmanship and he had found a product called the Neural-Linked Wheelchair.","According to the online description, the wheelchair came with a neural choker that, when worn, released a pulse that read the user’s motor intentions.","The wheelchair would move exactly where the user wanted to go, responding to subconscious directional impulses with zero lag.","Dexter set the GPS and drove.","***","Hextech Innovations boutique was a large building located in the city’s mid-district. It was all glass and polished steel, with billboard display showcasing rotating models of various Arctech. (Arcane technology)","Dexter parked the Vanguard V4 in the lot and walked inside.","A young lady who was a receptionist approached him with a professional smile.","\"Welcome to Hexatech Innovations. How can I help you today?\"","\"I’m looking for the Neural-Link Wheelchair,\" Dexter said.","The receptionist’s smile widened. \"Of course. Please follow me.\"","She led him to a dedicated section of the store where a sleek, futuristic wheelchair sat on a raised platform.","A slim, silver choker rested on a velvet display stand beside it.","Dexter examined the chair. It looked really elegant, light weight and not stuffy as Dexter would have expected.","Even the seat was padded with adaptive memory foam that adjusted to the user’s body shape.","\"This is one of our flagship products,\" the receptionist said enthusiastically.","\"The neural choker reads the user’s motor cortex impulses. The user simply thinks about where they want to go, and the wheelchair responds instantly.\"","She gestured to the wheels. \"It can navigate stairs, both up and down, using retractable treads. It automatically detects changes in elevation and adjusts its center of gravity accordingly.\"","Dexter sighed and knew he was going to be drained once more as he asked. \"How much?\"","\"One hundred and twenty thousand dollars.\"","Dexter blinked. Then blinked again.","$120,000. For a wheelchair.","He stared at the chair, then at the choker, then back at the chair.","One hundred and twenty thousand dollars just so a necklace could read someone’s mind and move them around.","He nearly laughed. For that price, he could push Mira himself for the next ten years.","*I’d rather be the one to push her,* he thought, shaking his head.","The receptionist, sensing his hesitation, quickly continued her pitch.","\"Sir, if I may—the wheelchair’s functions go far beyond simple mobility. Allow me to demonstrate.\"","She activated a holographic display above the chair, showing a detailed simulation of its capabilities.","\"The neural-link system also includes an automated toileting function,\" she explained, swiping through the display. \"When the user needs to use the restroom, the wheelchair’s seat module reconfigures, safely transferring the user to a toilet fixture and then returning them to a seated position afterward. This process is fully automated and requires no external assistance.\"","Dexter’s expression shifted slightly.","\"The wheelchair also contains a built-in emergency toilet system within the base,\" she continued. \"For situations where a restroom is not accessible, the chair can process waste internally through a sanitization cycle, maintaining complete hygiene and dignity for the user.\"","Dexter hesitated. The price was still staggering. But the functions... were functionable. Mira might be slightly less embarrassed by this.","If Mira had this wheelchair, she could move herself anywhere in the house. Outside, bathroom, toilet.","Most importantly, she wouldn’t need him to carry her to the toilet or transfer her from the chair to the bed.","She would have her independence back.","Dexter sighed and pulled out his phone. \"I’ll take it.\"","The receptionist beamed. \"Wonderful choice, sir.\"","As she began processing the order, a middle aged salesman approached Dexter cautiously.","\"Excuse me, sir,\" he said. \"I hope you don’t mind me asking, but I’m guessing the person you’re buying this for is a friend or family member who is paralyzed?\"","Dexter frowned at the man and his gaze turned cold.","The salesman quickly raised both hands. \"No, no, sir—please don’t misunderstand. I’m not making light of the situation. I simply wanted to introduce you to some companion products that I believe would significantly improve the user’s quality of life.\"","Dexter’s frown eased slightly. \"Go ahead.\"","The salesman gestured toward a large, rectangular box nearby. The box was sleek and white, with a glass front panel revealing what looked like a compact, vertical pod.","\"This is our Self-Operating Human Shower System,\" the salesman explained. \"It’s a Grade-One Arctech device designed to pair directly with the Neural-Linked Wheelchair. When the two systems are connected, the wheelchair can automatically transfer the user into the shower pod, where the system bathes them entirely—hair, body, everything—in under five minutes. Once the cycle is complete, the user is dried up dressed and then transferred back into the wheelchair.\"","He tapped the glass panel, and the pod hummed, demonstrating a series of internal spray nozzles and drying vents.","\"It’s fully customizable—water temperature, pressure, soap type, hair treatment. And because it’s mana-powered, it uses less than two liters of water per cycle.\"","Dexter stared at the shower pod. His mind went back to every morning he had spent carefully lifting Mira into the bathtub, washing her hair, scrubbing her skin, drying her with towels—all while she sat there with her ears burning.","Dexter assumed she was humiliated by it.","If he had this machine, Mira could bathe herself. Privately. Without him seeing her naked or touching her.","The salesman, reading Dexter’s expression, pressed his advantage. He pointed to a smaller device beside the shower pod—a compact, self-contained unit about the size of a mini fridge.","\"And this is our companion Portable Toilet System. It pairs with both the wheelchair and the shower unit, creating a complete personal care ecosystem. The wheelchair can transfer the user to any of these three systems—shower, toilet, or back to the chair—entirely through neural-link commands.\"","Dexter stood there, surrounded by three pieces of technology that could give Mira back her privacy, her dignity, and her independence.","\"How much for all three?\"","The salesman’s eyes widened slightly. \"The wheelchair is $120,000. The shower system is $180,000. The portable toilet system is $100,000. As a bundled package, that’s $400,000 total.\"","$400,000.","Dexter exhaled slowly. Three Grade-One Arch-tech devices for $400,000.","It was an astronomical sum for Grade-One items. But these weren’t weapons or cultivation tools—they were Arctechs. Very expensive.","But the value of Mira’s dignity? That was priceless.","\"I’ll take all three.\"","The salesman nearly vibrated with excitement. \"Excellent, sir! I’ll process the full bundle immediately.\"","While the paperwork was being prepared, Dexter wandered through the store.","His eyes landed on a display of newer smartphones with enhanced durability, and expanded battery life.","He purchased four.","Dexter inputted his home address for delivery of the wheelchair system, shower pod, and portable toilet. The store confirmed that a specialized installation team would follow him back to his home to install the items."]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116 | What Do Women Want?","paragraphs":["Dexter parked the Vanguard V4 in front of the bungalow just as the sun fully set.","He killed the engine and proceeded to revive his finances.","Starting balance: $1,070,000.","Vanguard V4 SUV: -$280,000.","Neural-Linked Wheelchair bundle: -$400,000.","Four mana-infused smartphones: -$8,000.","Fashion Items:- $ 70,000","Remaining balance: $312,000.","The delivery truck from Hextech Innovations was already parked outside the gate, and the installation team was unloading the boxes.","Dexter entered the house, carrying with him the Neural-Linked Wheelchair. He wanted to surprise Mira himself.","Mira was the only one in the living room. She sat in her old, hospital-issue wheelchair by the window, her eyes closed in deep cultivation.","She didn’t open her eyes even when he entered, but her brows twitched, letting Dexter know she knew he was here.","\"How are you?\" Dexter asked, walking over to her. \"I hope you’re doing well.\"","Mira opened her eyes, breaking her meditation as she glanced at him from the corner of her eye.","Her lips curled into a mocking smile. \"You’re back from playing with your other women?\"","Dexter was speechless. \"You know jealousy isn’t good for the body, right?\"","Mira sneered and was about to deliver one of her usual sharp retorts, when her gaze landed on the object beside Dexter.","It was a wheelchair, but it looked entirely different from hers. It was futuristic, sleek, and quite pretty.","Her crimson eyes narrowed. \"What is this?\"","Dexter smiled, beaming with pride. \"A gift. I got you an advanced wheelchair. I thought this might be more comfortable than the one you’re currently using.\"","He gestured to the silver choker resting on the seat. \"This one can read your mind. It carries your brain waves and determines where you wish to go or what you wish to do. It can even take you to the toilet and bathe you with just a thought.\"","He smiled proudly, fully expecting Mira to be thankful.","After all, he had spent $400,000 on this ecosystem. It was the ultimate solution to her lack of independence.","Suddenly, Mira’s eyes slowly started to glow until they turned blazingly fiery.","The temperature of the room rose to a drastic degree it was as though a sun was sitting in the center of the room!","Ever since they got the Grand Cosmos Scripture, they could use the star nodes to power their talents without the need to use mana.","A dangerous, burning anger flared in her crimson irises.","Dexter’s smile faltered. He frowned, taking a step back. \"You’re... angry?\" he asked, though it was more of a statement than a question.","Mira glanced at him, then at the high-tech wheelchair, and then simply closed her eyes, turning her face away.","’ What the hell?’","Dexter stood there, completely confused. He blinked his eyes and looked down at the wheelchair, and then at Mira who was radiating so much heat it was almost unbearable.","’ What did I do wrong? I’m obviously trying my best here; how did she manage to turn it around and get angry?’","He scratched the back of his head, wondering what on earth he had done wrong.","He sighed and then proceeded to check the girls in the bedroom.","Lyra was the only one inside. She sat cross-legged on her new fluffy bed, cultivating but Selene wasn’t there. So he assumed she was in the backyard.","Feeling his presence, Lyra opened her eyes.","Suddenly, a melodic voice sounded directly inside Dexter’s mind.","’ Don’t you want to take care of Mira anymore?’","Dexter blinked, greatly startled by the question.","’ Have you finally grown tired of her?’ Lyra continued as her voice took an accusatory tone.","’ Do you consider her and us a burden to you now?’","\"What?\" Dexter frowned, projecting his thoughts back to her. ’ What do you mean, don’t I want to take care of Mira any longer? Of course I want to take care of her.’","’ So why did you get her that particular wheelchair that can read her mind and take care of her? ’ Lyra asked.","Dexter almost yanked his hair out in frustration. ’ I thought she wanted to be independent! After the bathroom incident, I wanted to make her life a little bit easier. That was why I got the advanced wheelchair for her. I didn’t think she wouldn’t like it. Why didn’t she like it?’","Lyra blinked her eyes, gazing at Dexter’s face but seeing he was truly serious. She shook her head slowly, a faint, knowing smile touching her lips. ’She’s really angry. Which allows me access to her thoughts right now. Moreover, it’s loud.’","\"So what should I do?\" Dexter asked, rubbing the back of his neck. \"Explain to her that I just want to make her life easier. That was the exact reason why I bought the wheelchair in the first place.\"","Lyra shook her head again. ’ You should probably return it. She already likes the usual routine. She might not admit it, but she likes you taking care of her. Asking her to change that routine... she doesn’t like that.’","Suddenly Lyra hesitated but then a hidden devilish smile crossed her face.’ She doesn’t want a machine to replace you. Maybe she has feelings for you? I can’t tell.’","Dexter froze.","’ Replace me? Might have feelings for me? ’","[A/N: For conversations with Lyra, do you guys want it bold or italic?]","Dexter stared at Lyra, utterly baffled. He thought Mira disliked the sight of him and hated every second of him bathing her, carrying her, and feeding her.","He thought she was humiliated by her dependence on him, which was why he bought the three machines to surprise her.","But she actually ’liked’ the routine? She liked him doing it?","Dexter smiled bitterly, rubbing his face with both hands. \"I really don’t understand women at all,\" he muttered. \"Why are you all so confusing!?\"","Lyra glanced at him and let out a faint smirk as she closed her eyes and resumed her cultivation.","Just then, the installation team from Hexatech was about to come in, carrying massive boxes that contained the Self-Operating Human Shower System and the Portable Toilet.","Dexter quickly intercepted them before they could enter the living room. \"Hold on, please return the items.\"","The man in charge of the installation looked surprised. \"Sir? We’ve not even installed it yet. Is there something not up to your standard?\"","Dexter shook his head. \"No, the equipment is perfect. There was just a... change of heart. I want a refund. Please return the items.\"","The man blinked, stunned. \"A refund? But you already paid for the full bundle...\"","\"I know,\" Dexter sighed. \"Just pack it up and process the refund. I’ll cover any restocking fees.\"","The man eventually nodded, though he looked highly confused. He signaled his workers, and they began carrying the heavy boxes back out toward the truck.","Dexter stood in the doorway, watching them go.","After the workers left, Dexter went back to his room. He sat on his new fluffy bed, pondering the entire situation.","Everything was so weird. He thought she wanted nothing more than to be free of his help. But the moment he bought a machine that could do it all for her, she got really really angry.","He smiled bitterly, staring at the ceiling. ’ What do women truly want?’","He figured he would never truly understand.","Still, his mind wasn’t at rest knowing Mira was angry with him.","He remembered his portion of the pastries he had bought from Tessa’s bakery, which he had heated with his Heavenly Flame.","He also had some of the spiritual tea leaves left. He went to the kitchen, brewed a small pot of the sweet, rich grade-one tea, and plated a few of the warm pastries.","’ She should like this right? This should be enough to appease her right?’","He smiled as he carried the small tray into the living room. Mira was still in her wheelchair, facing the window, her eyes closed.","Dexter walked over and set the small table down right in front of her wheelchair.","Mira hearing the noise and smelling the scent of the tea and the pastries, opened her eyes.","She looked at the steaming tea and the warm pastries. Then, she looked at Dexter.","For a fraction of a second, the blazing flames in her eyes reduced slightly, but it wasn’t appeased.","Her face cold and without another word, she summoned her spectral arms, two glowing orange spectral arms materialized behind her.","They gripped the wheels of her wheelchair, and slowly, she turned until her back was turned towards Dexter.","Dexter stood there, holding the tray, staring at the back of her wheelchair.","He sighed deeply.","’ Women are really confusing.’"]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117 | Crimson Valkyrie That Loved The Rain","paragraphs":["Dexter stood awkwardly in the living room after Mira turned away from him, rejecting his apology meal as she radiated anger.","Even the tea in his hand was getting superheated by her aura.","Dexter sighed as he scratched his sprouting beards.","’ She’s really stubborn. Do I have to get down on my knees to say sorry for trying to help?’","He pursed his lips and turned around as he proceeded to the girl’s room. At that time, rain started to drizzle, beating down on the roof of the house.","As he got to the front of the room. He hadn’t even knocked yet when a dark-haired cutie popped her head out of the door, her eyes locked on the pastries and tea in Dexter’s hand with hunger.","Dexter chuckled. ’You’re easier to please.’","He said while giving her the tray.","Lyra glanced at him, and her lips curled up as she grabbed the tray.","She was about to leave when she suddenly paused. ’ Check her name on the internet.’","Lyra’s voice sounded in his head, and she immediately went inside before Dexter could ask what she really meant.","Dexter blinked his eyes in confusion. ’Search up her name?’","He had actually never truly done that. And all the gossip he heard about them was through random channels.","Dexter brought out his new phone, making him remember he hadn’t gifted the girls the new clothes and items he got.","’I just keep getting distracted and forgetting things.’ Dexter frowned. He turned on the Intranet app and typed on the search bar: Mira Calloway .","Several videos immediately popped up of her, but there was one in particular that stood out to him.","It was an old video from four years ago, back when she was the Crimson Valkyrie.","Dexter went inside his room, sat on the edge of the sofa, and pressed play.","The video opened with Mira sitting in a studio chair, dressed in a sleek, crimson-and-black combat suit.","She looked dazzling; her red hair was vibrant, her crimson eyes were bright with life, and she wore a massive, radiant smile. She looked like the sun itself, burning with fiery confidence and an infectious energy that lit up the screen.","Dexter played the video and he was immediately enthralled by it.","After 20 minutes, he got to a particular section.","The interviewer laughed. \"So, Mira, tell us. What is the one thing you really love? The one thing that can uplift you even during a bad day?\"","Mira tilted her head thoughtfully, a playful glint in her eyes. \"Ah, the one thing I love?\"","\"Yes! And you can’t say your parents, your fiancé, or your fans,\" the interviewer added jokingly.","Mira chuckled and it sounded so bright and melodic it seemed to belong to an entirely different person than the woman sitting behind him in the living room. \"That doesn’t leave much, does it?\"","She paused as her expression softened.","\"The one thing I love... is rain.\"","The interviewer’s lips parted, clearly surprised. \"Rain? But your talent is fire-based. Why rain?\"","Mira shrugged, her smile widening into something genuinely warm. \"I know, right? Maybe in my past life, I was probably a Legend-rank water ability user. That’s probably why I love it so much.\" She paused again, her gaze drifting slightly.","\"But honestly? Ever since I was a kid, I would go out into the rain anytime. Anytime I’m in a bad mood... if it rains, it melts my mood like ice.\"","The interviewer laughed loudly, and Mira laughed along with him.","\"Alright. We end the segment of...\"","Dexter lowered his phone. His face was clearly stunned.","’Did the feisty queen actually laugh?’","It was quite a surprise to him, as he had never even seen her smile for real.","The most he had seen was a half smile or a sneer.","Suddenly Dexter grinned as he heard the downpour of rain increasing even more.","He stood up and walked to the living room. Without a word, he walked towards Mira and unlocked the wheels of her wheelchair.","Mira’s eyes snapped open. She turned her head slightly, glaring at him coldly. \"What do you think you’re doing?\"","Dexter didn’t answer. He simply gripped the handles and began rolling her toward the back door.","\"Dexter? What are you doing?\" Mira’s frown deepened.","But Dexter still didn’t reply.","Her voice immediately rose as she growled.","\"Dexter!\"","Dexter smiled. \"You’ll find out soon enough.\"","As they neared the back door, the sound of the heavy downpour grew louder, and the scent of wet earth filled the hallway.","\"Pitta! Patti! Pitta!\"","Mira’s eyes widened as she immediately put two and two together.","\"Don’t,\" she said threateningly, like a cat about to strike. Only, this cat is paralyzed.","Dexter shrugged, still moving forward. \"Don’t what?\"","\"Dexter, I’m warning you, don’t,\" she repeated in an even firmer tone.","But Dexter pretended like he wasn’t listening. But actually, his enhanced hearing had spread really wide.","He knew her well enough by now to tell when she was genuinely furious and when she was just trying to maintain her pride.","So, he ignored her half-hearted protest and continued moving.","Selene was already in the backyard, cultivating quietly under the shade of the roof.","She opened her white eyes, completely confused as she sensed Dexter wheeling Mira directly out into the pouring rain.","The moment the wheelchair crossed the threshold of the overhang, the rain hit them like hail of water bullets.","\"Whoosh!\"","The rain came down, slammed heavily against the earth, and as Mira was pushed out, the cold rain gushed on her.","Falling on Mira’s shoulders, her hair, her face, and body.","Within seconds, her red hair darkened from copper to deep burgundy, plastering itself against her skull and neck as her clothes soaked, clinging to her slim body and revealing her succulent chest and curvy waist.","However, Mira didn’t move, nor did she speak.","She just sat there in silence with her head tilted upwards and her eyes open as the rain dropped directly into her eyes and face without blinking.","It was just like he was watching a horror movie in real time.","Dexter’s heart dropped as a cold, sickening weight settled in his stomach.","’ Shit! Have I misread the situation?’","He stood there for 30 seconds as the rain poured on her but she simply sat there in a terrifying silence that grabbed Dexter’s heart second after second.","’ She’s changed.’","Three years of paralysis, bitterness, loss and rage and the slow, grinding erosion of everything she used to be.","Who was he to think that a video from the past could override all of that?","Who was he to think that the girl who loved the rain still existed somewhere inside this woman who couldn’t even lift her own arms?","He had actually made a grave mistake, and he knew at this moment, Mira might never forgive him for this.","’I truly messed up.’","However..."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118 | First Connection","paragraphs":["Trauma freezes you. It locks you behind a wall of your own making, but who you are is still waiting on the other side of the ice. - Neil Gaiman","...","Dexter realized at this moment that he had made a mistake.","A really terrible mistake.","He had dragged her out here against her will into the rain as if three years of suffering wasn’t enough to kill whatever life she had for the rain.","Guilt surged through him like ice water. He immediately went forward, opening his mouth to apologize and quickly drag her back into the house when he saw it.","It was her lips, and they had actually curled upwards.","And it wasn’t curled upwards into a sneer as he had expected; it was a smile!","She was actually smiling!","Dexter’s breath caught in his throat, and the guilt and panic he had been feeling at that moment evaporated in an instant.","Her smile continued to widen as she tilted her head upwards, letting the rain pour on her face.","Somehow, the smile wasn’t as radiant as what he had seen in the interview and contained a hint of sadness. But it was the most genuine smile he had witnessed from Mira since he set eyes on her.","Then, slowly, two glowing orange spectral arms materialized behind her.","They unsteadily reached out into the downpour and scooped up handfuls of rainwater, bringing them back and gently pouring them over her face, neck, and arms.","She closed her eyes and scooped more as the arms continued to gather rainwater, letting it cascade over her.","Mira’s smile widened even further as a cute giggle escaped her lips.","Each handful seemed to wash and melt something within her.","Through it all, Dexter stood behind her, completely forgetting that he himself was getting soaked as his jaw hung slightly open in pure shock.","Had she actually giggled?","In all the time he had known her, he had never once seen Mira like this. Not once.","And the sight of the quiet, devastating beauty of this woman giggling in the rain made Dexter’s heart tremble with something he hadn’t felt in a long time.","No matter what happened to a person, the essence of who they were could never truly be destroyed. It could be suppressed, locked behind walls of anger and bitterness and pain, but it would always remain.","And with the right spark, it could always shine again.","...","Selene, who was standing beneath the overhang, had a soft, quiet smile on her face.","\"So that’s what you look like. You’re perfect.\"","She muttered as the vibration from the rain hitting Dexter’s body perfectly outlined his face and his figure. Everything was extremely detailed as she saw him clearly for the first time.","---","Dexter stood behind Mira in the downpour, completely soaked to the bone, yet he couldn’t feel the cold.","He was entirely too stunned by what he was seeing.","Even after 5 straight minutes of watching Mira play in the rain, scooping water with her spectral arms like a child, he still couldn’t believe his eyes.","Slowly, Dexter reached out and gripped the handles of her old wheelchair. The feeling seemed to bring Mira back to herself.","She immediately tried to wipe the joy from her face, attempting to rebuild her icy walls. But it was too late. Her lips didn’t cooperate with her, still locked in that perfectly radiant smile.","She felt Dexter’s gaze on her, and it was hot and intense.","Mira turned around and glared at Dexter, her crimson eyes narrowing with as much menace as she could muster, which, given the smile still ghosting across her face, was not nearly enough.","\"What are you looking at?\" she snapped.","Dexter stared at her. His mind went completely blank.","He looked at her rain-soaked body, her flushed face and those pretty crimson eyes glaring at him, and spoke without thinking.","\"You are really beautiful.\"","It was like a stone dropped into a still lake.","Mira froze.","For three years, no one had called her beautiful.","For three years, she had been the disabled talented heroine.","No one looked at her and saw beauty. No one looked at her like Dexter was.","And now this infuriating, reckless, stubbornly kind idiot was looking at her like she was the most breathtaking thing he had ever seen.","A deep crimson flush bloomed across her pale cheeks as her cold demeanor cracked.","She tried to retort or say something, but nothing came out.","Dexter saw the blush on her cheeks and her bashful eyes.","A sudden, reckless, playful impulse that he couldn’t resist surged through him, and he smirked playfully.","Mira’s eyes widened further. Her blush—if possible—deepened another shade. She looked away sharply, her jaw working, her spectral arms retracting against her sides as though she could somehow make herself smaller.","\"What are you trying to do?\" she demanded, her voice cracking slightly on the last word. She cleared her throat, trying to recover. \"What are you planning?\"","Dexter grinned.","\"What don’t you guess?\"","He tightened his grip on the wheelchair handles.","Then, without warning, he took off running as he pushed her around the backyard, spinning her in circles.","Like a father pushing a child at a park.","Mira wyws wiended.","\"Don’t you dare drop me—\" she growled in a commanding tone.","It was at that moment the wheelchair hit a puddle and sent a spray of water directly into her face.","Mira sputtered and blinked as the water fell down her face onto her clothes.","Dexter froze instantly and then burst out laughing as he pointed at her stained face.","Mira’s lips twitched and then, against her every will, Mira actually laughed.","...","From the window of the neighboring one-story building, Tessa watched them, and a small smile spread across her freckled face.","\"Dexter,\" Tessa murmured to herself, leaning against the window wall. \"You’re cute.\"","She felt a swell of warmth in her chest as she watched Dexter play with Mira, laughing like a kid.","For a moment, Tessa almost thought the two people actually married for love and not because of a silly contract."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119 | REWARDS!!!","paragraphs":["Thirty minutes later, Dexter finally wheeled a thoroughly soaked Mira back inside the house.","Her lips were still curled into a smile she couldn’t suppress, no matter how hard she tried to rebuild her cold mask.","Dexter wheeled her into the bathroom.","Without a word, he carefully stripped her naked by removing her soaked clothes, placing them in a pile by the side of the tub.","He adjusted the shower to a warm temperature carried Mira and placed her underneath the warm shower.","Mira didn’t blush this time nor did she give any sarcastic remarks.","She simply sat there, smiling quietly with her crimson eyes half-closed in contentment as Dexter took care of her.","The warm water rinsed away the rain and the cold, and she let herself simply exist in the moment.","Dexter carefullt washed her hair, arms and legs with soft sponge and soap and then turned off the shower, wrapped her in a fresh towel, and carefully dried her hair,","After which, he dressed her in a soft, warm cardigan and comfortable trousers.","Mira glanced up at him. \"Your fashion sense is terrible.","Dexter rolled his eye and smiled. \"Bite me.\"","Usually, she would have fired off a witty remark about how men shouldn’t say stuffs like that. But she simply rolled her eyes. She was still in a good mood.","Dexter carried her to her new bed the fluffy queen mattress the delivery workers had set up that morning. He gently placed her down, arranging the pillows behind her back so she could rest comfortably and covered her up with the duffel.","\"Sleep well.\"","He was about to turn and leave when something suddenly wrapped around his wrist.","He looked down and saw a glowing orange spectral arm had extended from behind Mira, its translucent fingers curled gently around his forearm.","Dexter turned toward her. Mira was lying with her back flat on the bed but she had turned her face from him, making her red hair fan out across the white pillow.","Then she mumbled in a small voice.","\"Thank you. It was nice.\"","Dexter smiled gently as warmth bloomed in his chest. he whispered back.","\"Any time.\"","The spectral arm slowly faded into nothing, realizing his wrist.","Mira closed her eyes and within minutes, her breathing slowed as she fell into the deepest, most peaceful sleep she had experienced in three years.","Dexter quietly left the bedroom, closing the door behind him. He was pondering what to make for dinner for the other two girls who would definitely eat when—","[Ding!]","Golden text erupted across his vision as notifications popped up all over his line of sight.","–––","[10,000x Investment Multiplier System]","[Investment Return Activated]","[Every investment made for the targets has been evaluated...]","[100× Return Multiplier Activated!]","–––","[Reward 1]","Three Premium Beds Invested.","Obtained: Three Grade-3 Spirit Dream Beds","Each bed is forged from Dreamwood and Void Silk. While sleeping on them:","• Cultivation speed increases by 200%.","• Mental fatigue disappears after only one hour of sleep.","• Nightmares cannot affect the sleeper.","• Mana recovery increases by 200%.","• The body continuously absorbs surrounding mana even while asleep.","• Minor injuries slowly heal throughout the night.","–––","[Reward 2]","Three Type-3 Weapons Invested → 100× Return Granted","Obtained:","• Type-6 Shadow Sovereign Sword","• Type-6 Inferno Phoenix Blade","• Type-6 Ice Titan Queen Greatsword","–––","[Reward 3]","Meals Cooked for Wives → 100× Return Granted","Obtained: Three Grade-5 Arcane Recipes","1. Heavenly Phoenix Dragon Steak","Temporarily increases fire affinity, strength, regeneration, and cultivation speed.","Duration: Seven days per serving.","2. Nine-Star Moonfish Essence Soup","Greatly increases mana recovery, strengthens the soul, improves concentration, and permanently increases spiritual perception after repeated consumption.","3. Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice","Improves physical constitution, removes cultivation impurities, greatly enhances mana absorption, and increases breakthrough success rate.","[Extra: Buying ingredients for wives]","Ingredients Received (10× Quantity per recipe):","• 10 Celestial Phoenix Steaks","• 10 Moonlight Spirit Fish","• 10 Star Crystal Rice portions","• 10 World Tree Leaves","• 10 Thousand-Year Spirit Mushrooms","• 10 Dragon Blood Peppers","• 10 Heavenly Snow Lotus Petals","• 10 bottles of Celestial Spring Water","–––","[Reward 4]","Pastries Purchased → 100× Return Granted","Obtained: Grade-3 Celestial Moon Pastries × 100","For one month after consumption:","• Cultivation speed increases by 50%, 0 side effect.","• Mental clarity greatly improves.","• Mana recovery becomes significantly faster.","• Physical fatigue is reduced.","• Hunger is greatly suppressed for a month.","–––","[Reward 5]","Three Necklaces Invested → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: Two Type-4 Necklaces","1. Type-4 Virgo’s Might Necklace","A life-saving treasure containing the full-powered attack of a Transcendent Realm expert. Once activated, it unleashes a devastating beam capable of heavily injuring—or even killing—an early Transcendent Realm cultivator.","Uses Remaining: 1/1","2. Type-4 Aurora’s Guardian Necklace","A defensive treasure capable of sensing fatal danger. The instant the wearer encounters a life-threatening attack, the necklace automatically teleports them anywhere within a 100-mile radius.","Can only be activated once before needing to be recharged with mana.","–––","[Reward 6]","Tier-4 Heaven Saber Technique: Thunder GodKill Saber Art","1) First Move: Godslayer Flash","2) Second Move: Roaring Thunder Fang","3) Third Move: Eightfold Lightning Severance","3) Fourth Move: Thunder Dragon’s Descent","5) Fifth Move: Divine Tempest Rend","6) Sixth Move: Ninefold Thunder Prison","7) Seventh Move: Wrath of the Thunder God","8) Eighth Move: Myriad Lightning Cataclysm","9) Ninth Move: Godkill Judgment","–––","[Reward 7]","Time spent to Prepare Meals for Wives → Reward Granted","Obtained: Two Years of Cultivation","–––","[Reward 8]","Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture evolves to Indestructible Buddha Endurance Body (Tier 7)","–––","[Reward 9]","Extreme Slaughtering Demon Body Tempering Art has evolved to Asura Slaughter Demon Body (Tier 6)","–––","[Reward 10]","Talent Upgraded: Enhanced Hearing — C-Rank → B-Rank","–––","[Reward 11]","Investment Detected: Purchased SUV for Family Transportation → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: Type-6 Arcane SUV — Ultima Skybreaker","A masterpiece forged by master Arcane Engineers and Arcane Blacksmiths.","Abilities:","• Transcendent Armor: Chassis forged from Type-6 Arcane Alloy, capable of withstanding several full-powered attacks from a Transcendent Realm expert.","• Flight Mode: By consuming Mana Cores, deploys hidden jet thrusters and can fly at tremendous speed.","• Ultra-Speed Engine: Top speed rivals a Peak Ultra Realm expert.","• Mana Cannon: Mounted beneath the chassis; capable of severely injuring an Ultra Realm expert and threatening an early Transcendent Realm cultivator.","• Arcane Machine Guns: Twin mana-powered machine guns with automatic hostile target lock-on.","• Adaptive Shield: Energy barrier automatically activates when danger is sensed.","• Amphibious Mode: Can travel across water and underwater for extended periods.","• Self-Repair System: Minor damage repaired automatically using stored mana.","• Spatial Storage Trunk: Contains a storage space several times larger than its exterior dimensions.","And that wasn’t all!"]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120 | REWARDS 2!!!","paragraphs":["[Reward 12]","Investment Detected: Purchased Mobile Phones → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: Three Type-3 Arcane Smart Devices","• Self-charging through mana and body heat.","• Unlimited internet access through automatic satellite synchronization.","• Can perform minor hacks to other devices","• Built-in emergency distress beacon.","• High-grade encrypted communications.","–––","[Reward 13]","Investment Detected: Purchased Ice Suppressant Medicine → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: Thirty Grade-3 Eternal Frost Suppressant Serums","Each serum suppresses unstable ice energy for one full week. While active:","• Ice outbreaks are completely halted.","• Pain caused by frost energy is greatly reduced.","• The user’s body slowly adapts to the ice energy instead of rejecting it.","–––","[Reward 14]","Investment Detected: Giving Possible Companion: Ancient Beast Egg → 100× Return Activated!","Reward: Incubation Accelerated","The incubation time has been reduced by 90%.","–––","[Reward 15]","Investment Detected: Cooked for wives → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: 100 Kilograms of Premium Diamond Spirit Rice","–––","[Reward 16]","Investment Detected: Protected Selene from Cold Energy → Reward Option Unlocked","Fusion Opportunity Available","Would you like to fuse the following flames?","• Heavenly Flame (Emperor Void Flame)","• Demonic Flame (Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline)","Fusion Result: Abyssal Heart Flame (6th Heavenly Flame)","–––","[Reward 17]","Target: Mira — Happiness Level Increased → 100× Return Activated!","Obtained: Grade-5 Divine Nerve Restoration Pill ×1","A legendary medicinal pill capable of restoring damaged nerves.","Effects:","• Instantly heals 20% of all damaged nerves.","• Greatly accelerates the regeneration of remaining damaged nerves.","• Permanently increases nerve vitality.","• Can only be consumed once every six months.","–––","[Reward 18]","Special Family Reward — Three girls’ trust has increased simultaneously.","Obtained: Family Guardian Barrier Formation (Grade-6)","A defensive formation that can be installed in the house. Once activated:","• Prevents enemies below the Transcendent Realm from entering by force.","• Conceals the house from ordinary perception.","• Detects hostile intent.","• Automatically alerts Dexter whenever an intruder approaches.","• Can operate continuously using Nexus Cores.","–––","The stream of golden notifications finally ended.","Dexter who was on his way to the kitchen was entirely stunned.","His face was flushed and he was panting heavily without him knowing!","Not to mention, his hands were trembling from the sheer magnitude of the rewards!","Three Type-6 relic weapons, a flying, armored, weaponized SUV. Grade-6 recipes and heavenly ingredients. A Grade-6 defensive barrier for the house and dozens of other priceless treasures.","Even a Transcendent Realm expert would go mad with envy if they learned what he had obtained in a single day!","If these items were suddenly found in the city, every family would wage war on each other for these items with him and yet, he had earned it all by buying, cooking meals, and pushing a wheelchair into the rain.","Dexter slowly exhaled as a wide smile spread across his face. The excitement that had calmed down after coming back from the rain increased drastically.","\"Worth it.\"","He looked toward the bedroom door, behind which Mira was were sleeping on the new bed he purchased for them and he couldn’t help but grin.","\"What a wonderful day!\"","...","Dexter sat cross-legged on his bed with widened eyes like a restless child on Christmas morning.","He pulled up the system interface again, and began sorting through his rewards one by one.","’Thankfully the Type 3 beds looks just the same as the one I bought. The girls shouldn’t suspect a thing.’","But he knew the girls would definitely notice something was off once the effect of the items started to show.","The three Type-6 weapons also retained the appearances of the Type-3 relics he had bought from the Ultra realm person at the black market.","’Seems like the system likes being discreet also.’ Dexter muttered in thought.","He decided to swap them when they were sleeping.","Of course the girls would notice the difference the moment they actually channeled mana into them, but he wasn’t worried. He wasn’t going to let them fight anytime soon anyway. He would protect them from everything.","His mind shifted to the three Grade-6 Arcane Recipes.l and his mouth practically watered.","The system had generously provided ten full portions of ingredients for each recipe.","Even if he failed a few times, with his Great Grandmaster Foodsmith proficiency, he was confident he could produce at least six or seven successful Grade-6 meals.","Also there was the Grade-4 Celestial Moon Pastries were. He planned to give them to the girls later while they cultivated, letting them munch on the pastries to sustain their energy and boost their absorption rates.","As for the two Type-4 Arcane Necklaces; the Transcendent Strike and the Spatial Guardian, hw planned to swap them with the girls’ current necklaces around 4’o clock.","They always slept deeply around that time.","Then there was the Tier-4 Martial Technique: Thunder GodKill Saber Art.","Dexter’s eyes sparkled as the knowledge of the saber art settled into his mind.","He had desperately needed a martial art. The fact that he had managed to kill those two Superhuman assassins on the highway was purely because of his bloodline and his type 3 weapon skill: Spatial Cleave.","Without the relic weapon and the bloodline he would have definitely died.","Now, he had a true, high-grade martial art for attacking and improving his attacks.","As for the two years of compressed cultivation. Dexter rolled his eyes. His cooking speed had advanced which was why he cooked with less and less time. Otherwise, he would have gained at least 5 to 7 years of cultivation.","Dexter closed his eyes. \"System, accept the Two Years of Cultivation.\"","Instantly, a roaring tsunami of pure, refined mana erupted from the core of his system, slamming into his physical body.","\"Bang! Bang! Bang!\"","Deep inside Dexter’s inner universe, the entire universe had changed drastically.","There were now seven star nodes around the massive, twelve-segmented helix-shaped DNA structure floating in the darkness of the universe.","But that wasn’t all, there was now a massive crackling blue cloud and a roaring golden flames in the inner universe.","Those were actually the two talents he extracted from the corpses of the two superhuman experts.","The Thunder and the golden flames were above and below the massive helix shape structure. Connected to it tightly.","The massive, twelve-segmented helix-shaped DNA structure spun slowly in the darkness.","The first three segments were already blazing with brilliant light.","As the two years’ worth of cultivation energy surged into the void, the darkness around the helix shattered. The energy crashed into the fourth segment.","\"BOOM!\"","The fourth segment lit up instantly, glowing tendrils extending downward to connect with the fifth.","The fifth segment began to glow, filling rapidly with vibrant energy until it reached its peak. It then extended tendrils to the sixth, lighting it up, and continued cascading all the way down to the seventh segment.","The flood of energy finally exhausted itself, leaving the seventh segment fully illuminated.","Dexter opened his eyes and a shockwave of energy rippled through his bedroom. He had broken through and he was now at the Seventh Stage of the Superhuman Realm!","Along with his cultivation leap, his body-tempering scriptures had evolved.","The Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture had upgraded to a Tier-7 technique, officially renamed the Indestructible Buddha Endurance Body.","The stages of the technique remained the same, but their effects had been magnified terrifyingly."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121 | Sorting Out Rewards","paragraphs":["The Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture had upgraded to a Tier-7 technique, officially renamed the Indestructible Buddha Endurance Scripture.","The stages of the technique remained the same, but their effects had been magnified terrifyingly.","The first stage, Iron Flesh, had previously made his skin as hard as steel. Now, his flesh was tightened and strengthened until it was vastly superior to refined steel.","The second stage which was Iron Bones, had drastically increased his bone density and strength.","Right now, he was currently at the third stage, the Golden Organs.","At this moment, he could feel his internal organs hardening, taking on a lustrous, gold-like resilience.","The chronic pain he continuously absorbed from Mira, Lyra, and Selene was actively tempering his organs. He could feel that he was on the edge of breaking through to the fourth stage. It wouldn’t be long now.","But it was the evolution of his second body art that truly caught his attention. The Extreme Slaughter Demon Body had evolved into the Asura Slaughter Demon Body.","Dexter frowned, rubbing his temples.","The technique actually bordered on evil.","The Asura Slaughter Demon Body was not like other body tempering techniques, it was extremely terrifying.","A practitioner of this art could possess the physical strength of a Transcendent Realm expert while their mana cultivation lagged far behind.","But the cost was steep.","The technique relied on something called slaughter Energy and it can only be harvested from a freshly killed corpse.","According to the technique, slaughter energy existed within a dying body for only the first ten to fifteen minutes after death. Human or beast, it didn’t matter. The moment a life was extinguished, the energy began to dissipate, vanishing completely within a quarter of an hour.","If he wanted to cultivate this technique, he had to be the one whose hands ended the life, only then could the slaughter energy be absorbed.","Asura Slaughter Demon Body","Description: A forbidden body refinement art that tempers the flesh through slaughter. Unlike ordinary body cultivation techniques that rely on mana, the Asura Slaughter Body evolves the body itself. Every kill strengthens the host’s muscles, bones, blood, organs, and meridians, gradually transforming them into the physique of a true Asura.*","Cultivation Requirements:","• 10 kills — Meta Stage","• 100 kills — Superhuman Stage","• 1,000 kills — Ultra Realm","• 10,000 kills — Transcendent Realm","• 100,000 kills — Peak Transcendent Realm","• 1,000,000 kills — Supreme Realm","• 10,000,000 kills — Mid Supreme Realm","• 100,000,000 kills — Peak Supreme Realm","• 1,000,000,000 kills — Legendary","–––","Dexter eyes widened in surprise. ’This technique is actually this terrifying?’","It actually possess a way to become a Legendary expert by simply killing.","One million kills for the Supreme Realm. One hundred million for Peak Supreme. One billion for Legendary.","He knew that if this technique fell into the wrong hands, the world would definitely burn.","There were people in this city, in this country, on this continent who would willingly sacrifice a hundred million lives to reach the Transcendent Realm not to mention Legendary.","If Dexter had not met the girls and had come across this technique, he wouldn’t hesitate either.","Before the marriage and the system, Dexter’s life had been cold and bitter. Treated as a slave by his own family.","Another darker truth was that the Assassins on the bridge weren’t his first kill either.","But now...","Now he didn’t hesitate either. The world be damned. If it’s to burn the entire city down or wipe the entire Ashford family become a Legend rank hero, he wouldn’t hesitate.","The Frost, Callowell and Vance family would be added bonus.","But the technique did not specify human kills.","Which meant that the slaughter energy could be harvested from any living creature that possessed life force.","Dexter’s ran his tongue across his lips.","Dungeons, he could head into a dungeon and clear the monsters there.","One thousand kills for the Ultra Realm was achievable within a month.","Ten thousand kills for the Transcendent Realm—achievable within three to five months.","One hundred thousand kills for Peak Transcendent—achievable within three to a year to two years of relentless dungeon raiding.","A Peak Transcendent Realm expert in two years.","Dexter leaned back as he smiled smirked.","Others spent 500 to 1000 years to reach the Transcendent Realm with mountains of resources, and dungeon raiding","But with this technique, he could do it in a year or two!","In the entire city, the number of Transcendent Realm experts could be counted on one hand. A Peak Transcendent could do whatever they wanted in the city with not many people that could stop them.","Dexter smiled. ’Now with my energy cultivation and body cultivation, things would be even simpler.’","With the extraction ability, his physique was alredy strong. Now with the body refinement art, he would be unstoppable.","He moved on to the next reward.","–––","The Vibrum Skybreaker — Type-6 Arcane SUV","Dexter was genuinely excited as he pulled up the vehicle’s specifications.","The most remarkable thing about the vehicle was its appearance. Despite being a Type-6 combat-grade vehicle with enough firepower to level a district, it looked.l very ordinary.","From the outside, it was indistinguishable from a standard family SUV.","But on the inside, it was a fortress. Armor plating that could tank a hit from a Transcendent Realm expert. Hidden jet thrusters that enabled full flight.","An ultra-speed engine that could outrun a Peak Ultra Realm expert and an explosive mana cannon concealed that could severely injure an Ultra Realm expert and threaten an early Transcendent, etc.","Dexter grinned. His fear of being sniped through the window vanished.","–––","Three Type-3 Arcane Smart Devices","Dexter shrugged at the phones. They were useful, certainly, but less thrilling than a flying armored SUV. The unlimited internet and calling access was a nice perk.","–––","Grade-3 Eternal Frost Suppressant Serums 30x","Dexter immediately sighed in relief.","With the serum, Selene wouldn’t break out in seven months.","–––","As for the Ancient Primordial Beast Egg reduction to 90%.","Dexter was excited about it.","’What kind of beast was inside? A dragon? A phoenix? Or something even better?’"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122 | Abyssal Emperor Demon Bloodline","paragraphs":["Dexter’s eyes drifted to the rice reward.","’One hundred kilograms of Diamond Spirit Rice?’","He rolled his eyes.","’I already have 1,100 kilograms sitting in my system storage from previous rewards. I haven’t even touched most of them yet.’","If the system really wanted to impress him, it could have dropped 10,000 kilograms.","He moved on, and his gaze landed on the next reward, and his pupils constricted.","[Fusion Available]","Would you like to fuse the following flames?","• Heavenly Flame: Emperor Void Flame (9th Heavenly Flame)","• Golden Flame Talent ( C-rank)","• Demonic Flame: Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline (Ancient Grade)","Fusion Result: Abyssal Emperor Flame Demon Bloodline","Flame Rank: 6th Heavenly Flame in the Flame Rankings","Dexter frowned as he remembered something from Selene’s status.","According to the system’s diagnosis, there were only two known methods to save her:","1. Locate a Grade-7 Heavenly Treasure called the Ice Warm Cocoon.","2. Acquire the Abyssal Demon Heart Flame—a legendary flame capable of slowly melting the Eternal Winter Ice without harming her physical organs.","But now, the system was offering him something called the Abyssal Emperor Flame.","Not the Abyssal Demon Heart Flame. The Abyssal Emperor Flame.","Dexter’s heart skipped a beat.","’What was the difference?’","The Abyssal Demon Heart Flame was born in the deepest trenches of the Demon Abyss. But the Abyssal Emperor Flame was the product of fusing a 9th Heavenly Flame, a golden flame talent, along with an Ancient Grade bloodline with flame ability.","If the Abyssal Demon Heart Flame could cure Selene... what could the Abyssal Emperor Flame do?","Dexter did not hesitate.","\"Fuse.\"","•—•—•","[Fusion Progress: 0%]","The moment said ’fuse’, his body instantly erupted with energy.","The Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline surged from deep within his DNA, igniting like a chain of volcanoes detonating simultaneously along every strand of his genetic code.","\"RUMBLE!\"","At the same time, the Emperor Void Flame blazed to life within his inner universe, roaring with a fury that shook his entire body.","[Fusion Progress: 2%]","The easiest was the Golden Flame talent. It was incredibly cooperative with two powerful flames suppressing it.","His veins popped beneath his skin, glowing a deep, molten crimson light that pulsed beneath the surface of his flesh as though his blood had turned into pure magma.","[Fusion Progress: 5%]","His veins lit up like rivers of fire coursing beneath transparent skin, painting his body in a web of burning, volcanic light.","Simultaneously, the Emperor Void Flame escaped his inner universe and came out to his physical body.","[Fusion Progress: 7%]","It suddenly spread outward like a golden flood, surging through his meridians, merging into his muscles, seeping into his bones as it merged with his bloodline.","The three flames collided inside him.","[Fusion Progress: 10%]","Dexter grunted as sweat started to drip off him rapidly.","The heat was indescribable, and it felt as though he was being cooked from the inside out! Not just that, he felt his soul was being stir fried!","The divine purity of the Emperor Void Flame, the silent Golden Flame, and the ancient, chaotic violence of the Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline clashed like three hurricanes spinning in opposite directions as they turned to emerge with each other.","[Fusion Progress: 20%]","Those two flames didn’t even merge when he tried to fuse them, and now they were being fused inside of him.","His expression changed drastically.","’This might have been a mistake.’","At that moment, the pain escalated beyond anything he had anticipated. It was ten times worse than the girls pain. This was raw, primordial agony. The three flames were tearing him apart and rebuilding him simultaneously.","[Fusion Progress: 30%]","Dexter’s quickly brought out the Tranquility Bracelet—one of the calming relics he had purchased for the girls—and slapped it onto his wrist.","A cool, soothing pulse spread through his nervous system, but it was barely helping!","It was like throwing stones into a still lake! It had no effect apart from ripples!","\"Hmph!\"","Dexter grunted in pain, and he tried his best not to scream and disturb the girls. But the pain he was feeling was just too painful. He had to bite down his lips, causing blood to drop on his white bed sheet.","’Why didn’t the system warn that it would be impossibly painful?’","Dexter roared in his mind as the pain started to reach a whole new threshold!","[Fusion Progress: 45%]","At that moment, the bed beneath his body started to burn rapidly, and in just half a second, it had silently disintegrated beneath him due to the heat from the violent reaction.","The Cloud Weaver bed evaporated into ash by the three flames.","Even the ash was consumed so thoroughly that not a single trace remained.","Dexter crashed to the floor.","He grunted in pain as his bare skin struck the wooden floorboards.","Suddenly, tears started to stream down his eyes.","However, the tears were not ordinary tears. They were crimson and thick, like blood but a thick, viscous blood.","If one looked at it, they would notice the blood glowing slightly as the blood tears ran down his cheeks. He was crying blood.","And it wasn’t just his eyes.","His pores began to turn bloody as blood came out of his pores.","That wasn’t all; his body was bleeding from every opening. His nose, his mouth, his ears rang with a high-pitched whine as warm liquid trickled from them.","The fusion progress climbed.","50%... 60%... 70%.","Dexter felt his consciousness fraying. The pain had transcended physical sensation and entered a realm of suffering that existed somewhere between life and death.","His body was being unmade and reforged at the same time, every cell destroyed and reborn in an endless, agonizing cycle, and at this moment, he knew if he didn’t do anything, he would definitely fall unconscious.","He remembered the pain medication he had taken after purchasing a pain relief for the girls. His shaking hand fumbled into his storage ring, withdrawing the Grade-2 Pain Alleviation Pill."]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123 | Handsome Appearance!","paragraphs":["The pill dissolved instantly. A wave of numbing coolness spread through his body, wrapping around his screaming nerves like a bandage.","But it wasn’t enough!","80%.","Dexter felt his limit approaching.","The fusion was consuming him. If he lost consciousness now for even a single second, the flames would consume him entirely. There would be nothing left but ash and a lingering trail of fire. No body. No soul. No Dexter.","The faces of Mira, Lyra, and Selene flashed through his mind.","Mira, laughing in the rain, her red hair plastered to her face, her spectral arms scooping water like a child playing in a puddle.","Lyra, blushing furiously as her telepathic voice whispered thank you inside his mind, her dark eyes shining with quiet gratitude.","Selene, clinging to his arm in the kitchen, her cold body pressed against his, purring softly as his warmth seeped into her frozen bones.","’I can’t leave them.’","The thought hit him with the force of lightning.","If he died here, alone, on the floor of his bedroom, consumed by his own ambition, Mira would never walk again. Lyra would never speak with her own voice as the shadow corruption takes place.","Selene would freeze to death, slowly and painfully, her ice consuming her from the inside out.","Their zeal might collapse, and they might actually become suicidal once more.","They had no one, no family, no protection. He was their only family, and if he died right here, it would be over for them.","’No!’","Dexter clenched his teeth hard as his fingers cracked through the tilted ground like it was made of paper as he squeezed hard on the earth.","’i refuse to die just like this!’","The fusion process continued.","85%... 90%... 95%.","Dexter’s vision faded and turned blurry as the edges of his consciousness dissolved into white static.","He could feel the last threads of his awareness slipping through his fingers like sand.","’ Hold on! Hold on! Hold on!’","Dexter roared like a beast to himself!","[Fusion Progress: 99%]","The world suddenly went blank.","Everything, including the pain, the heat, and the trembling body, stopped as it all went silent.","Then—","[Fusion Completed: 100%]","BOOM.","A shockwave of abyssal violet fire erupted from Dexter’s body, scorching the ground black","The walls cracked, windows shattered outward, sending glass fragments into the night. The ceiling above him was also charred and burnt.","At that moment, Dexter collapsed to the ground, unconscious.","His body lay motionless on the scorched floor, surrounded by a faint aura of deep violet flame that flickered and then faded into nothing.","•—•—•","Beep. Beep. Beep.","The shrill, electronic tone cut through the fog of unconsciousness like a knife.","Dexter’s eyes fluttered open. And saw it was the alarm he had set it to remind him to take Mira to the bathroom before dinner.","He groaned as he felt every muscle in his body felt like it had been run through a meat grinder. His joints ached. His skin tingled with residual heat.","He pushed himself up slowly, blinking against the dim light of his bedroom. Then he looked down.","His clothes were gone and burned away entirely, as though they weren’t there in the first place, as he stood there completely naked.","But that wasn’t what made him stare.","His entire body was covered in a thick, black, foul-smelling goo.","It coated his skin from head to toe, including his face.","But the worst of it was that it was freaking horrible.","The stench was indescribable. It was the concentrated essence of every impurity, toxin, and accumulated waste product that had been locked inside his body for years—purged in a single day.","Dexter lifted his hand and watched the black sludge drip slowly from his fingers, landing on the scorched floorboards with a wet splat.","\"...Gross.\"","He stood up unsteadily like Mia Khalifa does most of the time.","His nose wrinkled in disgust as he felt his body trembling in irritation.","’ So freaking disgusting!’","Suddenly, he felt something new within his body. It was similar to suddenly realizing you’ve grown a tail. He knew it was the Abyssal Emperor Flames","He paused as he looked at his hands, then he closed his eyes for a moment.","Suddenly, a thin tendril of deep violet flame materialized above his palm.","It was incredibly beautiful. It had a violet core and two layers of white and gold at the edge.","The Abyssal Emperor Flame, the 6th Heavenly Flame.","And somewhere in the backyard, deep inside Selene’s broken body, the Eternal Winter Ice trembled.","Dexter extinguished the flame and headed for the shower. He couldn’t handle the gooey substance all over his body.","•••","The grime coating his body was thick and stubborn.","He grabbed a fresh bar of soap and desperately washed his body as the water gushing down his body changed to a deep black and crimson color.","By the time he was done an hour had gone by.","He had washed himself 4 times before the water turned clear.","As he rinsed the last traces of sludge from his hair, he happened to glance up at the small, foggy mirror mounted in the shower stall.","Dexter immediately did a double-take as he stared at the stranger in the mirror.","’Who’s that?’","Dexter wasn’t the type of person that looked in the mirror.","’ Wait, is that... me?’","He already knew how ordinary he was, so he didn’t need the everyday reminder of the fact.","He had always showered every morning and never bothered to check his appearance because of how busy he was with himself and the girls.","It had been months, possibly two months or more since he had last properly looked at his own face.","And right now, the face staring back at him from the foggy glass was not the face he remembered.","Dexter had never considered himself ugly, but he was quite ordinary even more so amongst ordinary people.","His chin had been meaty, his cheeks round and his head not a perfect symmetry.","Years of cheap alcohol during his time at the Ashford estate had added an extra puffiness to his face, making him look tired and slightly bloated","The only thing remotely distinctive about him had been his hair.","He kept it long, because he couldn’t afford salon visits.","In the Ashford estate, he had been paid a servant’s wage. Haircuts were an unnecessary expense.","He could simply cut his hair with a pair of scissors whenever there was a chance.","Even after leaving the Ashfords and coming into money, he had simply forgotten about his hair, and he usually tied it back in a loose ponytail or let it hang loose depending on his mood.","But the face in the mirror..."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124 | Lord Have Mercy & Strange Dinner","paragraphs":["But the face in the mirror... was handsome?","His jaw has actually become chiseled. The soft, rounded edges of his former face was gone, replaced by sharp, angular lines that looked like they were carved out from stones!","His cheekbones looked nice too and the baby fat was completely gone without a single trace left.","And his eyes were still their normal brown, however from certain angle, they seemed dark red instead.","Dexter was stunned and he subconsciously leaned closer to the mirror, his breath fogging the glass further as he glanced at the stranger in the mirror.","’ What the actual hell?’","He could barely recognize himself!","His brows scrunched in disbelief when his eyes suddenly caught sight of his stomach.","He looked down at his body and was faced with a perfect grid six packs. He hadn’t even hardened his muscles yet but they were there as though he was born with it. And it wasn’t just 6 packs but seemed more like 10 packs.","He looked further down and his eyes widened.","’ Lord have mercy.’","Dexter speechlessly removed his gaze and focused on the golden markings on his arms and neck.","They looked like tattoos, covering his chest, neck, arms and shoulders.","’Seems like the merging did more than create another bloodline.’","He frowned as he gazed at the tattoo around his skin","The merging of the Emperor Void Flame, The Golden Flame along with his Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline must have imprinted these marks onto his body as a byproduct of the union divine and demonic energy permanently branding his flesh.","’Sigh. Mira will certainly enjoy mocking me if she saw this.’","He could already imagine the conversation.","Mira: \"Hehe. Anything to look handsome right?\"","Selene: \"...\"","Lyra: \"Are there more pastries?\"","Dexter groaned internally. How was he to explain the sudden emergence of tattoo overnight. But he felt like he might be overreacting, the girls might not even care about it.","At that moment, the golden markings k. His body started to fade.","Within seconds, the runes had retreated entirely beneath the surface of his skin, as though they had never existed.","Dexter raised an eyebrow but shrugged.","\"I’m definitely not complaining.\"","He turned off the shower, dried himself, and returned to his bedroom.","Dexter dressed in a dark t-shirt and joggers as he glanced at the clock.","’One hour behind schedule.’","He should have started cooking an hour ago.","***","Dexter entered the kitchen and assessed his options. He briefly considered skipping a proper meal and simply serving tea with the Celestial Moon Pastries. It would be quick, easy, and the pastries’ cultivation-boosting effects would benefit the girls during their midnight meditation.","But he shook his head. The girls were still thin, they needed a proper meal to end the day.","The question was what should he cook.","Dexter stood before the refrigerator, contemplating.","He pulled out vegetables, herbs, eggs, spices, fruits, and a thick cut of steak from the market.","Nothing extravagant.","He tied on his apron, activated his newly awakened Abyssal Emperor Flame, and began cooking with the Type II pot.","Even with ordinary ingredients, his Great Grandmaster Foodsmith skills transformed them into culinary masterpieces.","His control over the crimson flames was even more astonishing. At his command, they danced through the air, weaving into lifelike dragons, phoenixes, and blooming flowers before gently enveloping the ingredients without burning them.","Forty minutes later, a sumptuous feast sat on the table; a perfectly flame-seared herb steak accompanied by butter-glazed vegetables, a fluffy herb omelet, and a vibrant fruit medley, all infused with rich spiritual energy.","[Ding! Congratulations! You have successfully prepared a Grade-Two Spiritual Meal!]","[Effects:]","• Recovers physical stamina and soothes muscle fatigue.","• Increases cultivation speed by 30% for four hours.","•Increased libido by 200%","• Reduces friction during breakthroughs, making it easier to advance from one level to another.","• Calms the nervous system and promotes deep, restorative sleep.","Dexter nodded in satisfaction. A Grade-Two meal from ordinary grocery store ingredients.","It seemed like he didn’t actually read through the effect.","He set the dining table: four bowls, four spoons, four cups of tea, arranged them neatly and turned toward the living room to call the girls—","Lyra was already standing at the kitchen entrance, a fork and knife clutched in each hand as her dark eyes locked in the food, almost drooling.","Dexter chuckled. \"You could have helped me set the table, you know.\"","Lyra’s cheeks flushed slightly but she didn’t put down the fork. Dexter sighed as he shook his head.","Selene was still in the backyard so he went to the backyard and found her sitting cross-legged beneath the overhang with hee eyes closed as she cultivated.","The rain had stopped and the sky was clear as the moonlight illuminated her silver hair, making her look like a goddess who had just descended to the mortal world.","She looked incredibly peaceful and also extremely beautiful. Dexter immediately inhaled sharply, calming himself as he called out softly.","\"Selene, dinner is ready.\"","Her ears trembled as the vibration called out everything around her.","She opened her eyes, nodded, and stood up gracefully. She walked toward him without hesitation, her feet was bare but she didn’t seem cold as she entered the kitchen and took her usual spot beside Lyra.","Her hand found the spoon on the table without fumbling as her fingers easily wrapped around it the handle.","Mira was still sound asleep in the bedroom so rather than wake her up, Dexter decided to save her portion.","He placed her covered plate inside the microwave for whenever she woke up.","At the dinner table, Lyra was practically inhaling her food.","Selene ate quietly beside her with her eyes closed.","’Hm?’","Dexter felt like he was being watched. He looked at Lyra but she was drinking her food and Selene eyes was closed as she also focused on her meal.","However, Dexter couldn’t shake the feeling of being watched. Whicj only left one person, Selene. She doesn’t rely on her eyes but her ears.","Dexter could feel she was focusing entirely on him, mapping his body and the mana radiating from him with pinpoint precision.","He glanced up at her, but Selene was expressionless as she continued eating.","Dexter frowned slightly but shrugged it off.","Maybe she wanted something but didn’t know how to ask, or maybe she was waiting for Lyra to leave. He decided not to press the issue.","A few minutes later, Lyra scraped her bowl clean. She let out a satisfied sigh with cheeks flushed as she drank two glass full of water. Her massive chest rising and falling at the movement.","’ Good night,’ her soft, melodic voice echoed in everyone’s mind.","\"Good night, Lyra,\" Dexter smiled.","Lyra stood up and padded silently down the hallway to the bedroom, leaving Dexter and Selene alone at the table.","The moment Lyra left, the intensity of Selene’s focus instantly doubled.","Unable to hold it in any longer, Dexter set down his spoon and asked, \"Selene, do you need something?\"","Selene froze for a moment. She slowly shook her head, but then hesitated, and slowly nodded.","\"Did you... do something?\" she asked quietly.","Dexter frowned, confused. \"What do you mean?\""]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125 | Mira & Dexter Almost...","paragraphs":["\"What happened to you?\" she asked quietly.","Dexter frowned, confused. \"What do you mean?\"","Selene’s brows slightly furrowed. \"I meant... Did something happen to you?\"","Dexter blinked, suddenly remembering that he had broken through to the seventh stage of the Superhuman Realm earlier that evening. He smiled, trying to play it off. \"Oh, I just had a breakthrough. That’s probably what you’re feeling. It’s normal for your senses to pick up a shift in mana when someone advances.\"","Selene remained silent for a long moment as she pondered but then, she slowly shook her head.","\"No, that’s not it,\" she said firmly. \"What did you do?\"","Dexter’s smile faded. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Previously, you were like a burning flame. But right now... all I can see is a... wildfire. Your aura has changed. It’s still calm but is extremely aggressive. Did you take any strength enhancing drug? You should know not to take those things.","Selene said with a frown as she warned him.","Dexter was stunned.","He hadn’t expected Selene’s senses to be so perceptive that she could actually see the shift in his bloodline.","He tried thinking of a reply but couldn’t come up with a plausible response.","Finally, he simply shrugged as he said casually.","\"Maybe my body is just evolving and getting used to the changes. That happens sometimes when you break through.\"","He then changed the subject. \"You should go inside and rest. Afterall, you’ve been cultivating all day. Even if your body is willing, your mind needs to rest.\"","He didn’t wait for her to respond as he stood up, gathered the plates, and took them to the sink. The sound of running water and clinking sound of the plates filled the silence.","Even with his back turned, he could still feel Selene’s focus on him. She didn’t remained there for about ten minutes, before she eventually stood up and quietly retreated to the bedroom to join Lyra.","’Are all my wives this scary? Sigh, Lyra is still the only cute one.’","Dexter sighed in relief, dried his hands, undid his apron, and went to the living room.","He flipped his palm and a Matrix core appeared in his palm. It was the Tier 6 Guardian Matrix Formation.","He took almost an hour to set the formation up and eventually he got it and then activated it.","Another invincible barrier appeared around the Ashford home, making two protective barrier.","At this rate, even a Peak Transcendent would have difficulty entering the Ashford compound.","Satisfied, he went back to his room to resume cultivating.","***","3’o clock AM.","The bungalow was silent but there was a few insect noises occasionally breaking the quiet.","Inside his room, Dexter sat cross-legged on his bed, quietly cultivating as mana surged directly into inner universe, filling up his 7th star nodes.","Suddenly, his eyes snapped open.","\"Squeak...\"","His enhanced hearing immediately picked up the faint sound and it was coming from the hallway.","Mira.","Dexter smiled helplessly.","She was trying her best to move quietly, but the wheelchair she used was old. Every movement of its worn wheels produced an unmistakable squeaking sound. In the silence of midnight, it was impossible to hide.","He already knew what she was doing.","Without making a sound, Dexter stood up and stepped out of his room.","Sure enough, Mira was slowly making her way toward the kitchen. Using her Spectral Arms, she carefully pushed the wheelchair forward, moving much more skillfully than she had a few days ago.","Hearing the bedroom door open, Mira turned her neck around.","Their eyes met.","She blinked once, her face expressionless, then simply turned away and continued toward the kitchen as if she hadn’t seen him.","Dexter couldn’t help but chuckle.","Without saying a word, he walked behind her and gently took hold of the wheelchair handles.","Mira didn’t protest.","Silence accompanied them as Dexter slowly pushed her into the dining room.","He stopped beside the table and positioned her where she usually sat.","Then he walked into the kitchen.","He reheated the food he had prepared earlier, arranged it neatly on a plate, placed a spoon beside it, and carried everything back.","He gently placed the meal before her.","\"...Thank you,\" Mira muttered quietly.","One of her Spectral Arm picked up the spoon as she started to feed herself.","Compared to before, her movements were noticeably smoother. She no longer struggled with every motion, and feeding herself had become much faster.","Dexter watched quietly.","After taking several bites, Mira noticed he was still standing there.","She frowned.","\"What? Is it fun watching the crippled girl struggle to eat? You can go back to sleep now. Thank you for your help.\"","Dexter suppressed his chuckle and shrugged. \"I still have to wash the dishes.\"","He pointed toward the sink.","\"If dirty plates are left overnight, they’ll attract cockroaches and other insects.\"","Then he looked at her with an innocent smile.","\"You don’t want a cockroach wandering into your room, do you?\"","Mira’s expression immediately changed.","She glared at him, knowing fully well he was implying something.","\"Do you think I’m scared of a mere cockroach?\" she shot back.","Dexter fought back a grin. I’m just saying...\"","He leaned slightly closer.","\"So if you suddenly found one crawling onto your bed...\"","\"...or hiding underneath your pillow, you wouldn’t be scared, right?\"","Mira glared at him.","\"You better not have any stupid ideas. I’m warning you.\"","Dexter immediately raised both hands in surrender.","\"Relax. I was joking.\"","Mira let out an annoyed huff before returning to her meal.","Knowing she would be uncomfortable with him standing there watching her, Dexter went back to his room as he resumed cultivating.","Even with his eyes closed, his enhanced hearing remained focused on the dining room.","The faint clinking of the spoon against the ceramic plate continued for several minutes.","Eventually, there was silence.","Dexter smiled.","He stood and walked back into the dining room almost immediately.","Seeing him appear almost instantaneously, Mira chuckled. \"You will make a perfect stalker, you pervert.\"","Dexter burst into laughter.","The sound echoed throughout the otherwise quiet bungalow.","Mira simply sighed and shook her head.","\"Hmph.\"","Still smiling, Dexter wheeled her back toward the bedroom.","Once inside, he locked the wheelchair before carefully sliding one arm beneath her knees and the other around her back.","He lifted her effortlessly.","Mira body uncontrollably leaned against him.","As he carried her toward the bed, the top of her head rested lightly against his chest.","Then—","Her lips accidentally brushed against the side of his neck.","At that exact moment, Dexter’s entire body stiffened and his heart actually skipped a beat!","Almost unconsciously, he lowered his gaze but at that exact moment, Mira looked up at him, their faces 3 inches away from each other and their lips just 3 centimeters away from each other!","Both of them stiffened as their breathing froze as they gazed into each others eyes, neither of them spoke.","Time itself seemed to slow.","Dexter found himself lowering his gaze as he stared ar her her soft, rosy lips.","For a brief, dangerous moment...","An overwhelming urge he couldn’t control possessed him. And at that moment, his one true wish at that moment was to consume those sumptuous lips and kiss her deeply.","The temptation came so suddenly that it caught him completely off guard.","Just as he leaned a fraction of a centimeter, the Serenity Band around his wrist emitted a faint calming warmth.","Instantly, a cool sensation washed over Dexter’s body and the hotness he was feeling calmed down. helping him regain control before he could do anything stupid.","He slowly looked away.","Mira’s cheeks had already turned a delicate shade of red and she hadn’t said a single word.","Dexter pretended as though what he had almost done wasn’t him.","He carefully laid her onto the bed, adjusted the pillow beneath her head, and gently pulled the duvet over her body.","\"...Goodnight,\" he said, his voice husky.","Without waiting for a response, Dexter turned and quickly left the room."]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126 | Don’t Go!","paragraphs":["The next morning, Dexter woke up early, freshened up, and went through his routine. He took care of Mira, and both of them pretended as though the midnight event didn’t happen as Dexter finished up with her, dressing her up in a cloth she liked.","He had figured out the root of the problem. One of the herbs he used to make dinner last night gave a slight unwanted effect, which was definitely the reason for everything.","He sighed in relief and headed to the kitchen to cook breakfast.","The four of them were seated at the dining table, eating in comfortable silence, when it happened.","’Ding! Ding! Ding!’","Dexter’s phone suddenly erupted with a loud, blaring alarm—a sound he had never heard before.","Startled, he pulled the device from his pocket and stared at the screen. A bright red banner flashed across the display.","[EMERGENCY ALERT]","[F-Rank Hero: Dexter Ashford]","[Please rush to this location immediately to assist!]","[A Gate has appeared and a Monster Outbreak Detected]","[Estimated Gate: F-Rank to E-Rank]","[Based on your current location, you are the closest registered hero. Estimated arrival time: Under 3 minutes.]","[Please hurry! Every second wasted could cost a civilian life!]","Dexter’s eyes widened. It hadn’t even been three days since he had registered at the Hero Association, and he was already being dispatched to a monster outbreak.","Just as Dexter was about to push his chair back, a cold voice cut through the morning air.","\"Don’t.\"","Dexter was startled as he looked up in surprise. He could see Selene glaring at his phone, her white eyes staring at him with furrowed brows.","\"You’re not going.\"","This time, Mira spoke in a firm tone as she glared at the phone in his hand.","Dexter scratched the back of his head as he frowned. He was a registered hero now, and a part of the Hero Association.","He received a monthly stipend, and that came with obligations. He couldn’t simply ignore an emergency dispatch. Worse, the alert had explicitly stated that every second wasted could cost a civilian life.","If the Association tracked his GPS, they would know he had received the alert and chosen not to respond.","He glanced sideways and saw Lyra was also glaring at his phone.","The three girls’ faces had turned cold by now.","’It seems the trauma from the dungeon still haunts all three of them.’","Anything related to monsters, outbreaks, or dungeons triggered a deep, visceral fear that Dexter understood completely.","But he needed kills, not just for the Asura Slaughter Demon Body, but to upgrade the investment multiplier from 100x to 1,000x.","Right now. He needed 51 more kills to hit the 1,000x milestone for that; he would need to head into dungeons, go for more monster outbreaks, not just for the system but also for the girls.","If he wanted to find a cure for them, he would head into Dungeons more often than they would be comfortable with. As for the civilians, Dexter wasn’t too keen on saving them.","But he had just reconciled with Mira, if he left now, all of that progress might crumble and Selene and Lyra might just hate him for it.","Dexter’s brows tightened even further","Mira watched the struggle play across his face. The conflict in his eyes was unmistakable","As she gazed at him, her furrowed brows started to ease, and her gaze eventually softened. Because Mira understood something in that moment, something that cut through her fear and her trauma and her selfish desire to keep him safe within arm’s reach.","Dexter was a good person by nature.","If he weren’t, he would never accept taking care of a cripple, but he took on three instead.","If he wasn’t a good person, he could have ignored them, brought in several women into their home, or even had other girls on the side.","But he hasn’t done that. He has stuck with them, made sure they didn’t starve or lack anything, endured their insults, absorbed their pain, and never once complained.","He had pushed a wheelchair into the rain just to make her smile, spent hundreds of thousands of dollars or even millions not because he had to, but because he wanted to.","If she told him not to go, if she forced him to sit here while people died while he might listen, he would have to suppress that good part of himself that needed to save innocent lives.","And in doing so, she would be forcing him to go against his nature, changing him, twisting his good heart into something else until eventually he might just stop caring entirely.","Mira sighed internally, and her face shifted as it went from being fierce to indifferent.","\"Just go if you want to go,\" she said flatly.","Dexter, still locked in his internal debate, was stunned as he turned toward her.","Lyra and Selene’s eyes widened as they turned towards Selene in surprise.","Mira turned her head away, refusing to meet his eyes. \"When did you start listening to us?\"","\"Since you really want to go, just go.\"","Her gaze suddenly turned cold as she glared at him. \"If you like, get yourself killed and don’t come back. I am going to haunt your soul.\"","Dexter stared at her, stunned. ’She’s really serious.’","Mira, feeling the intensity of his gaze, rolled her eyes. Two spectral arms materialized behind her, one of them scooping up a spoonful of rice as she ignored him and continued eating.","Lyra and Selene’s brows were still furrowed. Selene’s fists were clenched, her nails almost digging into her palm.","Dexter smiled gently. \"Don’t worry. I promise to come back.\" He paused, a hint of playfulness entering his voice.","\"As you three keep pointing out, I apparently have a mysterious backing. So I’ll be fine.\"","Mira’s eyes snapped to him. \"So you admit it,\" she said, her voice sharp. \"You admit having a mysterious backing.\"","Dexter shrugged innocently. \"I never said I did. I never said I didn’t.\"","Mira clicked her tongue and rolled her eyes, returning to her meal.","Dexter smiled as he turned to Selene and Lyra. But Lyra had resumed eating while Selene was staring at Mira with her white eyes.","Seemingly to have gotten their permission, he pushed back from the table and disappeared into his bedroom.","In under ten seconds, he had pulled a clean shirt over his wife-beater singlet, grabbed his shoes, and was at the front door.","He turned back to the girls. \"I promise I will be back. Don’t open the door for anyone.\"","Mira snorted in irritation. \"Not funny.\"","Dexter chuckled and waved goodbye, opened the door, and stepped out. The door closed behind him with a soft click.","•—•—•","The dining room fell silent.","Then Lyra and Selene’s gaze snapped toward Mira, their expressions hardening.","’Why did you do that?’","Lyra’s telepathic voice echoed inside Mira’s mind, and for the first time, the soft, melodic tone had turned cold. Dangerously cold.","Selene’s face was equally frigid. Her sightless eyes were narrowed, her jaw tight. \"You shouldn’t have told him to go,\" she said quietly. \"After what happened to us, monster outbreaks and dungeons should be the one thing we prevent him from walking into. Yet you let him go.\"","Mira finished chewing her bite, swallowed calmly, and set down her spoon.","\"You two are also his wives,\" she replied evenly. \"You could have told him to stay, and he would have listened.\"","Lyra rolled her eyes so hard it was almost audible.","Selene indifferently spoke. \"We all know you are closer to him than either of us,\" she said. \"He wouldn’t have listened to us. But if you had said something, regardless, he would have stayed. Just like he always does when it matters to you.\"","Mira blinked, and she found herself momentarily caught off guard. She glanced between the two girls, reading their expressions. Her eyes widened slightly in sudden realization.","A small smile crept across Mira’s lips. \"Are you two... actually jealous?\"","Lyra’s eyes blinked rapidly, and a slight flush crept up her neck to her cheeks. She immediately ate her last spoon and stood up, then announced into their minds: ’I’m done.’","She practically fled the dining room, leaving Mira and Selene alone at the table.","Selene, however, didn’t back down. She continued glaring at Mira without blinking, and her chin tilted upward in defiance.","Mira’s smirk widened. \"Since you two are jealous, that means you are beginning to like him,\" she said casually. \"Since you like him, why don’t you just tell him? I’m pretty sure it would make his day—two pretty girls confessing their feelings to him.\"","The silence that followed was deafening.","Selene’s lips pressed together tightly, but she didn’t flinch. Her pale, sightless eyes accurately locked on Mira’s eyes.","Mira’s smirk shifted into something more dangerous. She tilted her head slightly. \"What? Do you truly want to fight for his attention with me?\"","There was silence at first, but then Selene replied in a cold and indifferent tone. \"I can try.\"","Mira’s smile widened further and then suddenly broke into a genuine, incredulous laugh. \"Are we really about to quarrel because of a man?\" She shook her head, her red hair swaying in disbelief. \"I’m really fighting about a man.\"","Selene remained unblinking, unyielding, and she was dead serious.","Mira’s laughter faded. She studied Selene’s face for a long moment, searching for any trace of jest but there was non!","Mira frowned but then shrugged. \"Fine. You can have him.\"","Selene held her gaze for three more seconds. Then, slowly, she lowered her head and resumed eating her breakfast in silence.","Mira’s brows remained furrowed, her eyes lingering on Selene for a few more seconds before she finally looked away."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127 | Monster Outbreak","paragraphs":["Dexter was completely unaware of the drama back at home.","He was behind the wheel of his Vanguard V4, weaving through morning traffic at dangerous speeds.","He couldn’t use the Type-6 Aegis Skybreaker as it was still daytime, and pulling a combat-grade flying SUV out of thin air in broad daylight would raise too many questions.","So the ordinary-looking armored SUV would have to do.","The GPS on his phone displayed the pinned location. He was already two minutes behind schedule thanks to the argument at the breakfast table. The Vanguard V4’s engine roared as he floored the accelerator.","In under four minutes, he crossed into the next district.","The moment he arrived, chaos greeted him.","The street was in pandemonium.","The bustling market district had become a living nightmare.","People ran through the streets with faces twisted in absolute terror, their desperate screams echoing from every direction.","\"Run!\"","\"It’s coming!\"","\"Help! Somebody help!\"","Children cried as parents dragged them through the streets. Some stumbled and fell, only to be yanked back to their feet before the stampede swallowed them.","Cars had collided with one another in desperate attempts to escape. Twisted metal blocked entire intersections as horns blared endlessly, some vehicles still idling with their doors hanging wide open.","It was obvious their owners had abandoned them in blind panic.","A truck slammed into a traffic light with a deafening crash.","Glass exploded across the road.","Another vehicle flipped onto its side after swerving to avoid something charging through the smoke.","\"BOOM!\"","An explosion erupted somewhere down the street.","The shockwave rattled nearby buildings as black smoke billowed into the morning sky.","The air was a symphony of horror.","Screams.","Gunfire.","Crunching metal.","Shattering glass.","And above it all...","Deep, loud roars that no normal creature on earth should have been capable of producing.","The monstrous cries reverberated through the district, making even the bravest civilians freeze in fear before instinct forced them to run once more.","Dexter parked the Vanguard V4 and stepped out.","The moment his boots touched the pavement, recognition flashed through his eyes.","This was the market district.","The very place where he had bought groceries and supplies during his first week after moving into the bungalow.","Only days ago it had been lively and crowded.","Now, It looked like a battlefield.","Storefronts had been ripped open as though struck by a missile.","Market stalls had been reduced to splintered wood scattered across the streets.","Fresh vegetables and fruits lay crushed beneath countless footprints, their juices mixing with shattered glass, spent shell casings, and pools of fresh blood.","A delivery truck had crashed straight through the front of a pharmacy, its engine still sputtering while flames sparked beneath the hood of the vehicle.","At the daw end of a store, a woman knelt beside a motionless man, desperately shaking his shoulders while sobbing uncontrollably.","\"Husband, wake up... please... please wake up...\"","\"Ahhhhh!!!\"","Nearby, another civilian was dragged screaming into an alley.","His cries lasted only a few seconds before ending in a sickening crunch.","There was silence, then a wet tearing sound reverberated.","The people who witnessed it screamed even louder and fled in every direction.","At the center of the devastation, reality itself had been torn apart.","A massive dimensional gate floated several meters above the ground, crackling with unstable energy.","The space around it distorted continuously, as if the world itself were struggling to heal the wound.","And from that rip in reality, monsters surged in like a swarm, leaping and clawing their way out of the gate as they shoved and climbs over one another in their eagerness to reach the fleeing civilians.","The creatures roared with savage excitement the instant they caught sight of prey.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","\"Fiend-Class monsters...\"","He recognized them immediately.","Four-Armed Goblins.","A far deadlier evolution of ordinary goblins.","Unlike their smaller cousins, these creatures stood as tall as fully grown adults, with several towering well over two meters.","Their sickly green-gray skin stretched over powerful, corded muscles that rippled with frightening strength.","Elongated snouts jutted forward, lined with rows of jagged yellow fangs slick with saliva.","Small bloodshot eyes burned with animalistic hunger.","Long, pointed ears twitched constantly as they searched for the next terrified victim.","Some possessed only two muscular arms.","Others had four.","The greater the number of arms, the stronger the goblin.","The Four-Arm goblins have two massive arms protruding normally from their shoulders, while another pair sprouted from behind their shoulder blades, giving them a grotesque, spider-like silhouette.","Each arm moved independently.","One could wield crude weapons while the others clawed, grabbed, or tore apart anything within reach.","Against ordinary civilians, they were living, breathing nightmares.","Dexter assessed their strength.","’Level 3 to Level 12.’","And they are all Fiend Class. Most F-rank heroes, would be cautious and wait for back up.","But Dexter wasn’t most people.","At that split second, a car swerved wildly, trying to bypass a goblin.","The creature’s four arms swung simultaneously, catching the vehicle’s side panel.","\"Bang!\"","The car spun sideways as it slammed into a building nearby.","The driver crawled out, bleeding from the head, as he stumbled away on foot, panicking.","Not far from him, a young couple were running together, as they fled from a four-armed goblin chasing after them.","The Four-arm Goblin chased after them. It’s speed fast as its mouth stretched wide in a horrifying grin.","The man’s expression changed. Them all of a sudden, he grabbed the woman by the side and shoved her backwards.","The woman was stunned and she stumbled backward by the force, falling tk the ground as her head hit a nearby car.","\"S-Simon!? What are you doing!? Help me!!!\"","She wasn’t Valentin finish her sentence when the goblin descended on her.","The boyfriend didn’t look back but ran faster.","Although it took a while to explain m, everything happened in a split second.","With Dexter’s hearing, he could map out everything in a 300 meter radius and it would be visible to him as though he was there, rendering a 3d image of the surroundings to him.","Dexter raised an eyebrow. A flicker of disgust crossed his face, but he didn’t waste time judging. He was already moving.","[Flame Burst Step]"]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128 | Monster Outbreak 2","paragraphs":["\"Flame Burst Step!\"","The world blurred as heat exploded beneath his feet.","His body rocketed forward, crossing thirty meters in a fraction of a second as he materialized beside the four-armed goblin just as its jaws unhinged and its mouth opened wide enough to swallow the young woman’s entire head.","The Macro Splicing Saber appeared in his hands as he called it out from the storage ring.","\"Squelch!\"","Dexter easily drove the blade through the back of the goblin’s skull.","The black steel tore through its skull and its brain before erupting from the creature’s open mouth in a shower of thick, green blood pouring down on the woman’s face, nose and mouth.","The goblin’s body stiffened, and it instantly went limp as it collapsed forward, crashing to the ground inches from the young woman’s body.","As the green blood splattered across the woman’s body, she shrieked even more as though the stain was worse than death!","\"AAAAAAHHH!\" \"AAAAAHHH!\"","\"Shut up,\" Dexter growled, his voice cutting through her panic like a blade. \"Find a safe place and hide. Now.\"","The woman’s mouth snapped shut. She opened her eyes through the green gore on her face and saw Dexter standing above her.","She sniffed hard as tears streamed down her face. She quickly scrambled to her feet. \"Th-thank you,\" she stuttered, her body shaking violently. \"Thank you, I—\"","Dexter immediately ignored her as he activated Flame Burst Step, blasting towards the nearby Goblin.","[Slaughter Extraction System: Kill Count — 1/51]","The notification registered in the back of his mind, but Dexter barely noticed. He was already moving.","He had noticed something different when he activated the bloodline technique.","It was easier to use, and he felt like he could use it way longer than he used to.","Instead of a 500% speed increase for two seconds, he could actually control and sustain the blast of energy beneath his feet to not just be a single violent explosion but a steady stream of explosions.","His body blurred forward as his head blasted behind him, and this time, the bloodline skill didn’t cancel after five seconds.","With his upgraded bloodline, he felt like he could sustain it for nearly a minute before his body began to show strain. And if he pushed himself, he could probably extend it further.","’ This is new,’ he thought, a grim smile touching his lips as he rocketed toward his next target.","The second goblin was attacking a man inside his store.","\"Graaa!\"","The goblin growled as it cornered the store owner behind its own counter, its four arms reaching over the top, clawing at the man who was desperately trying to hold it back with a baseball bat.","Dexter’s eyes locked onto the shopkeeper’s face and he immediately recognized him.","The shopkeeper was the same man who had sold him groceries during his first week at the bungalow.","The same man who had doubled the price of pork just because he heard a rumor on the internet.","Dexter’s gaze turned dark, and he smirked. ’","’ Let him suffer a bit.’","Dexter turned away and moved to save someone else.","As he turned around, the goblin smashed the counter, grabbed the man before tossing him across his own store like a rag doll.","\"Bang!\"","The man crashed into a wall, slid down, and tried to crawl away.","\"Help! Help! Somebody help me!!!\"","He tried to fight back, but the hiblkn sneered as it smacked him sideways into a rack of canned goods.","Cans exploded in all directions. The trader spat blood as his face bled with blood and pure terror.","At this moment, Dexter appeared before another Goblin.","It was a level 10 Goblin, and it had gripped the neck of a woman tightly, squeezing the life out of her as it watched with relish.","\"Whoosh!\"","The air shook as the goblin quickly reacted and punched at the space beside it.","\"Bang!\"","Shockwaves exploded in a circular pattern as the Dexter caught the punch with his palm.","\"Whoosh!\"","A dark light glinted and blood splattered in the air as Dexter’s blade easily sliced a long blood line through the Monster’s skull.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","The woman dropped to the ground with a flushed face as she wanted to thank Dexter, but he was long gone.","Dexter’s speed was so fast he appeared behind another Goblin.","\"Roooar!\"","The goblin was roaring and angry as it clawed at a locked car door.","His Type-3 blade easily cut through its skin without hesitation.","At this moment, the trader’s screams had turned faint as though he had given up.","Dexter sighed.","’ Fine .’","He activated Flame Burst Step and closed the distance in an instant.","The Macro Splicing Saber swept upward in a clean, horizontal arc. The goblin’s head separated from its shoulders with surgical precision, the creature’s four arms still reaching for the shopkeeper as its body crumpled to the floor.","Green blood fountained from the severed neck, splattering the shelves of canned goods behind it.","The shopkeeper screamed as he scrambled on the ground. He looked up through the gore and debris, and saw Dexter standing over the goblin’s twitching corpse.","\"D-Dexter?\" the man stammered, his face pale with shock. \"You’re—you’re the—\"","Dexter glared at the trader indifferently as he turned to leave.","[Slaughter Extraction System: Kill Count — 4/51]","[Extracted: +2 Strength, +1 Agility]","\"W-who’s going to pay for the damages?\"","Dexter wanted to turn back and choke the man to death but he inhaled deeply and blurred out of the man’s store.","Flames erupted behind him as it burnt a few nearby items.","\"Hey! What the hell!?\"","The trader shouted after Dexter.","A few goblins actually carried crude weapons like clubs, sharpened bones or stone spears.","Dexter was like a grinding machine; he easily cut through them like a scythe through wheat.","***","As he drew nearer to the center of the district, his ears flickered as he heard the sounds of two children crying.","He changed direction immediately, his body cutting through the chaos like a missile as he saw two kids standing in the middle of the road.","They were quite young. The older one was perhaps 9 years old and the younger one, no more than 3 years old.","The 9-year-old had his arms wrapped tightly around his toddler brother, as they crouched in the middle of the wrecked street.","\"Mom!\" \"Mom!\"","The sound of their crying carried through the market district. And it immediately attracted attention.","A massive goblin emerged from the smoke as it shot towards them like a missile.","’Level 12 Fiend Class Monster!’"]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129 | Cold Hearted Hero","paragraphs":["Dexter’s face changed.","\"Level 12, Fiend Class Monster.\"","Six levels higher than Dexter.","This particular Goblin was different. It was much bigger than the others as it stood nearly two meters tall with a large crude hammer in its massive arm.","And its eyes weren’t particularly bloodshot like the rest, but it had a tinge of intelligence in them.","The goblin’s nostrils flared as it caught the children’s scent. The moment its eyes landed on them, its mouth stretched into a grin as thick saliva dripped from its jaws.","It stepped forward and appeared half a meter away from them as it stretched three of its four arms at the kids.","One of its hands stroked the kid’s hair as if fascinated by the brown hair of the kid.","Its mouth watered, and the drool in its mouth increased. It had never had such fresh and tender meat before.","Before the invasion, the commander promised so much meat that they could never finish, but he didn’t expect to see such premium and fresh meat. Not to mention, there were two of them.","The older kid seemed to have felt the arm on its head, and it looked back.","\"Waaaaaaah!\"","The kid screamed, which caused the goblin to scream more as its mouth slowly spread open.","The air shimmered with heat as a dark saber flashed through the air in a large arc.","\"Whoosh!\"","The blade caught the goblin’s lower-right arm at the elbow, severing it cleanly as green blood sprayed in a wide arc.","However, it was able to react quickly, saving its three other arms from being severed.","\"ROOOOOOAR!\"","The goblin roared in pain as its severed arm flew in mid-air. The sound was so loud that the glass windows of the nearby vehicle and shops vibrated.","That was because, along with the roar, it had also activated its crowd control skill without hesitation.","It was so deep and powerful that the windows of nearby cars vibrated. But the roar wasn’t just sound. It was a technique.","[Intimidating Roar]","The sonic roar hit Dexter’s brain like a sledgehammer.","With his enhanced senses, he received more than double the effect!","The entire world blurred as his vision spun.","His thoughts scattered like leaves in a hurricane as an invisible, crushing pressure invaded his consciousness, trying to stun him.","\"Bang!\"","The Abyssal Emperor Flame erupted within his body as the violet fire blazed through his meridians, his blood, his very soul.","The divine-demonic flame didn’t just resist the mental intrusion; it incinerated it.","The two children weren’t as fortunate. The roar’s mental attack overwhelmed their young minds instantly as they collapsed to the ground.","Although Dexter managed to recover, he had been stunned for 0.2 seconds.","In this world, 0.2 seconds was more than enough time for one to die three times over.","\"Graaaa!\"","The goblin growled as it swung its hammer in a wide arc, slamming it directly against Dexter’s skull.","\"Whoosh!\"","Dexter managed to shift his head to the side as the hammer slammed directly to his shoulder.","\"BOOM!\"","A massive shockwave erupted from the point of impact as it radiated through the air like stone dropped into still water.","Every car within ten meters had its windows explode simultaneously as glass fragments showered the street like rain.","The pavement beneath Dexter’s feet instantly shattered as his body transmitted the force directly to the ground.","This was one of the benefits of Iron Body Stage, transmitting force easily without damaging the body!","Any normal level 7 Superhuman hero’s body would have shattered immediately, but Dexter was not just cultivating a 7th Tier body technique; the Slaughter Extraction System also extracts attributes from dead monsters, strengthening his body to a terrifying level!","Dexter’s brows furrowed slightly. \"That hurts.\"","The goblin’s eyes widened in panic, and it punched out with another fist.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter caught the fist with his left hand.","\"My turn.\"","\"Bang!\"","He instantly kicked out, and the entire body of the Goblin was sent flying like a bullet as it collided against the wall of a building.","It wasn’t even able to recover when Dexter appeared before it.","The Macro Splicing Saber swept upward in a single, devastating arc.","\"Whoosh!\"","The goblin tried to block it with its hammer, but it was too slow.","The saber swept upwards as it cleanly passed through the goblin’s body.","The goblin stood frozen there in disbelief.","Then a thin, crimson line appeared at the center of its body. The line spread slowly at first, then rapidly until it divided the goblin into two perfect halves.","The two pieces fell apart in opposite directions, hitting the ground with twin wet thuds.","[Kill Count — 17/51]","[Extracted: +5 Strength, +4 Agility, +3 Physique, +2 Mana]","Dexter didn’t pause to admire his work. He sheathed his blade, scooped both unconscious children from the ground, activated Flame Burst Step, and carried them to the nearest intact storefront.","He kicked the door open, gently laid them on the floor behind the counter, and checked their pulses.","Stable but unconscious, and they were breathing normally. The Intimidating Roar’s effect would wear off soon.","He stepped back outside and launched himself back into the chaos.","***","Dexter moved through the market like a rotor blade, his Flame Burst Step easily carrying him with bursts of speed as his blade slashed through one goblin after the other.","His kill count climbed steadily.","[Kill Count — 21/51]","[Kill Count — 22/51]","[Kill Count — 23/51]","Then, at the far end of the main street, he spotted another hero.","The hero was a tall man with broad shoulders. From his energy wave, he was a level 12 superhuman. He wielded a spear that crackled with blue mana.","Dexter immediately recognized the hero from TV as Bullet Spear.","A popular neighborhood E-rank hero loved by the masses and popular amongst the children for his fast spear attacks.","He is said to have cleared multiple F-rank dungeons and responded to multiple monster outbreaks, saving countless lives in the process.","Currently, Bullet Spear moved through the goblin ranks as he pierced through them with his spear, moving like a bullet.","Each strike found a vital point—throat, heart, spine. Goblins fell before him in rapid succession.","By Dexter’s estimate, his killing speed was impressively faster than Dexter’s simply because he wasn’t stopping to rescue civilians!","And that was the problem.","Unlike his hero title, Bullet Spear wasn’t saving anyone, he was using the civilians as bait to clear monsters and upgrade his rank!","Dexter coldly watched from fifty meters away as the spear-wielding hero engaged a group of four-armed goblins.","The creatures had been attacking a cluster of trapped civilians huddled inside an overturned bus.","Instead of drawing the goblins away from the civilians, Bullet Spear waited until the goblins were fully focused on their prey, killing them.","With their backs turned, it was then he struck, killing them from behind while they were distracted.","It was effective and efficient but incredibly cold-hearted.","Dexter found himself grudgingly impressed by the idea. But shook his head.","Bullet Spear was treating the outbreak like a hunting ground, and the civilians were nothing more than bait to lure his targets into vulnerable positions.","Dexter shook his head and continued his kills.","At that time, more heroes began to arrive with vehicles. One after the other. It was obvious that they too had received the alert.","Small groups of E-rank and F-rank heroes rushed in rapidly to help kill monsters and save civilians.","They fanned out through the district, engaging goblins and evacuating civilians.","It was at that moment that the sky suddenly changed."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130 | The Goblin King","paragraphs":["Then the sky changed.","\"Rumble!\"","The clouds parted with a resonant boom, and a figure descended from above, dropping through the atmosphere like a meteor, trailing streams of compressed air and crackling electrical energy.","\"Boom!\"","The figure landed at the center of the market square sending out a shockwave of wind and dust rippling outward. Every goblin within fifty meters was knocked off its feet.","Dexter shielded his eyes from the dust cloud and when it cleared, a woman stood at the center of the impact crater.","Long silver hair flowed behind her like a river of moonlight. A black combat coat with silver trim clung to her frame, moving in the wind like living shadow. On her chest, gleaming in the morning light, was an S-rank badge.","She was the woman he had seen at the Hero Association entrance. The one Rachel had pointed out. The rising star who had recently been promoted to S-rank after clearing her first S-rank dungeon.","Aurora.","The one with the sky manipulation talent.","Her gaze swept across the market as she observed everything going on.","Suddenly, she glanced upwards .","\"Boom!\"","She raised one hand and the space itself twisted.","A four-armed goblin that had been climbing a building nearby suddenly found the air around it warping.","The air compressed and slapped the wrapped around the creature’s body, sending it flying through the air directly toward Aurora.","The S-rank hero didn’t even blink. She extended her palm as the goblin’s body arrived, gently pressing her hand against its back.","\"Crumble!\"","The creature disintegrated.","The goblin’s body shattered into multiple pieces—arms, legs, torso, head—all separating cleanly as if the creature had been made of glass struck by a hammer. The fragments fell to the ground in a shower of green blood and ruptured organs, pooling beneath Aurora’s boots.","Dexter who had just killed a beast and saw this had a change of expression.","’ That talent...’","If she pressed that palm against his body . Dexter wasn’t certain his body could withstand it.","He shook his head and resumed his killing.","Across the district, the spear-wielding hero Bullet Spear Hero continued his own killing spree. His kill count was impressive, easily matching Dexter. But unlike Dexter, he still hadn’t directly saved a single civilian.","But Aurora was on another level entirely.","The S-rank hero moved through the battlefield like a ghost, her silver hair trailing behind her like a banner. Every goblin she approached died eith a simple touch.","Her kill count was the highest by far. In the time Dexter had killed thirty, she had dispatched over forty. The goblins didn’t even slow her down.","In under three minutes, the heroes had turned the tide. Most of the civilians in the market district had been evacuated to safe zones, and the streets were now littered with the corpses of two-armed and four-armed goblins.","The heroes excitedly killed more of the beasts as adrenaline fueled them.","They were so focused on their killing sprreeband raising their ranks that none of them noticed the dimensional gate begin to violently ripple again.","A massive hand, reached out, grabbed the edges of the torn space and pulled it apart as it walked out.","A Six-Armed Goblin King. The dungeon boss had emerged.","There were two ways to resolve a dungeon outbreak. The first was to use a space stabilizer to temporarily seal the dimensional gate.","This was the easiest and most common method, as it immediately stopped the flow of monsters, but it didn’t guarantee the same gate wouldn’t reopen in the future.","The second, and permanent, method was to kill the dungeon boss. Once the boss was slain, the dungeon core was destroyed, ensuring it would never appear again.","But a boss of this caliber wasn’t something a group of low-ranking heroes could simply gang up on.","And the King was not alone.","Four massive, four-armed goblins stepped out behind the boss. These were elite Goblin commander, each radiating a terrifying, suffocating aura.","A Mutated Class monster equaled a Meta Hero. A Fiend Class equaled a Super Hero. And an Ultra Class equaled an Ultra Hero.","The four commanders were Ultra Class monsters, ranked at Levels One, Two, Three, and Four respectively.","But the boss, the Six-Armed Goblin King—was a Level Seven Ultra Class monster.","They appeared silently, observing the distracted heroes with predatory amusement.","Without warning, the Level Four commander blurred into motion as it appeared behind a celebrating hero who was busy finishing off a Level 5 Fiend Class goblin.","\"Squelch!\"","The commander swept stabbed its crude sword into the hero’s neck.","\"W-what?\"","The hero ea stunned as she felt a cold sensation in her neck as her spine severed and a blade lashed through her neck.","Before the body could even hit the ground, the commander opened its massive jaws and bit half of the female hero’s head.","The skull popped like a grape. The monster chewed loudly, grinning happily as blood and brain matter oozed down its chin.","\"Be careful!\" someone seem to have noticed this and screamed in terror frim across the street.","The heroes’ expressions changed as they looked around.","But it was too late. The commanders had already spread out, charging into the crowd of heroes with devastating force.","The Goblin King’s burning crimson eyes swept the battlefield, instantly locking onto the most dangerous presence: Aurora.","Space twisted as it simply folded the distance, appearing directly behind the silver-haired S-rank hero.","Its massive, armored fist swung downward toward her massive chest.","Before the blow could land—","\"BOOM!!!\"","A massive explosion rang out a sa massive force slapped the Goblin King mid attack, sending it skidding sideways, its massive feet digging trenches into the asphalt as though the road were made of soft sand.","Aurora turned as she looked at her side.","Beside her was Dexter. He head the one who attacked and intercepted the Goblin King midway.","Aurora’s face was cold and indifferent as she glanced at him as though looking at an ant. \"I didn’t need your help.\"","Dexter didn’t even look at her.","He glanced toward a battered taxi sitting just behind where Aurora had been standing.","Without waiting for her response, he flashed over to the taxi. Using his enhanced hearing, he had heard the heartbeat of someone hiding beneath the dashboard.","If the Goblin King’s strike had connected with Aurora, the resulting shockwave of their clash would have instantly pulverized the old man inside the vehicle.","That was why Dexter had intercepted the blow.","He ripped the dented car door off its hinges, gently pulled the trembling old man out, and activated Flame Burst Step.","In a blur of crimson fire, he carried the civilian out of the warzone, depositing him safely in an alley three blocks away.","The old man quickly thanked him.\"Thank you, hero. Thank you.\"","Dexter merely nodded, turned, and launched himself back toward the market district.","At this moment, the four commander beasts were tearing through the heroes. The difference between the Superhuman Realm and the Ultra Realm was as vast as the distance between the earth and the sky.","While every level breakthrough in the Superhuman Realm granted a fifty-point increase to each attribute, the Ultra Realm granted a staggering one hundred and fifty points to each attribute per level.","But it wasn’t just numbers. There was a fundamental, qualitative shift in the body at the Ultra Realm. As one edged into the transcendent realm, they began to become one with the world.","Their mana changed at a molecular level, gaining the terrifying ability to condense from pure energy into solid, physical matter!","A Level Four Ultra Goblin commander grabbed a fleeing civilian. It drove its clawed hand directly into the man’s belly.","The man screamed, a sound of pure, unadulterated agony, as the beast’s arm plunged through his abdomen. With a violent yank, the commander ripped the man’s spine entirely out through his stomach.","The civilian didn’t die instantly.","He hung in the air, held up by the beast’s grip, screaming as his spine which was still dripping with blood and gore was waved in the air like a trophy."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131 | Facing An Ultra Class Beast!","paragraphs":["As the Goblin King and its commanders unleashed their aura, the surrounding heroes’ faces changed when they realized they were facing Ultra Level monsters.","\"This is clearly not a E rank Gate!\"","One of them said through clenched his teeth. Most of the heroes present were only in the Superhuman Realm.","Aurora’s cold voice echoed through the ears of every hero nearby, cutting through the panic.","\"I will stop the Level 7 Ultra-level boss. The rest of you, find a way to stop the other four commanders.\"","She didn’t wait for acknowledgment. Aurora vanished, moving so fast she created a sonic boom that shattered the remaining glass in the district.","\"BOOM!\"","She collided with the Six-Armed Goblin King, and the resulting impact blasted both of them directly into a massive shopping mall.","Deafening booms echoed from within the building, sounding like the beating of a massive war drum as the two Ultra powers clashed.","Left with no other choice, the remaining heroes divided into groups to confront the four commander beasts. Their only hope was to gang up on them.","Just as the Bullet Spear Man was contemplating whether he should even attempt to fight an Ultra-level beast, a figure plummeted from a tall building nearby.","\"Bang!\"","His hero name was Kinetic Man, a popular C-rank hero, but more importantly, a Level One Ultra Realm expert.","He turned to the Bullet Spear Man. \"Let’s deal with this one,\" he said, pointing at the Level Four Four-Armed Goblin Commander.","Then he turned to the others. \"You guys handle the other three.\"","The Bullet Spear Man’s face tightened, but he had no choice but to nod. He and Kinetic Man charged forward to engage the Level Four beast.","The rest of the heroes quickly split up. Five heroes went to face the Level Three commander. Four heroes engaged the Level Two, and another three rushed the Level One.","Dexter had just returned from dropping off the old man. He surveyed the battlefield instantly.","He saw the five heroes facing the Level Three beast. They had absolutely no chance. Even with a numerical advantage, the power gap was too immense.","On the other side, Kinetic Man was faring better. Using his kinetic talent and his shield, he was able to absorb the kinetic energy from the Level Four beast’s strikes, effectively tanking the attacks.","Meanwhile, the Bullet Spear Man used his incredible speed and piercing spear strikes to chip away at the beast. Dexter had heard of Kinetic Man; his ability to absorb and release kinetic energy made him the perfect shield. They would be alright.","But the five heroes fighting the Level Three commander were being slaughtered.","A simple punch from the beast sent one hero flying through a wall. A stomp nearly crushed another, but a third hero with a speed talent managed to push his comrade out of the way just in time.","They were barely containing it, saving each other from fatal blows, but they were taking heavy damage. Blood dripped from the corners of their mouths, and their movements were growing sluggish.","Dexter immediately sprinted toward them.","As he closed the distance, the Level Three goblin commander reached out with one of its massive hands and grabbed one of the heroes by the neck.","It lifted the man off the ground. The hero screamed, frantically punching the beast’s thick, armored arm, but it was like hitting a mountain.","The other heroes lunged forward to save him, but the goblin’s remaining three arms moved, perfectly blocking their attacks effortlessly.","\"Graaaa!\"","The beast’s grip tightened and was about to snap the hero’s neck like a twig.","Dexter’s eyes flared with violet light.","\"Flame Burst Step!\"","He crossed the remaining distance in a blink, leaving a trail of scorched air behind him as he materialized directly in front of the Level Three Ultra beast.","\"Flame Slash!\"","Dexter activated the bloodline skill without hesitation, his saber erupting in a crescent of compressed violet fire as he swung it directly at the four-armed goblin’s neck.","\"CLANG!\"","A green dome barrier materialized instantly around the beast, erupting from its skin like a translucent tortoise shell.","Space warped around the point of impact, as shockwaves rippled outward, cracking the asphalt beneath their feet.","The beast unconsciously released its grip on the hero and the man dropped to the ground, gasping and clutching his throat in horror.","The speedster hero quickly grabbed his comrade by the arm and dragging him away from the beast’s reach.","\"Hold it for thirty more seconds!\" a voice roared from behind.","Dexter glanced sideways. A hero in a red and white suit, had his entire body crackling with blinding blue plasma energy.","His hero name was Plasmatic.","Dexter frowned slightly but he eventually nodded his head.","The space around him shifted as his speed exploded. He vanished from in front of the beast and reappeared behind it.","The beast smirked and it stepped forward. Space folded around its massive body, and the creature vanished, reappearing directly behind Dexter.","Dexter’s eyes widened and before his conscious mind could process the threat. He spun backward, his saber sweeping upward in four rapid, desperate slashes.","\"Ding! Ding! Ding! Ding!\"","Four strikes, each one meeting one of the goblin’s four fists. The creature had launched all four arms simultaneously, each fist glowing with dense, emerald-green mana that had been condensed into solid, physical form.","The impacts sent tremors through Dexter’s entire body. The ground beneath his feet cracked and cratered as the reverberating force traveled through his legs and into the earth.","His arms shook as his jaw clenched. The difference in raw strength between a Seventh Stage Superhuman and a Third Level Ultra was staggering. Every blocked strike felt like being hit by a tank.","Then the beast grinned evilly.","Four blades materialized in its four hands, constructed of compressed mana, each one as sharp and durable as a physical weapon.","The creature didn’t waste a single motion as it launched a barrage of attacks, all four blades swinging at Dexter from different angles in a coordinated, relentless assault.","Dexter’s expression changed drastically as he overdrew Flame Burst Step, increasing his agility to be able to respond thickly."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132 | Killing Three Ultra Class Monsters!","paragraphs":["The beast’s attack flowed seamlessly, creating an endless, crushing barrage that gave Dexter no room to counterattack.","He was purely on the defensive.","But Flame Burst Step was still active. His speed was amplified by over 500%, and the Slaughter Extraction System had granted him substantial agility bonuses from the monsters he’d already killed. Combined with the physical enhancements from his body-tempering techniques, he was managing.","’This won’t do.’","Dexter realized. If this continued, he might actually be in trouble.","\"How long?!\" Dexter roared.","\"Five more seconds!\" Plasmatic roared back as his entire body now wreathed in blinding blue light. The plasma sphere between his palms had grown to the size of a basketball.","Five seconds.\"","Dexter gritted his teeth and continued to tank the assault. His saber moved in a blur, blocking, parrying, deflecting. The ground beneath him had been reduced to rubble. His arms burned.","Then the goblin commander suddenly glanced at Plasmatic Hero and its gaze hardened as it activated its skill.","\"ROOOOOOOAAAAR!\"","The sonic-mental assault erupted outward in a wave of devastating psychic pressure. Every hero within a ten-meter radius froze instantly, their minds disorientated as even two heroes collapsed and others stood still in confusion.","However, Dexter seemed to have expected it.","Like the saying goes. ’Bite me once shame on you, bite me twice, shame on me.’","The moment the roar began, he deactivated his Enhanced Hearing and detonated his Abyssal Emperor Flame. The deep violet fire blazed through his nervous system, incinerating the mental attack before it could do anything.","The Goblin Commander was still roaring, expecting everyone to be stunned.","Dexter didn’t waste the opening and vanished, reappearing directly behind the still-roaring creature. He immediately thrust forward with his entire strength.","\"Puchi!\"","The blade punched through the air and struck the creature’s back.","\"Ding.\"","The saber had penetrated barely an inch when resistance materialized. A layer of dense, emerald mana barrier appeared beneath the beast’s skin, stopping the blade from reaching any vital organs.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","Ultra-level beings could condense mana into physical matter and that included protective barriers formed directly beneath their skin.","The beast was essentially wearing a suit of invisible, mana-forged armor.","The beast’s roar cut off abruptly as it registered the pain. Its crimson eyes widened with surprise and then shifted to pure, concentrated fury.","\"ROOOOAR!\"","It angrily spun around and all four swords swept in a devastating in multiple devastating arcs.","Dexter immediately tried to move but he wasn’t fast enough as one of the beast’s mana blades slices through his shirt and opening a deep gash across his ribs","Dexter hissed through clenched teeth but didn’t falter. He landed in a crouch, one hand pressed against his bleeding side, his dark red eyes locked on the beast.","\"THREE SECONDS!\" Plasmatic’s voice thundered across the battlefield.","The goblin commander seemed to have heard it too. Its crimson eyes flickered toward the plasma-glowing hero","It immediately turned away from Dexter and launched itself toward Plasmatic, all four mana blades raised, intending to kill him before he could release his attack.","Dexter immediately flicked his wrists and a hairpin needle stabbed through the air like a silent bullet.","The hairpin left his hand like a comet, as it rocketed toward the beast’s back.","The weapon’s built-in Aimlock accuracy found its mark, slamming into the same one-inch wound Dexter had already opened on the creature’s spine.","\"Puchi!\"","Along with its penetrative ability, it stabbed even deeper this time.","The pain disrupted the beast’s spatial manipulation mid-step, causing it to stumble out of its folded space and materialize ten meters short of Plasmatic.","The beast roared in fury, pain and shock.","Just a bit more and needle would have pierced its heart. It slapped the needle away from its back.","\"Everyone, duck!\" Plasmatic roared as he released his attack.","Dexter didn’t hesitate. He dropped to the ground instantly. Every hero nearby followed suit.","The four-armed goblin commander was confused at first. Then its survival instincts screamed.","It tried to activate its spatial teleportation, folding space to escape whatever was coming.","But the gravity hero called Graviton among the group had already acted.","The air around the beast thickened instantly as gravitational force multiplied 10 fold. The goblin’s movements slowed drastically as if suddenly made of lead.","The slowdown lasted only 0.1 seconds.","That was all Plasmatic needed.","The hero’s chest plate split open, revealing a blinding core of concentrated plasma energy that had been charging for the past minute.","The energy erupted from his chest in a massive pillar of pure, white-hot light—a beam so intense that the air along its path ionized instantly, creating a vacuum corridor that the plasma traveled through at the speed of light itself.","The goblin face change it roared in fury and terror.","It immediately crossed all four forearms in front of its chest, activating its defensive technique.","Instantly, four layers of dense, green mana barriers materialized in front of it, each one thick enough to stop a Superhuman’s full-powered attack.","\"Bang! Bang! Bang! Bang!\"","The four barriers disintegrated as the plasma beam punched through all four layers of defense and struck the beast’s chest with the force of a small star going supernova.","The beast managed to dodge slightly as a massive hole appeared in the right side of the Level three beast’s torso.","Its entire right shoulder and both right arms were destroyed cleanly—vaporized by the plasma energy, leaving behind a cauterized, steaming wound that exposed the creature’s internal organs.","But the beast was still alive.","\"ROOOOOOAR—!\"","It roar of pain was cut short as Dexter activated GodSlayer Flash.","\"Crackle!\"","Thunder crackled underneath his foot as another image of Dexter suddenly appeared behind the beast.","Two Dexter appearing simultaneously, all at once.","But then, one Dexter started to fade, it was actually an afterimage.","Dexter stood up straight and flicked the blood off his blade.","For a heartbeat, nothing happened. The beast stood motionless, its remaining arms still raised, its mouth still open mid-roar.","Then a thin line appeared around the goblin’s neck as its head toppled forward, hit the ground with a wet thunk and rolled twice before coming to rest against a piece of rubble.","The massive, headless body swayed for a moment, green blood fountaining from the severed neck, before collapsing forward with a ground-shaking crash.","[Extracted: +10 Strength, +8 Agility, +7 Physique, +5 Mana]","Dexter exhaled slowly.","The heroes around him let out a collective breath of relief.","\"You did it!\" one of them cheered, slapping Plasmatic on the back. \"Nice! Well done!\"","\"Beautiful shot,\" another added, giving the plasma hero a thumbs up.","They turned to Dexter as well, offering grateful nods and thumbs-ups. \"Good job stunning the beast,\" the speedster hero said, extending his hand.","Dexter shook the man’s hand briefly, then shook his head. \"We need to help the others.\"","His voice cut through the celebration like a blade.","The heroes’ smiles faded instantly as they remembered the other Level four, Level Two, and Level One commanders were still active.","Kinetic Man and Bullet Spear was still holding the line against the Level Four’s remnants.","Dexter was already moving. \"The Level two first. Same strategy.\"","The five heroes nodded.","***","The Level two commander was still engaged with its group of heroes when Dexter’s reinforced squad arrived.","Two of the heroes were already down, one unconscious, one bleeding from a head wound. The remaining three were barely holding.","Dexter assessed the situation in a single glance.","\"Same setup!\" he roared. \"Gravity hero, slow it down! Plasmatic, charge! Rest of you, keep it contained!\"","The heroes moved into position.","The Graviton extended both hands, and the air around the Level Two beast thickened. The creature’s movements slowed down as Dexter charged in.","He engaged the beast head-on, drawing its attention, forcing all four arms to focus on him.","Thirty seconds, Fourty-five seconds.","\"NOW! DODGE!\"","Dexter flashed sideways. The plasma beam erupted from Plasmatic’s chest for the second time, screaming across the battlefield at the speed of light.","This time, the Level Three beast couldn’t dodge as the beam struck its body and punched through the creature’s body like paper.","Dexter followed up with a slash, severing its head immediately.","The beast didn’t even know how it died as it collapsed.","[Extracted: +7 Strength, +6 Agility, +5 Physique, +3 Mana]","The heroes didn’t celebrate this time. They simply turned and ran toward the next target.","***","The Level One commander fell next.","With the full group of heroes now free to concentrate their forces, the strategy executed flawlessly. The gravity hero slowed the beast. Dexter drew its aggro, tanking its attacks with his tempered body while the other heroes created openings.","Plasmatic charged his beam. Almost a minute later, another smoking hole appeared in a goblin commander’s chest.","Kinetic Man and Bullet Spear Man had finished the Level Four beast at this time.","***","The market district fell silent.","All four commander beasts were dead. Their massive corpses littered the streets, green blood pooling beneath them in expanding lakes. The surviving heroes stood among the carnage, exhausted but alive.","Dexter leaned against a wrecked car, pressing his hand against the gash on his ribs. The wound had actually stopped bleeding by itself.","Moreover, he could actually see his wounds been healed rapidly, visible to the naked eyes."]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133 | Selene!","paragraphs":["As the last Four-armed Goblin fell, the market district fell into a strange quiet.","The entire district had transformed into a battlefield, littered with goblin and human corpses alike.","Heroes were scattered across the streets, panting heavily. Some were kneeling beside fallen comrades, closing the eyes of the dead. Others were bandaging injuries.","At that moment, the popular female hero called Regen stated to go from one hero to another as she used her healing talent to heal the injured heroes.","Dexter stood in the middle of the street, his violet colored eyes reduced till it settled on dark with a hint of red.","If one looked closely, they would see he had three rings in his eyes: one dark, one red, and the third violet.","But the violet vanished like it wasn’t there, and the red ring faded till it was barely visible, leaving just the dark one.","His eyes looked into the mall where Aurora had vanished with the Goblin King.","\"Boom!\" \"Boom!\" \"Boom!\"","Sounds of battle still echoed inside the massive hall as Aurora and the Goblin King were still locked in battle.","Dexter frowned worriedly. If the Goblin King defeats her, then it might spell trouble for them.","All of a sudden, a resounding boom echoed from the ruins of the massive shopping mall.","\"KA-BOOM!\"","Shockwaves exploded out from the mall as half the massive mall collapsed instantly and the other half had its roof blown to bits.","An entire freaking mall had actually been reduced to rubble just like that!","The earth-shaking impacts finally ceased, and 10 seconds later, space warped as Aurora appeared in the air above the destroyed building.","The entire mall had been devastated—half of it had collapsed entirely, and the remaining half was reduced to a single wall.","Aurora hovered for a moment as her silver floated in the sunlight. In her right hand was the severed head of the Six-Armed Goblin King, dripping blood.","She casually threw it to the ground.","\"Thud.\"","The massive head hit the pavement, rolling slightly before coming to rest in a pool of green blood.","\"Whoohoo!\"","The surrounding heroes erupted into cheers and whistles. The nightmare was over, and the boss was dead.","Aurora didn’t smile. She turned and flew directly into the still-open gate. She was gone for barely a minute before she emerged again.","In her hand, she now held a treasure chest, the dungeon core. She had gone in to claim it, and this would ensure that the dungeon would never reopen.","As she landed on the ground, the spatial rift behind her began to shrink, its edges folding inward until it vanished with a soft pop.","The heroes cheered even louder. Aurora nodded at the group. Her gaze swept over the crowd, landing on Kinetic Man and Bullet Spear Man.","She gave them a curt nod.","\"Well done,\" she said to Kinetic Man. \"You held the line.\"","Kinetic Man smiled, nodding his head in acknowledgment, though he was clearly exhausted.","Then, Aurora turned her head. Her eyes found Dexter standing alone in the middle of the street.","She began to walk toward him. The heroes parted ways for her.","Aurora’s face was indifferent through which a small apologetic smile touched her lips.","She then opened her mouth to speak. \"I apologize for earlier—\"","Aurora froze. Her words died in her throat as Dexter raised a hand all of a sudden to shush her.","Dexter’s face changed dramatically as his eyes widened and his expression transformed into one of panic.","He didn’t look at her as his head snapped towards a particular direction!","Frost Sense was ringing!","\"Selene!\"","Aurora’s gaze turned cold. She opened her mouth to say something when Dexter exploded with Flame Burst Step and Godslayer Flash!","The ground beneath him shattered into pieces!","\"Crackle!\"","Blue thunder erupted around his right leg.","’Whoosh!’","Violet flames exploded around his left leg.","He combined Thunder Manipulation and Flame Burst Step, transforming into a blurring streak of blue and violet light as he dashed straight for his parked Vanguard V4.","The moment his hand touched the metal frame, he willed it into his storage ring.","The vehicle vanished in a flash of golden light.","He didn’t stop. He rocketed into a secluded alley between two collapsed buildings, hidden from the eyes of the heroes and Aurora.","He threw his arm out.","Golden light flashed, and a normal-looking family-type SUV materialized on the ground. The Type-6 vehicle!","Dexter yanked the door open, dove into the driver’s seat, and slammed his hand on the ignition.","The arcane engine roared to life, humming with terrifying power. He reached into his storage ring, pulled out a glowing green nexus core he had harvested from a goblin corpse, and shoved it into the mana-fuel slot beside the steering wheel.","The console blazed to life.","\"Flight mode activated,\" a mechanical voice chimed.","The SUV’s chassis shifted. Hidden panels retracted, and two massive jet thrusters deployed from the undercarriage. Four smaller, directional thrusters unfolded from the sides.","Dexter gripped the wheel. \"Go!\"","\"BOOM!\"","The jet engines ignited with a deafening roar, unleashing a massive shockwave that blew the brick walls of the alley apart. The Type-6 SUV shot into the sky like a bullet, leaving a trail of blue fire in its wake.","Dexter pushed the engine to its maximum speed. The city blurred beneath him as he crossed districts in seconds.","In less than a minute, he arrived home.","The moment he reached the corner heading to his street, he killed the thrusters and descended into a nearby alley. The jet engines retracted, the chassis shifted, and four armored tires deployed.","He didn’t even wait for the landing gear to fully lock before slamming the accelerator.","\"Vrooom!\"","The SUV screamed out of the alley as he drifted around the final corner and screeched to a halt directly in front of his bungalow.","He didn’t turn off the engine nor did he close the door. He burst out of the vehicle and sprinted toward the house."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134 | Abyssal Emperor Heavenly Flame Might","paragraphs":["The front door was already open and cold air could be seen seeping out in forget like foggy smoke.","He crashed into the living room. The air inside was so cold that his breath crystallized instantly into thick, white plumes.","The girls weren’t in the living room.","Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing tracked them to the hallway. He burst through the corridor and found Mira, Lyra, and Tessa standing at the entrance of the bedroom, their faces pale with worry.","Tessa.","Dexter was stunned to see the baker’s daughter standing there.","’The hell she’s doing here?’","But he couldn’t afford to ask why she was there.","He looked past them and into the bedroom.","Selene lay on her bed.","The entire mattress had been frozen solid into a block of pure, translucent ice that coated her body like a crystalline coffin.","The frost had spread outward from the bed, consuming the walls, the ceiling, the floor, and had already covered Mira and Lyra’s beds on either side.","The room was a frozen wasteland. The temperature was so low that the very air seemed to burn with cold.","The moment she saw him, Lyra’s voice exploded in his mind.","\"I searched everywhere for the suppressant serum! I couldn’t find it anywhere!\"","Mira didn’t speak. She simply glared at Dexter, her crimson eyes burning in a slightt accusatory tone.","Tessa stared at him in shock. ’Was this what Dexter deals with every day?’","Dexter didn’t have the time nor the luxury to say anything or explain himself.","The moment he stepped inside, he simply exploded with a wave of energy.","The Abyssal Emperor Flame erupted from his body like a hurricane as deep violet fire blazed outward from every fiber of his being.","As the flames erupted, the ice immediately started to recede, melting and evaporating at the same time.","\"Tsssssssssssssssss!\"","The frost on the hallway walls vanished instantly upon contact with the violet fire, transforming directly from solid to gas in a hissing burst of steam.","The air itself seemed to part before him, the cold retreating like a subject bowing before an emperor.","Dexter walked forward.","Each step melted the frozen floorboards beneath his feet. The ice parted before him in perfect, circular waves, steam rising in elegant spirals around his body.","He approached Selene’s ice-encased bed. The frozen coffin around her body was thick—easily six inches of solid, mana-infused ice that pulsed with the hostile, parasitic energy of the Eternal Winter.","Dexter placed his hand on the ice.","The Abyssal Emperor Flame surged.","\"CRACK!\"","The ice instantly cracked as the molecular structure of the frozen water simply broke apart. Chunks of ice fell away from Selene’s body, melting into steam before they could hit the mattress.","The frost on the walls, the ceiling, the other beds, all of it retreated, evaporating into clouds of white vapor that drifted out through the window.","Within seconds, the room was clear.","Selene lay on the bed, her skin ghostly pale, her lips blue, her silver hair damp from the melted ice. Her breathing was shallow and erratic, her chest barely rising.","Dexter flicked his right hand. A syringe materialized in his palm; the Grade-3 Eternal Frost Suppressant Serum appeared from his system storage.","He stabbed it directly into Selene’s arm.","\"Click.\"","The serum discharged into her bloodstream. The warm, golden liquid spread through her veins, fighting back the parasitic cold energy that had nearly consumed her from the inside out.","Dexter felt the needle pierce his own skin simultaneously as the Ring of Shared Burdens transferred the pain to him as it always did, but he barely registered it. He was focused entirely on Selene.","He placed both hands on her body, channeling the Abyssal Emperor Flame through his palms and into her skin. The warmth was gentle.","And his control was perfect. He was a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith Afterall; manipulating flames was his specialty.","The violet fire carefully seeped into her meridians, countering the Eternal Winter’s parasitic cold at its source.","Her breathing gradually steadied. The blue faded from her lips as color slowly returned to her cheeks.","If she wasn’t resistant to Ice, she would have definitely died five times over.","Dexter stayed beside her, kneeling on the floor, his hands resting on her arm as he continued to pump controlled warmth into her body.","***","In the hallway, three pairs of eyes stared at Dexter with various expressions on their faces.","Lyra’s eyes were wide with astonishment. She had never seen Dexter use a flame talent before.","The man she had married, the quiet, unassuming house husband who cooked their meals and took care of them was currently blasting out violet flames so intense he looked like a flame god!","She had thought he might have been talentless but knew something wasn’t right when Dexter killed those two assassins.","Now she definitely knew his talent wasn’t worse than hers.","Mira’s reaction was different.","Her brows were furrowed as she stared at Dexter.","’ Heavenly Flame?’","The Crimson Flame-Heart was an S-rank ability that had once made her the youngest S-rank hero in the city. She was obsessed with all types of flames and she could feel the one around Dexter wasn’t ordinary.","The heat radiating from his body was far, far hotter than her own S-rank flame talent.","If she had to grade it, she would grade it S-rank at minimum. Possibly higher.","But Dexter was supposed to be F-rank. The useless, talentless bastard son of the Ashford family. An F-rank mana affinity that would never amount to anything.","’If he has an F-rank talent, then what were these flames? Was it a second talent? Or did he actually manage to get his hands on a Heavenly Flame?’","She was quite surprised.","Dexter had shocked them again and again, and each revelation was more impossible than the last, to the point that the surprise was even starting to fade.","She had already suspected he had a powerful backing. This simply confirmed it.","***","Tessa stood further back from the other two girls, her green eyes locked on Dexter’s flaming silhouette with undisguised shock.","’ Is this the useless bastard son of the Ashford family?’","The heat radiating from his body was oppressive even from the hallway.","’ He actually possesses such high level talent and a high-level Heavenly Flame too’","It was as though she could see right through him the moment he exploded with the flame.","’ What was the Ashford family thinking, discarding someone like this? As expected of a backwater family.’ Her lips curled as she shook her head, a mischievous glint in her eyes.","[A/N:My steady release rate is 5 or 4 Chapters per day. Your Super gifts can increase that all the way to 10 Chapters per day.","A super gift for 10 Chapters.","2 super gifts, 20 Chapters will be released in that same week.","3 Super gifts? (kill me! lol) 30 Chapters that same week. That’s my limit, can’t go higher than that or my stockpile will be exhausted.","Enjoy!]"]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135 | Sigh, Women Are So Confusing","paragraphs":["Dexter continued warming Selene’s body until he was certain she was stable. He slowly withdrew his hands, extinguishing the Abyssal Emperor Flame, and exhaled a long breath of exhaustion.","He had been battling for the past hour and rushing here without resting, along with being worried about Selene, which added to his exhaustion.","’ Thank God I came early. I don’t know what would have happened if I’d been a minute later.’","He almost slapped himself.","In the excitement of the monster outbreak, the emergency alert, the argument with Mira, amongst other things, he had completely forgotten what he planned to do after the meal.","He had planned to inject Selene with the new Grade-3 Eternal Frost Suppressant Serum after breakfast.","But after the sudden emergency, it escaped his mind, leaving Selene vulnerable to another attack.","The old serum had worn off days ago. The new one sat in his storage ring the entire time he was fighting goblins, completely forgotten.","It was his fault—all of it.","If he had been more responsible, taking five seconds to inject the serum before leaving, Selene wouldn’t have nearly frozen to death.","His jaw clenched, and he sighed as he slowly stood up, intending to leave the bedroom and let her rest.","But the moment he shifted his weight, a small, icy hand shot out and grabbed his arm.","Dexter froze.","Selene, still fast asleep, pulled his arm toward her with surprising strength. She hugged it tightly against her chest, wrapping both of her arms around it and pressing her cheek against his skin, clinging to him like a child holding a teddy bear.","Dexter was stunned. He immediately dialed back the active, visible flames of the Abyssal Emperor Flame. Still, he kept the internal heat radiating from his body, knowing she needed the warmth to stave off any residual frost energy.","However, a major dilemma presented itself.","His entire body was caked in blood, sweat, and gore.","He had just returned from a battlefield, and his clothes were torn and stained with green goblin blood and his own red blood.","Mira slowly wheeled her self into the bedroom, using her spectral arms. She glanced at Selene clinging to Dexter, then her crimson eyes traveled down Dexter’s body.","\"You are injured,\" she stated indifferently.","Dexter looked down at himself. He had almost forgotten about his injury.","There was a deep gash on his ribs from the Level Three goblin commander; although it had stopped bleeding, it was still healing.","Dexter smiled awkwardly. \"It’s just superficial injuries. Don’t be worried about me.\"","Mira immediately snorted, her eyes narrowing. \"Who is worried about you? I’m only worried you’re going to end up getting infected. Once you’re infected, you won’t be able to take care of us any longer. \"","With that, she turned her wheelchair around and began to leave. As she passed Lyra in the doorway, she paused as she said, projecting her thoughts. \"You should help him clean his wounds. I can’t.\"","Lyra nodded her head slowly. ’ Okay.’","Her voice echoed in Mira’s mind. She then turned and headed toward the kitchen to fetch the medical kit.","While Lyra was gone, Dexter turned his attention to the other person still lingering in the room.","He frowned. \"What are you doing here?\"","Tessa smiled, casually leaning against the doorframe. \"I was playing chess with Grandma Lucy opposite your house when she sensed something. I thought they were under attack, so I came in. I didn’t expect this scene.\"","Dexter’s frown deepened. His eyes locked onto her with sharp suspicion. \"The formation didn’t stop you?\"","Tessa innocently blinked her green eyes. \"What formation?\"","Dexter stared at her. She looked completely genuine, but he knew she was lying. The Type-5 House Protection Talisman was fully active and intact.","It restricted even space itself, and even Transcendent Experts can’t enter.","Yet Tessa had walked right through it as if it didn’t exist, without breaking the formation.","*What kind of monster is this girl?* Dexter thought as his face turned slightly grim.","He had no idea what this little girl’s intentions were, but if she wanted to harm them, not even the formation could help.","But now wasn’t the time to interrogate the baker’s daughter.","\"Thanks for your help,\" Dexter said. \"And thank Grandma Lucy for me. You can leave now.\"","Tessa blinked as she stared at Dexter for a moment, then nodded and pushed off the doorframe. \"Anytime.\" She flashed him a brilliant smile, turned, and skipped out of the room.","***","A minute later, Lyra returned with a white medical box, a bowl of warm water, and a clean cloth. She walked towards him and sat down on the edge of Selene’s bed.","Lyra opened the medical box and began pulling out supplies: a bottle of ethanol, cotton wool, and bandages. Then, without asking his permission, she picked up a pair of scissors from the kit.","\"RIIIIIIIIIIIIIP!!!\"","Dexter’s torn, blood-soaked shirt fell away in two pieces, dropping to the floor and revealing his muscular but bloody body.","Dexter blinked. \"...That was my nice shirt.\"","Lyra ignored him completely. Her expression was frigid, her dark eyes entirely devoid of their usual softness.","She soaked a piece of cotton wool with antiseptic ethanol and reached out, gently but firmly pressing it against the deep gash on his ribs.","Dexter winced, his muscles tensing involuntarily as the stinging alcohol bit into the open wound. \"Ah...\"","Lyra didn’t react.","She continued dabbing the injury, cleaning away the dried blood, then she moved to the cuts on his chest,","She then dipped the clean cloth into the warm water, wiping away the layers of green goblin blood, sweat, and dirt that coated his torso, face, and arms.","Despite her gentle care, her face remained incredibly cold.","’ She seems mad.’","Dexter blinked as he saw her face.","Dexter scratched his chin awkwardly, then spoke.","\"I’m sorry, all right? See, it’s nothing serious. It’s just superficial wounds. \"","Lyra did not reply, nor did she look him in the eye. She just kept wiping the blood from his abdomen, with her jaw clenched tight.","Dexter sighed. He racked his brain, trying to figure out how to break through this icy wall of anger.","Suddenly, an idea popped into his head. He flipped his right hand, and a golden light flashed.","A Celestial Moon Pastry materialized in his palm, perfectly baked, glowing faintly with mana and smelling absolutely divine.","\"Here,\" Dexter said softly, holding it out to her. \"I bought this for you on the way.\"","Lyra’s nose flared. Her dark eyes locked onto the pastry, and for the first time since she had entered the room, they lit up.","The pastry looked incredible, and the aroma was tantalizing. Just smelling it, she could tell it would be the best thing she had ever tasted.","She stared at it, her eyes wide with desire for a while. But then, Lyra shook her head violently.","She tore her gaze away from the pastry, glared at Dexter angrily, then grabbed the bowl of warm water and the medical kit, stood up, and marched out of the room.","\"Bang!\"","The door slammed shut as she angrily walked out.","Dexter was left sitting on the edge of the bed, shirtless, covered in half-cleaned blood, with a pastry in his right hand.","On the bed beside him, Selene shifted, hugging his arm tighter and letting out a soft, contented sigh.","Dexter looked down at the pastry, then at the closed door, and let out a long, heavy sigh.","\"Women,\" he muttered under his breath. \"So confusing.\"","[A/N: Really thought she would accept the pastries uhn?\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136 | What Am I Supposed To Do, Let You Go?","paragraphs":["The Hero Association headquarters never slept.","Even at this hour, the corridors hummed with activity.","Heroes in armor strode through the hallways with confidence.","Support staff shuffled papers behind desks.","Jasmine Constance sat at her assigned workstation in the Silver-Rank Administrative Wing, her fingers moving mechanically across the keyboard.","A stack of dungeon clearance reports sat beside her elbow, each one requiring review and verification before being submitted to the central archive.","She was halfway through the seventh report when a familiar voice called out from behind her.","\"Hey, Jasmine, did you see the morning broadcast?\"","It was Darren, her colleague. A guy who had been trying to get with her since she started working here.","Jasmine didn’t look up. \"I’ve been busy.\"","\"You should check it out.\" Darren leaned against the edge of her desk, arms crossed. \"That Ashford mess. You know, the noble family?\"","Jasmine’s fingers paused on the keyboard. Just for a second. Then she resumed typing.","\"What about them?\"","\"Turns out the bastard son he’s actually not as useless as everyone thought. The Ashford family thought he was useless and disowned him after burdening him with marrying three cripples.\" Darren whistled low.","Jasmine’s hands stopped moving completely.","\"Three?\"","\"Three. And not just any three. The three crippled daughters from the Calloway, Vance, and Frost families.\" Darren shook his head slowly. \"The ones from that SSS-rank dungeon disaster a few years back. The Crimson Valkyrie, the Shadow Saintess, and the Eternal Ice Princess.\"","He let out a low, pitying breath.","\"The bastard son of the Ashford family, married to three crippled women. Dumped in some run-down bungalow in the outer district but he actually turned out not to be usless. He actually showed up in a C-rank dungeon outbreak and managed to deal with the disaster along with Aurora, Kinetic Man and a few heroes. A few heroes were even praising him that he saved them. \"","Darren clicked his tongue. \"I wonder what the Ashford family would do now that they’ve found out he’s no longer usless and actually at the superhuman realm.\"","Jasmine stared at the glowing screen in front of her. The text blurred.","She could feel her heartbeat in her throat.","’Dexter.’","The name screamed inside her skull but not a single sound left her lips.","She remembered him.","Of course she remembered him.","She was the one who had been there when the world told him he was nothing.","---","Five years ago.","Ashford Family Stable.","Jasmine had found him sitting on the edge of the roof, looking sad.","She had seen the way the other servants treated him and after she was done with her Servants duties, she run across the entire Place to find him.","When she reached the rooftop, she didn’t speak immediately. She simply walked over, sat down beside him, and wrapped her arms around his waist.","\"Not even the servants...,\" he had whispered. His voice was empty and hollow.","\"Not just being a slave, I possess an f rank talent and lowr mana affinity. I can’t even absorb mana properly. I’ll never become a hero. I’ll never be anything. There’s no hope I can ever escape this place.\"","Jasmine had held him tighter.","\"Your rank doesn’t define you, Dexter. You can leave anytime you wish. No one can stop you.\"","\"You don’t understand—\"","\"I understand perfectly.\" She pulled back just enough to look into his eyes. Her own were fierce. Burning. \"I’ve watched you train for years. I’ve watched you push yourself harder than anyone else. Your affinity is low. So what? Talent is low, who cares?. But determination? Will?\" She pressed her palm flat against his chest. \"That can’t be taught. And you have more of it than anyone I’ve ever met.\"","For a brief moment, something flickered in his eyes. A tiny ember of hope in the middle of a dying fire.","That was the day they became inseparable.","And now, standing in the present, standing in that same hallway with Darren’s words echoing in her ears, Jasmine felt that same ember burning inside her own chest.","---","\"Jasmine?\"","Darren’s voice snapped her back.","She blinked. Her hands were trembling slightly. She pressed them flat against the desk to still them.","\"You okay?\" Darren frowned, leaning closer. \"You look pale.\"","\"I’m fine.\" Her voice came out quieter than she intended. She cleared her throat and repeated herself, louder this time. \"I’m fine. Just tired.\"","Darren studied her for a moment. He clearly didn’t believe her. But he knew better than to push a woman you’re trying to court.","\"Anyway,\" he continued, straightening up, \"the whole thing is a mess. The three families thought they were marrying the legitimate heir. Turns out the bastard was the firstborn. So they got scammed. Now they’re stuck with a disowned nobody living in the slums with their crippled daughters.\"","He laughed dryly.","\"Can you imagine? Three former S-rank talents, reduced to... that?\"","Jasmine’s jaw tightened.","\"He’s not a nobody,\" she said quietly.","Darren blinked. \"What?\"","\"Nothing.\" Jasmine turned back to her screen. \"I need to finish these reports.\"","Darren shrugged and wandered back to his own desk.","Jasmine stared at the holographic text floating before her eyes. None of the words registered. Her mind had already drifted far away.","’Dexter... what happened to you?’","---","The rooftop. One year ago.","The last day she had seen him.","But everything else was different.","Dexter stood at the edge of the stable rooftop, his back to her.","\"The marriage contract came through,\" he said. His voice was flat, emotionless.","\"The family gave me two options. Accept the arrangement and leave the estate. Or refuse and.l remain here as a servant for the rest of my life.\"","Jasmine’s heart had trembled.","\"Then refuse!\" She said grimly.","\"Dexter, refuse and come with me. We can leave this city. We can go somewhere far away. My family isn’t powerful, but we can—\"","\"Your family isn’t powerful.\" He turned to face her. His eyes were dead. \"That’s exactly the point, Jasmine. If I run, the Ashfords will hunt us down. And your family cannot protect you from them. No one can.\"","\"Then let them come!\" Her voice cracked. As her eyes shook. \"I don’t care about the Ashfords! I don’t care about any of them! I just want—\"","\"But I care.\"","His voice was so quiet she almost missed it.","He reached up and gently wiped a tear from her cheek.","\"I care about what happens to you, Jasmine. And if I run, they will use you to get to me. They will hurt you. And I...\" His voice faltered. \"I can’t let that happen.\"","\"Then what am I supposed to do?\" she whispered. \"Just... let you go?\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137 | You’re In My Bed","paragraphs":["Dexter was startled awake by a crisp, chiming notification from his system.","He blinked, his eyes adjusting to the darkness. The digital clock on the nightstand read 5:00 AM. It was the dead of night.","As his senses sharpened, he realized he was not in his own room. He was in the girls’ bedroom. He hadn’t managed to leave the night before; the exhaustion from the battle, combined with Selene’s iron grip, had pulled him straight into a deep sleep.","He lay still, scanning the room with his enhanced hearing. To his left, Mira was asleep on her own bed, completely silent, not making a single sound. To his right, Lyra was also sleeping, but instead of snoring, she was making a soft, rhythmic purring sound, like a cute tiger cub.","Then, Dexter’s eyes widened.","Mira’s fingers were twitching. Not just one finger, but all five of her fingers on her right hand were making subtle, grasping motions, as if she were trying to hold onto something.","\"Finally!\"","Dexter whispered happily.","A massive smile broke across Dexter’s face. All their efforts, the Grade-1, Grade-2, and Grade-3 meals, the tea, the massages and the arduous cultivation—were not in vain.","Myrawas actually healing. Slowly but steadily, her nerves were regenerating. He could tell that given enough time and his continued cooking, she would heal rapidly.","His joy, however, was immediately accompanied by a sharp, tingling numbness in his left arm. He looked down.","Selene was still fast asleep, but she was clinging to his arm like a lifeline. She had wrapped both of her arms around it, pulling it tightly against her chest, hugging it like a giant teddy bear. He could feel two incredibly soft, massive mounds of flesh squeezing tightly against his forearm, making him feel incredibly embarrassed. The blood flow to his arm had been completely cut off, leaving the limb frozen and numb.","Yet, looking at her sleeping so peacefully, her silver hair—which looked significantly healthier and prettier than when he first met her—spilling across the pillow, he found himself thinking the numbness was entirely worth it. Her eyelashes fluttered softly, and she murmured something inaudible in her sleep, pulling his arm even closer.","As if sensing his gaze, Selene’s eyes suddenly snapped open.","Through her echolocation, her sightless gaze immediately locked onto Dexter. At first, her brows furrowed in confusion, as if she thought she was dreaming. Then, she blinked, realizing it was reality.","\"You are here,\" she muttered softly.","Dexter nodded. \"Yes, I’m here.\"","Her brows furrowed even deeper. \"You are here on my bed.\"","\"Yes, I’m on your bed.\"","She remained silent for a few seconds as though waiting for it to sink into Dexter. But Dexter was also doing the same.","She couldn’t handle the silence anymore and tilted her head as she said.","\"Why?\"","Dexter chuckled and glanced down at his left arm, which she was still desperately clinging to.","Selene followed his gaze downward. She saw her own hands and even one of her leg tightly wrapped around his bicep, pressing it against her chest and belly.","\"Eh—\"","Her eyes widened in shock. She instantly let go, her pale face flushing a deep crimson. She tried to hide her embarrassment by lowering her head, but her skin was simply too pale to conceal the blush.","She looked like a child who had been caught doing something wrong, yet even with her head down, Dexter could feel her echolocation completely focused on him.","Dexter chuckled at her incredible cuteness but didn’t say anything to further embarrass her. He stood up, shaking his numb arm vigorously to get the blood flowing again.","As he turned to leave, he heard Selene’s tiny, whisper-like voice. \"Sorry. And... thank you.\"","Dexter smiled warmly. \"You’re welcome.\"","He left the bedroom and headed straight to his own room. Sitting on his bed, he finally opened the system notification that had woken him up.","***","[Investment Return Detected: Suppressed Eternal Winter Ice Curse & Sustained Emotional Care]","[Multiplier: 100x]","[Rewards Granted:]","1. E-Rank Talent Advancement Card: Ice Manipulation.","2. Raw Materials: 10 kg of Premium Diamond Rice and additional spiritual ingredients.","3. Grade-3 Divine Peak Recovery Pill ×1","Dexter inspected the Grade-3 Divine Pill carefully. The system’s description was very specific:","[The pill can temporarily heal all injuries and return the user to their absolute peak form for exactly 24 hours. However, once the 24-hour duration expires, the user’s original injuries will not only return but will significantly worsen, making the pill a desperate, win-lose situation.]","Dexter frowned. Selene was blind. Although she could \"see\" through echolocation now, it wasn’t true sight. A pill that could temporarily heal all injuries and restore her to her peak would be incredibly tempting for a crippled hero.","But the backlash was too severe.","\"I don’t think it’s safe to give this to them,\" Dexter muttered to himself. \"If they get desperate, they might use it, and end up hurting themselves more.\"","Yet, he also realized that giving them the pill was like giving them hope. It was physical proof that their conditions could be reversed, that a cure existed. He wasn’t 100% sure how long it would take to fully heal them, but with the system, he was at least 50% sure he could do it eventually.","He decided to hold onto the pill for now, keeping it as a safety net rather than giving it to the girls prematurely.","As he put the pill away, a sudden thought hit him. He slapped his forehead.","\"Damn it. I didn’t make dinner.\"","He had been so exhausted and distracted by Selene’s outbreak that he had completely forgotten to cook the evening meal. He stood up and walked to the kitchen to see what the girls had eaten.","Upon checking the kitchen, he found the pots and pans exactly where he had left them. The girls hadn’t cooked.","Instead, he checked the microwave and found it completely empty. The Celestial Moon Pastries he had stored there were gone.","Lyra and Mira had eaten the pastries for dinner. While Selene hadn’t eaten anything.","Dexter leaned against the counter, deep in thought. Lyra had been so angry the day before that she had rejected the pastry he offered her directly. For her to reject food meant she was truly mad at him.","Usually, food was his ultimate peace-offering. If food couldn’t calm Lyra down, he had no idea what would. He needed a new plan to appease her.","As for Mira, he temporarily placed her in the back of his mind. Her emotions were so unpredictable, swinging between angry, indifferent, and secretly pleased, that trying to decipher her was like dealing with someone bipolar.","He would tackle Lyra first. Her expressions were usually more readable, and right now, her face was frigid.","He sighed, staring at the empty microwave. \"How do I fix this?\" he muttered, scratching his chin as the sun began to peek through the kitchen window."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138 | Mad Lyra","paragraphs":["Dexter didn’t go back to sleep.","He sat cross-legged on his bed and closed his eyes, as he cultivated.","Suddenly he noticed something different with his body.","\"I’ve broken through?\"","Dexter chuckled. He hadn’t even been trying, Yet his body had continued absorbing mana automatically.","This was the benefit of an EX-Rank affinity. His body automatically drew in energy into his body.","Whether he was awake or asleep, meditating or eating or fighting, the world offered its power to him willingly, and his body accepted it without hesitation.","He hadn’t even noticed the breakthrough happening. One moment he was Seventh Stage Superhuman. The next he had woken up and was in the Eighth Stage.","Dexter closed his eyes and turned his attention inward, entering the vast, dark universe of his inner world.","The cosmic DNA helix floated in the void, its first seven segments blazing with stable, radiant light.","The eighth segment had ignited during the night, its gray shell crumbling away to reveal a fresh, pulsing glow that connected seamlessly to the chain.","But that wasn’t all.","Dexter’s gaze shifted to the seven brilliant Star Nodes floating near the top of the helix.","They burned steadily, each one a miniature sun radiating independent mana.","But there were actually newer ones.","Overnight, he had awakened three more!","’It seems what they said is true, fighting an killing monsters really unlocks one’s potential.’","And he hadn’t even absorbed the nexus cores of the beasts yet.","Now he possess ten mana reservoirs, each one capable of storing and supplying mana separately from the others.","This meant that his total mana capacity was equivalent to ten individuals of the same cultivation realm combined.","A single Eighth Stage Superhuman would normally possess one mana pool. Dexter possessed ten.","With this kind of capacity, if he ever acquired an ultimate technique that could drain an ordinary cultivator dry in seconds or maybe when he reach a high stage in the Godslayer Thunder Saber art, he could use it recklessly.","But the true advantage of the Star Nodes was beyond that.","The Grand Cosmos Scripture didn’t use meridians.","It bypassed them entirely. Each Star Node functioned as an independent power source, capable of feeding mana directly to a specific technique or body part without needing to circulate through the traditional meridian network.","This meant Dexter could use multiple techniques simultaneously.","Conventionally, a cultivator channeled mana through their meridians to power a technique.","Using two techniques at once required splitting the mana flow, which reduced the effectiveness of both and demanded immense concentration.","Highly proficient fighters could manage two, maybe three, techniques simultaneously.","But Dexter wasn’t using meridians.","With ten Star Nodes, he could assign one node to power a flame technique with his left hand.","Another node to power a thunder technique with his right.","A third to sustain a movement technique.","A fourth to maintain a defensive barrier.","A fifth to fuel an auxiliary talent.","A sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth, and tenth—all running independently, all simultaneously, without any loss of efficiency or concentration.","Ten techniques at once.","And if he awakened twenty Star Nodes, he could use twenty. If he awakened a hundred, he could use a hundred.","The Limitless Primordial Universe Star Scripture had no ceiling. Every new Star Node didn’t just increase his mana pool—it multiplied his combat versatility exponentially.","Dexter opened his eyes, a quiet, satisfied smile settling on his face.","\"Fascinating,\" he murmured.","That wasn’t all, he noticed his injuries has all healed and when he checked them, he saw 42 rows of crimson marks on his chest.","’I killed 42 monsters yesterday, is this... the Asura Slaughter technique?’","Dexter frowned. The mark looked wierd and bloody but strangely bewitching.","He could also see his muscles and physique had improved drastically.","He had reached the 10 kills of the Asura technique. The next stage is 100kill which would take his body to the Superhuman realm.","Just his body skin and flesh alone had advanced but there wasn’t much improvement. Simply because alredy possess a body strengthening technique but it wouldn’t be bad mixing the two together.","Then his physique would be even more terrifying!","***","It was time to cook.","Dexter moved through the morning routine like he done time over again.","He washed his hands, tied his apron, and began preparing breakfast.","He used his heaven and earth herbs as ingredients along with the diamond rice and even went all out and produced his Sun Alcohol with it, cooking them a perfect meal.","By 6:50 AM, the meal was complete. A Grade-4 Arcane meal was ready for them.","He turned back but didn’t see Lyra waiting in the kitchen’s entrance.","Usually, she would hover near the kitchen doorway while he cooked, her eyes tracking every movement.","Today, she hadn’t come near the kitchen.","’ This girl might hold grudges even more than I thought.’","He set the dining table and listened for movement in the hallway.","The girls were already awake. He could hear them shuffling through their morning routine, bathroom doors opening and closing, the sound of running water, the soft rustle of clothes being changed.","One by one, they emerged.","Mira came first, using her spectral arms to wheel herself to the dining table. She was expressionless as usual, didn’t look at Dexter and simply positioned herself at her usual spot and waited.","Selene came next, her bare feet padding softly against the floor. She stopped eating slippers in the house when she noticed she could feel vibration easily without them.","She found her chair by memory and echolocation, sat down gracefully, and placed her hands in her lap.","She didn’t look at Dexter either but for a completely different reason","Lyra appeared last. She walked to the table without a word, sat down, and picked up her spoon.","Her dark eyes were fixed on her bowl. Her AI glasses sat on her nose, their tiny lights blinking.","\"Good morning ,\" she said.","It was devoid of the soft, melodic warmth that usually accompanied her telepathic greetings.","She didn’t project the words into his mind, instead, she typed on her phone and it spoke them aloud.","Dexter smirked at her antics to appear cold and aloof.","Dexter served the meal in silence."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139 | Trying For Forgiveness","paragraphs":["The four of them ate in suffocating quiet.","Just the clinking of spoons against the plate could be heard in the dining room.","Dexter cleared the table when they finished and started tk washed the dishes, listening to the girls disperse throughout the house.","Mira’s wheelchair rolled to the living room window. Selene’s went to the backyard while Lyra’s footsteps retreated to the bedroom.","’I can’t possibly explain to them that I need to kill monsters to increase my cultivation and upgrade my system.’","Dexter sighed as he stood at the kitchen sink, washing the last plate.","’I should probably speak to Lyra first.’","But she hadn’t given him the space to approach her. Every time he came near, she found a reason to leave.","’We’re staying in the same house. She will eventually let it go.’","Dexter shrugged, dried his hands, and went to his room.","He sat on his bed and began cultivating.","The mana flowed into him effortlessly as the ten Star Nodes greedily sucked energy from the surrounding.","But his mind wasn’t truly on cultivation. A few hours into cultivation—","\"Ding-a-ling-a-ling!\"","His alarm rang.","Dexter opened his eyes and checked the time.","It was the alarm he had set for Mira’s daily physical therapy session, the massage routine designed to stretch her muscles, prevent atrophy, and maintain what little function remained in her paralyzed limbs.","Especially for now that she was healing.","’I should move to the next style. Now.’","He stood up, stretched his legs, and headed to the living room.","Mira was at the window, her eyes closed, her spectral arms retracted.","She was cultivating deeply, her Star Nodes pulling in mana with speed.","Dexter walked over and stood behind her wheelchair.","\"It’s time for your massage,\" he said.","\"Hm.\"","Mira didn’t open her eyes, still indifferent as ever and didn’t respond.","Dexter didn’t wait, to ask for permission he had learned that asking Mira for permission only gave her an opportunity to refuse.","Dexter wheeled Mira to the bedroom. She didn’t like the other girls watching as her pride couldn’t bear being vulnerable in front of the other girls.","That was why she preferred to be taken care of by Dexter, rather than the two girls. She might not be able to do anything right now, but she still possess her pride and wasn’t willing to let it fall before the other girls.","Moreover, Dexter was a stranger to her back then so it didn’t count.","Lyra was already in the bedroom, sitting cross-legged on her bed with the ancient beast egg cradled in her lap.","She had taken a particular liking to the egg, always volunteering to cultivate with it despite not being the strongest cultivator among them.","When she saw Dexter wheel Mira through the doorway, she immediately understood what was about to happen. Without a word, she picked up the egg, stood, and left the room.","Dexter closed the door behind her.","He carried Mira from the wheelchair and placed her softly on the bed.","He removed her outer clothing, leaving her in just a sports bra and cotton briefs.","They had done this routine enough times now that Mira’s embarrassment had reduced considerably, though the faint pink tinge on her ears never quite disappeared.","Dexter, however, was a different story. No matter how many times he performed this ritual, his heart always raced.","He inhaled deeply and retrieved the nearly empty bottle of massage oil from the nightstand.","Pouring a small pool of oil into his palm, he warmed it between his hands and began.","The 36-Style Massage Technique activated instinctively, channeling precise threads of mana through his fingertips as he worked.","He started with her fingers, then her hands, her wrists, her forearms.","He moved up to her shoulders, kneading the atrophied muscles with careful, methodical pressure. Her neck followed, then her upper back, his thumbs working the tight bands of tissue along her spine.","He turned his attention to her legs. Starting at her toes, he stretched each one gently, then worked upward her calves, knees and thighs.","He stopped just below the junction of her thighs and waist, then gently turned her over.","The front of her body received the same careful treatment, her abdomen, her collarbones, her arms.","The oil seeped into her pores, carrying its restorative properties deep into her tissue.","When the massage was complete, Dexter lifted her carefully and carried her to the bathroom.","He used warm water and a soft cloth to clean the massage oil from her skin, patting her dry with a fresh towel the took he back to the room.","Then he dressed her in clean clothes.","Mira immediately closed her eyes and resumed cultivating.","She didn’t say a word throughout the entire process—not during the massage, not during the bath, nor after.","Dexter glanced her and smirked. \"I’d thought I’d never see the day the Crimson Valkyrie would be silent.\"","Mira opened her eye and glanced at him. \"Righteous idiot.\" Then she closed her eyes and ignored him.","Dexter almost choked on his own spit. ’ Why was this girl such a savage?’","\" Hmph!\" He snorted and took her to the sitting room, close to the window.","***","Lyra was on the couch, the beast egg back on her lap.","Dexter glanced at her and an idea came to him.","He went to the kitchen and began preparing tea. He went all out, brewed a Grade-4 Arcane tea using the premium leaves and also mixed it with his premium alcohol.","He then retrieved the Celestial Moon Pastries from his storage ring.","He arranged them on small plates and paired each with a cup of the Grade-4 tea.","Mira first.","He carried a cup of tea and three pastries to Mira.","\"I don’t want,\" she said flatly, without opening her eyes.","Dexter smiled. \"Then toss it away if you don’t want.\"","Mira frowned and glanced at him. \"Are you trying to bully me?\"","Dexter grinned brilliantly. \"Then stand up for yourself.\"","Mira’s eyes brow rose at the clever retort. \"Hmph! Glib tongue.\"","She ignored him.","Dexter chuckled and placed the tea before her. She didn’t summon her specter arm to toss it which was quite the achievement.","Next, Lyra.","Dexter carried a cup of tea and four pastries instead of two.","He set the tea and pastries on the small stool directly in front of her.","Lyra opened one eye. She glanced at Dexter, then she closed her eye again, ignoring both him and the food.","Dexter chuckled softly but didn’t press. He placed the items where she could reach them and moved on.","Finally, Selene.","She was in the backyard, sitting on the old hanging swing chair that creaked softly.","Her hands rested on her knees, palms upward, and faint wisps of cold mana drifted around her like morning mist.","Dexter walked over and placed two pastries and a cup of tea on the empty space beside her swing.","Selene’s head turned toward him without opening her eyes. Through her echolocation, she could perceive his outline which was a blazing wild fire in the dark world.","\"This is your cultivation pastry,\" Dexter said quietly. \"It will help improve your cultivation speed. Try it.\"","Selene was silent for a moment. Then she muttered softly, \"Thank you.\"","Dexter smiled. At least one of the three girls had thanked him today.","He turned to leave, but paused when Selene’s mouth opened slightly—as if she wanted to say something more. She hesitated, her lips parting and then closing.","The moment stretched.","Dexter raised an eyebrow but didn’t push. She would say it when she was ready. He simply nodded and walked back inside."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140 | Lyra + Food + Food = Forgiveness!","paragraphs":["Dexter loaded the clean laundry into the heater and activated the drying cycle.","\"Beep!\"","The machine hummed to life as the clothes started to tumble.","As he turned to check the cycle, he saw Lyra walking past him.","She was carrying an empty plate, the one he had give her with pastries in it.","But currently, it was empty and she headed toward the kitchen sink.","She placed it in the sink without looking at him, then turned and walked back past him again.","Suddenly, a soft voice whispered in his mind like a mosquito’s whine.","’ The pastries were good.’","Dexter’s eyebrows raised in surprise and he turned to look at her face.","The anger and coldness which was on her face all morning had already melted away.","The pastries and the Grade-3 Arcane tea seemed to haves worked.","Dexter smiled.","’ They say the way to a man’s heart is through his stomach,’ he thought. ’ But whoever said that clearly never met Lyra.’","\"So you’re finally talking to me,\" Dexter said in a light tone as he teased.","Lyra’s body stiffened. She blinked, then immediately turned to rush back to the living room,","\"Wait,\" Dexter called out.","She stopped but didn’t turn around.","Dexter scratched the back of his head awkwardly. \"I know you’re still angry. And I’m sorry for worrying you. I know you didn’t want me to leave for the monster outbreak yesterday.\" He paused, choosing his words carefully. \"But I had to go. Not just for the Association—I had personal reasons too. If I don’t grow stronger, I won’t be able to protect us. And the resources I need to grow stronger... I can only get them by fighting.\"","Lyra stood motionless with her back turned to him. Several long seconds passed.","Then, her soft, melodic voice echoed inside his mind.","’I know .’","Dexter blinked, frowning slightly. \"So why are you still angry?\"","Lyra remained silent for a while as her fist clenched tightly. Her tone thick with accusation as she spoke.","’ You promised to come back safely. But you came back covered in blood instead. You broke your promise.’","Dexter was momentarily stunned.","’ That was why she was angry?’","She wasn’t mad that he had chosen the Hero Association over staying home.","She was mad because he had ’promised’ to come back safely, and he hadn’t.","He had broken his word. And to Lyra, who had already been abandoned by everyone she had ever depended on, a broken promise was just as bad as a betrayal.","’ And Selene almost died. If you hadn’t come back when you did...’","Dexter remained silent. She was right of course.","He had promised to come back safely, and he hadn’t. And in his excitement and urgency, he had forgotten to inject Selene’s suppressant serum before leaving.","Both failures were his. Both were avoidable. And both had been witnessed by three women who had already lost everything once and couldn’t bear to lose again.","Lyra shook her head, her expression closing off again. ’ Forget it. It doesn’t matter.’","She turned to leave.","\"It matters a lot.\"","Dexter’s voice was quiet but firm. Lyra stopped.","\"It matters a lot, Lyra,\" he took a step closer.","\"I can’t change what happened. But I can tell you that I’m sorry and I promise to keep my promise to you. Next time, I will come back safely.\"","Lyra stood frozen for a long moment.","Then, slowly, her shoulders dropped. The rigid tension in her spine softened. She turned her head slightly, just enough to glance at him from the corner of her eye.","’Promise?’ her mental voice asked. It was small, stripped of all its usual composure, sounding almost childlike in its vulnerability.","Dexter nodded as he thumped his chest. \"Promise.\"","She turned even more as she faced Dexter and stared into his eyes.","There was silence for a few seconds and then Lyra lips curled up to a small smile.","Her dark soul-consuming eyes started to light up as she returned to the usual expression. She blinked and stared at Dexter.","Dexter immediately knew she had forgiven him and when he saw her expectant gaze.","Dexter couldn’t help it. He laughed.","He flipped his right hand, and golden light flashed as four Celestial Moon Pastries materialized in his palm.","He had planned to give her two, but seeing the look in her eyes, he added two more.","Lyra’s eyes widened as her pupils dilated.","Her mouth fell open slightly, and for a moment, she looked like a child who had just been handed the keys to a candy store.","In a flash, she reached out and took the pastries from his hand with both hands, cradling them against her chest like precious treasures.","Then, without another word, she turned and practically ’skipped’ away down the hallway,","’Thank you!’ her siren voice echoed in his mind.","Dexter chuckled as he watched her disappear around the corner. He shook his head, still smiling.","He had known Lyra wouldn’t stay mad at him for long. She was a foodie through and through.","’Jasmine was like that too,’ a thought surfaced unbidden in his mind.","The name hit him like a soft punch to the chest.","Jasmine Constance. His ex-girlfriend.","Another foodie with an almost bottomless appetite and a smile that could light up a room.","The parallels between Jasmine and Lyra were uncanny—both quiet, both emotionally guarded, both absolutely ravenous when it came to exceptional food.","A warm, bittersweet feeling bloomed in Dexter’s chest. The memories of Jasmine—both the good and the painful—rose to the surface of his mind like bubbles in still water.","He let them linger for a moment, acknowledging them without drowning in them.","Then, deliberately, he pushed them to the back of his mind.","He wasn’t going to think about Jasmine. Not now. Not when he had three wives who needed him. Dwelling on the past would only complicate the present, and the present was already complicated enough.","He turned back to the drying machine and checked the cycle."]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141 | Holding A Grudge","paragraphs":["That left Mira.","Lyra was handled. Selene had never truly been angry to begin with, just embarrassed about the midnight clinging incident. But Mira was a different creature entirely.","Dexter leaned against the kitchen counter, rubbing his jaw in thought. Mira was... complicated.","One moment she was laughing in the rain, the next she was glaring at him. He couldn’t tell when she was genuinely angry versus when she was simply maintaining her pride.","He knew one thing for certain: she liked rain.","He glanced out the kitchen window. The sky was clear. Pale blue, not a cloud in sight. No indication of rain anytime soon.","So that plan was out.","He needed another approach. But what?","He stood there for a long time, staring out the window, his mind turning over possibilities.","He thought about the wheelchair incident. He had bought her a $120,000 neural-linked wheelchair, and she had been furious. Not because the gift was unwelcome, but because she liked the routine. She liked ’him’ taking care of her and she had rejected it because the machine wasn’t him.","Dexter massaged his brows as a headache started to form.","The drying machine beeped, signaling the end of its cycle. Dexter pushed off the counter and began folding the warm laundry.","[Ding!]","[Investment Return Detected: Improved Lyra’s Emotional State & Reduced Shadow Corruption]","[Multiplier: 100x]","[Rewards Granted:]","1. Grade-3 Divine Peak Recovery Pill ×1","2. 10 kg Premium Diamond Spirit Rice","Dexter didn’t even check the rewards fully. His attention was caught by two words in the notification: Reduced Shadow Corruption.","He frowned, pulling up Lyra’s status panel. His eyes widened in shock.","Her shadow corruption, which he had diligently reduced to a mere 1% through weeks of spiritual meals, had somehow skyrocketed to 10%. According to the system, his recent actions had reduced it back down to 5%, but the damage had already been done.","’How did it increase so fast?’","Then, it hit him. She had been angry at him. She had spent almost twenty-four hours furious, radiating dark, gloomy, and resentful emotions.","Because Lyra was finally starting to experience genuine emotions again after years of numbness, her negative feelings directly fueled her Shadow Manipulation talent.","And when those negative emotions spiraled, the shadow mana turned inward, corrupting her physical cells.","Dexter broke into a cold sweat. If just one day of anger had increased the corruption by 10%, it would only take ten days of sustained misery for the corruption to reach 100%. At 100%, her body would collapse and become a permanent portal to the Shadow Realm, unleashing horrific monsters into the physical world and killing her instantly.","He had never considered that emotional distress could be so lethal to her. All this time, she had been living in a state of emotional numbness, which was why the corruption had remained stagnant. Now that she was healing and feeling again, her anger was a ticking time bomb.","Dexter rubbed his forehead, realizing he would have to check the girls’ status panels every single day to prevent any unexpected surprises. If he had missed this, Lyra could have died without him even realizing why.","He looked at the Grade-3 Divine Peak Recovery Pill. Just like the one he received for Selene, it could temporarily heal all injuries and return her to her peak Ultra Realm form for six hours, but at the cost of permanently worsening her injuries afterward.","He firmly decided not to give the girls these pills. It was better to take the long, slow road to recovery than to let them risk everything for six hours of fleeting normalcy. He secured the pill deep within his storage ring, making a mental note to never reveal their existence to the girls unless absolutely necessary.","’’’","Lunch was a quiet affair, though noticeably lighter than the morning. Lyra sat at the table, happily eating her meal with one hand while cradling the ancient beast egg in her other arm. She finished six massive portions in under ten minutes.","Dexter shook his head in amazement.","’Where does all that food go?’ he thought, baffled. ’Is she secretly feeding the entire Shadow Realm?’","As she stood up to leave, his eyes inadvertently dropped to her chest. He blinked. Her chest had grown even larger since she started eating his arcane meals.","He quickly averted his gaze before she could catch him staring.","’Thank you,’ Lyra’s sweet voice chimed in his mind, her mood completely restored. She skipped out of the kitchen, leaving Mira and Selene to eat in silence before they too returned to cultivating.","As for the Hero Association’s message, Dexter decided to delay his response until tomorrow. The girls were still highly sensitive about anything related to dungeon outbreaks, and he didn’t want to trigger their trauma by announcing he had to report to the Association today. He would handle it in the morning.","’’’","Evening came, and after dinner, Dexter suddenly grabbed Mira’s wheelchair and began wheeling her toward the bedroom.","Mira squinted her eyes. \"What do you want?\"","Dexter prepared the bed and pulled out the massage oil. \"I’ve decided to increase the duration of your massage therapy to twice a day now. The results should accelerate with this routine.\"","Mira’s face remained indifferent, but her crimson eyes narrowed. \"Are you just looking for an excuse to touch my body?\"","Dexter rolled his eyes. \"Yes, Mira. I desperately wish to touch your supple skin. Please, let me have my way with you.\"","Mira glanced at him from the corner of her eye. \"Hmph!\"","She harrumphed coldly and closed her eyes, submitting to the massage without further protest.","Dexter took her to the bed and began the 36-Style Massage Technique. Halfway through, as he worked on the muscles below her waist, he decided to test the waters.","\"So, Lyra has forgiven me,\" he said casually.","Mira said nothing.","Dexter blinked, waiting for a sharp retort, but none came. \"When are you going to let it go?\"","Still nothing.","\"If you don’t say anything, I will stop the massage,\" he threatened lightly.","Mira’s head shifted slightly. Despite her silence, he knew she loved the massage and the relief it brought her.","\"Do what you want,\" Mira replied coldly.","Dexter sighed and resumed the massage. He couldn’t actually use her physical recovery as leverage to force her forgiveness. That would be cruel.","When he was done, he carried her to the bathroom, cleaned the oil off her body, and dressed her in her pajamas. Specifically, he dressed her in the flower-print pajamas he had bought for her—the ones she absolutely despised.","Instead of returning her to her wheelchair, however, he locked the wheels and crossed his arms in front of her.","Mira glanced at him suspiciously. \"What do you want to do now?\"","Dexter blinked innocently. \"Why do you think I want to do anything?\"","Mira sneered. \"You are very devious. Of course you want to do something. What is it?\"","Dexter smirked. \"Alright, since you know I’m devious... you are not leaving this bathroom until you forgive me.\"","Mira frowned, her crimson eyes blazing. Then, without a word, she simply closed her eyes and started cultivating.","Dexter stood there, utterly stunned. She would rather cultivate in the bathroom than say the words ’I forgive you’. She truly held a grudge of iron.","He stood there patiently for almost fifteen minutes. Finally, Mira opened her eyes, her brows furrowed in irritation.","\"This is bullying,\" she snapped. \"If people find out you are bullying your crippled wife in the bathroom, do you know what they will say?\"","Dexter grinned. \"Luckily, there’s no one here to find out.\"","Mira’s lips curled into a dangerous smile. \"I can simply scream ’pervert,’ and the whole neighborhood will come rushing in, right?\"","Dexter blinked, momentarily stunned, before his grin widened. \"I placed a Grade-6 formation matrix around the house. Unless I wish it, no one below the Transcendent Realm can come in.\"","Mira was startled. ’A formation?’ This guy actually possessed the connections to purchase a barrier formation capable of repelling Transcendent experts?","She smirked, refusing to be outplayed. \"What about Selene and Lyra? They’re in the house. They’d think you’re doing something to me.\"","\"Hm,\" Dexter hummed thoughtfully. \"Let them think that. They’d probably just assume it’s a normal activity between husband and wife.\"","Mira glared at him, her face flushing slightly. \"Pervert! Who is doing husband-and-wife activities with you!?\"","She looked away, her jaw tight. Dexter laughed and waited.","He could see the battle happening behind her eyes—her stubborn pride fighting against the absurd, somewhat amusing reality of being held hostage in the bathroom over a grudge.","Finally, she let out a sharp exhale. \"Fine! I’ve forgiven you. Happy?\"","Dexter smiled brilliantly and clapped his hands together. \"See? That was so simple!\"","He laughed out loud as he unlocked her wheelchair, spinning her around and wheeling her out of the bathroom toward the bedroom.","Behind him, Mira muttered under her breath, \"Devious bastard.\""]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142 | Eccentric Old Lady Lucy","paragraphs":["The next morning, Dexter sorted through his routine.","He woke early, cooked breakfast for the girls, took care of Mira’s morning needs, and served the meal at the dining table.","If it were another person, they would have gotten tired a long while ago. Even a good person would have definitely complained after a while.","But Dexter was happy to do these chores everyday. Who knows if he’s starting to develop something for the girls, or maybe it’s purely transactional and he looked forward to the investment returns from the system.","Halfway through breakfast, he suddenly asked, \"How would you all feel about renovating the house?\"","He leaned back in his chair. \"I’ve saved up quite a bit of money. I think it’s about time we fixed this place up properly.\"","Lyra and Selene both looked up from their meals.","Mira, meanwhile, remained completely focused on her breakfast.","She calmly used her Spectral Arms to scoop food from her plate, eating without reacting as though Dexter hadn’t said anything.","Selene glanced around the house before speaking softly. \"...I don’t think there’s anything wrong with it.\"","Lyra nodded in agreement. ’... Mm .’","Dexter pursed his lips. He understood their reluctance. The idea of strangers stomping and entering the house, disturbing their peace, they probably hated it.","Just like when those people came in to arrange the new beds, they hated it. Now if others came once more, especially since they would take more time during the repair, they might hate ie even more.","But the house needed work.","The wallpaper in several rooms had peeled away, exposing bare plaster.","The bathroom wall had cracked during Mira’s outbreak, and the mirror had shattered.","The front porch gate was rusted and the swing chair in the backyard was also rusty and its wooden slats splintering.","The kitchen roof had developed a slow leak that dripped into a bucket he had strategically placed during the last rainstorm.","And the exterior walls which had been originally painted a clean cream color had faded to a muddy, dull brown that made the bungalow look abandoned.","The Hero Association had repaired the structural damage from the monster outbreak, and hadn’t bothered with rest.","Dexter nodded slowly. \"Okay. I won’t call anyone for renovations. I guess I’ll have to do it myself.\"","Selene slowly nodded. Lyra blinked her eyes glanced curiously at Dexter and then nodded before returning her attention to her food.","Still, Mira still hadn’t said anything.","Dexter shrugged, a faint smile tugging on his lips n at his lips as he recalled the events of the previous night.","After breakfast, the girls retreated to their bedroom to cultivate, arranging themselves in a loose circle around the ancient beast egg, which sat at the center like a shrine.","They cultivated in unison. The Grand Cosmos Scripture activated simultaneously in three bodies, each one drawing mana through their awakened Star Nodes rather than their shattered meridians.","Mana surged toward the bungalow from every direction, invisible currents of energy converging on the small house like rivers feeding into a lake.","The Mana Hurricane phenomenon began again.","The ancient beast egg absorbed its share of the mana, its surface glowing faintly with a warm, golden pulse that had grown steadily brighter over the past few days.","The three girls absorbed their own mana simultaneously, their Star Nodes drinking greedily from the hurricane they had created.","•••","Dexter stood in the kitchen, staring at the notification on his Type-3 Arcane phone. It was another message from the Hero Association—a reminder this time.","> ’[Reminder: Promotion Processing]’",">","> Hero Dexter Ashford, this is a second notification regarding your approved promotion. You are required to report to your nearest Hero Association branch within twenty-four hours to complete your promotion procedures.",">","> Failure to report may result in suspension of your hero license and associated benefits.",">","> Please confirm your intended arrival time.","’Suspension? Aren’t this guys ruthless?’","Dexter frowned and then pocketed the phone.","\"Will go later.\"","For now, he needed to stay home, partly to keep an eye on the girls after yesterday’s near-disaster with Selene, and partly because he wasn’t ready to leave them again so soon after reconciling.","He finished washing the breakfast dishes, dried them, and placed them in the cabinet.","He wiped down the counter, swept the kitchen floor, and checked the leak in the kitchen ceiling and it was actually still dripping slowly into the bucket. He made a mental note to fix it as part of his renovation plan.","Then he gathered the trash, food scraps, packaging, the empty syringe from the empty serum he’d used on Selene—and carried the dustbin outside to the curb.","The morning air was cool and fresh. The street was quiet, most of the neighbors already at work.","A few birds chirped from the power lines.","The sunlight was pale but pleasant, casting long shadows from the houses across the street.","Dexter placed the dirt in the trash can ans as Dexter was about to turn back toward his gate, his eyes caught movement across the road.","Old Lady Lucy.","The old lady who lives in the house directly opposite his bungalow.","Her gate was open, and she was tending to her front yard, mowing the small patch of grass with a manual push mower.","Dexter had greeted her once before and she had responded with a curt nod and immediately returned to her gardening without a word.","She was eccentric—sometimes acknowledging him, other times pretending he didn’t exist. He had learned not to take it personally.","This morning, he decided not to greet her. Better to avoid the awkwardness of being ignored.","He turned toward his gate.","Then, from the corner of his eye, he saw movement. The old woman had stopped gardening.","She was looking directly at him.","Then, to his surprise...","She raised a hand and waved.","Dexter blinked.","\"...Me?\"","The old woman nodded gently before waving again.","Surprised, Dexter raised his own hand and waved back.","A faint smile spread across the old woman’s wrinkled face. She slowly lifted a finger and curled it twice, gesturing for him to come over.","Dexter paused.","His gaze lingered on the white-haired old woman standing quietly among the colorful flowers.","Should I go?"]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143 | Business Shaping Up","paragraphs":["’Should I go?’","Dexter hesitated for several seconds before shaking his head.","’Well... it won’t hurt to find out.’","Dexter crossed the street toward the old woman’s gate.","She was a small, white-haired woman with her pale blue eyes. Up close, she looked to be in her seventies, but her posture was straight and she behaved younger than her age.","\"You must be Dexter,\" the old woman said, smiling warmly. \"I’m Lucy.\"","\"Good morning, you must be Old Lady Lucy\" Dexter replied politely.","\"Ah, Seems like Tessa has told you about me,\" Lucy said, her eyes crinkling at the corners.","\"How are you finding the neighborhood? Hope there’s no problem like the previous time?\"","Dexter shook his head. \"Apart from the monster outbreak, everything’s been fine.\"","Lucy nodded thoughtfully. \"All right. These things happen.\" She paused, wiping her hands on her apron. \"Oh, Tessa informed me that you’re an Arcane Chef. Is that true?\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow, glancing at the old woman. He slowly nodded. \"Yes. I am.\"","Lucy’s smile widened. \"Tessa also said you two are planning to go into business together. Selling food at her father’s bakery.\"","She chuckled softly. \"It’s a really nice idea, actually. A really nice idea.\"","Dexter frowned slightly.","Tessa had only mentioned the business idea once. He had assumed she was joking. But it seemed she was serious. And now that the old woman across the street knew about it, the idea had clearly gained momentum.","Moreover, Dexter had to admit he needed a platform. He couldn’t just set up a stall on a random street corner and start selling Arcane meals.","The bakery was an already established business with loyal customer base, and a reputation in the neighborhood. It was the perfect testing ground.","\"When are you starting?\" Lucy asked, her pale blue eyes curious.","Dexter rubbed the back of his neck. \"I plan on doing the business, but not today. Definitely this week, but not today.\"","Lucy nodded. \"Tessa hasn’t stopped praising your cooking,\" she said, laughing softly. \"Now you’ve made me curious. I wonder just how delicious your food really is.\"","Dexter chuckled. \"When we finally open, I’ll prepare a portion for you. My treat. You’ll be the first customer.\"","Lucy’s eyes softened, a gentle warmth replacing her sharp eyes. \"Thank you, Dexter. It’s been a long time since someone spoiled this old woman.\"","Dexter smiled. \"You’re welcome.\"","After exchanging another goodbye, he turned and walked back toward his house.","As he pushed it open, a familiar voice drifted down from above.","\"Hey, Dexter.\"","He looked up. Tessa was sitting on the wall again, her red hair tied back with a strip of cloth as her green eyes brightened with mischief.","Dexter rolled his eyes. \"You’re in trouble, Tessa.\"","Tessa blinked widened, her freckled face expressing false innocence. \"What did I do this time?\"","Dexter furrowed his brows. \"First of all, today’s Wednesday. Why aren’t you in school this morning? And don’t tell me you’re on a break.\"","Tessa’s eyes rolled around rapidly and then her eyes lit up ws she spoke.","\"Um, we were supposed to go for an excursion today, but my dad doesn’t have money to pay for such an expensive excursion. So I decided to stay at home.\" She smiled brightly.","Dexter stared at her for a long moment, then nodded. \"That’s a believable excuse.\"","Tessa puffed out her cheeks indignantly. \"It’s not an excuse. It’s the truth!\"","Dexter rolled his eyes. He knew she wasn’t going to tell him the real reason, and he definitely knew she wasn’t going to school. He decided to drop the matter.","\"Second,\" he said, turning to face her fully with his arms crossed. \"You only told me about the idea of going into business together. You never told me you’d already implemented a full-blown plan.\"","Tessa’s smile widened into a grin. \"Oh, I forgot to tell you.\" She swung her legs casually. \"I wanted to tell you, but I didn’t know how to approach you after coming into your home the last time. I thought you might be angry that I entered without your permission.\"","Dexter remained silent for a moment, his expression unreadable.","Tessa, reading the disapproval on his face, scratched her head awkwardly. \"Look, it’s actually a simple business plan,\" she continued quickly. \"I feel we should test the waters by making twenty portions first. Twenty portions of whatever food you want to make. Then we see how the twenty portions go. If they sell well, we can decide whether to increase or reduce the daily portions for selling at the bakery.\"","Dexter uncrossed his arms. He considered the plan and felt it was feasible.","Twenty portions was a manageable number he could cook that in an hour to two hours with his Great Grandmaster Foodsmith skills.","And if each portion sold for even five thousand dollars. the same price the Akane Restaurant charged for a Grade-One meal—twenty portions would generate one hundred thousand dollars in a single day.","The numbers were insane!","And that was just ghe conservative estimate.","If his Grade-Two or Grade-Three meals commanded higher prices—and they should, given their vastly superior quality and taste the revenue could be even greater.","\"Fine,\" Dexter said. \"But we start small. Twenty portions. Grade-One meals only.\"","Tessa’s eyes lit up. \"Really? You’re in?\"","\"I’m in.\"","Tessa practically bounced on the wall. \"Yes! Okay, so when do we start? Tomorrow? Today? Right now?\"","Dexter held up a hand. \"Not today. I have somethings to do and certainly not tomorrow. Let’s start the day after. That gives me time to prepare ingredients and figure out the logistics.\"","Tessa nodded rapidly, her red ponytail bouncing. \"Day after tomorrow. Got it. I’ll tell Dad to clear a space in the bakery for a food counter.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Good.\"","Tessa nodded her head and then spoke. \" I assume you don’t have containers to place the food in.\"","\"","Dexter shook his head. \"No, I plan on purchasing those at the market.\"","\"We have a few,\" Tessa said, swinging her legs. \"My dad bought extra this week. Maybe you can use some to pack the food inside.\"","Dexter pursed his lips, looking at her. After a moment, he shrugged. \"Alright then. I assume you’ll be either at the bakery or at home?\"","Tessa nodded her head like a chicken pecking grain. \"Yep!\"","Dexter glanced at her, a fleeting thought crossing his mind—why did she never have any friends over? She was always alone, on the wall, in the bakery, or playing chess with old Grandma Lucy. But it wasn’t any of his business.","He waved at her. \"I’ll see you later.\"","He turned and walked back into his house.","After washing his hands, he changed into clean clothes, a dark shirt and joggers, and slipped on proper shoes.","He walked to the living room where Lyra was sprawled on the couch, the beast egg cradled in her lap.","\"I’m heading out to get some things for the renovation,\" he announced."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144 | Promotion: D-Rank Hero","paragraphs":["Dexter walked to the backyard. Selene was on the old swing chair with her eyes closed in cultivation.","\"Selene, I’m heading out to purchase some things at the market.\"","She looked up from the swing, her echolocation mapping his outline. \"...Okay.\"","Dexter nodded and headed back inside. He walked to the living room. Where Lyra was seated on the couch and Mira was at the window.","\"I’m heading out.\"","Dexter said announces to then.","’Take care, Dexter,’ Lyra’s soft, melodic voice echoed in his mind.","Dexter smiled at her. \"I will.\"","Then he turned to face Mira.","Mira opened her eyes. She looked at him with a flat expression.","\"Okay,\" she said. Then, without changing her expression, she added: \"Tell the fourth wife we said ’hi’.\"","Dexter almost choked on his own spit. \"Fourth wife? What fourth wife?\"","Mira simply sneered, closed her eyes, and resumed cultivating.","Dexter felt Lyra’s gaze on him from the couch.","He turned and saw her looking up at him through her AI glasses, her dark eyes narrow with suspicion.","He coughed awkwardly. \"Don’t mind her. She just likes stirring up trouble.\"","Lyra blinked and looked at him suspiciously before slowly nodding her head.","Dexter glared at Mira who sat there with that infuriating ghost of a smile on her lips as he opened the door and left.","•••","Dexter took the Tier-6 car and drove out of the neighborhood. But he wasn’t actually heading to the supermarket.","He was going to the Hero Association.","Since he was heading to get somethings, he might as well finsh all his task today.l instead of postponing it till tomorrow.","The drive took about fifteen minutes.","The familiar fortress-like structure of the Hero Association Branch soon loomed into view. It was just as majestic and intimidating as the first time Rachel had brought him here.","He pulled up to the main gate and lowered his window.","\"Identificarion Please?\"","The guard leaned forward, scanning the golden identification card Dexter held out.","The guard’s posture changed instantly. He snapped to attention, his fist slamming against his chest in a sharp salute.","\"Welcome, Mr. Dexter! Have a great day, sir!\"","Dexter nodded politely, rolled up the window, and drove through the gate.","He parked in the visitor lot, killed the engine, and walked toward the administration center.","The main hall was as enormous as he remembered, hundreds of heroes moving through the place. He approached the reception counter, where a young woman with glasses and a professional smile sat behind a sleek terminal.","\"I’m here for my promotion,\" Dexter said. \"Dexter Ashford.\"","The receptionist offered him a courteous smile. \"One moment, please.\"","She lowered her gaze and began typing rapidly on her terminal.","A few seconds passed. Then her expression changed slightly as her smile became more genuine and less forced.","She looked back up at Dexter.","\"Mr. Dexter, we’ve been expecting you.\" She straightened in her chair. \"You’ve been scheduled for the twentieth floor. Please take the elevator at the end of the corridor.\" She gestured toward a hallway on the left.","\"Someone will be waiting to receive you.\"","\"Thank you,\" Dexter said, keeping his expression neutral.","He walked down the indicated corridor and at the end of the corridor, a sleek elevator waited with its doors already open.","He stepped inside. The doors closed with a soft hiss and he pushed the button marked ’20’.","A few seconds later.","\"Ding!\"","The elevator chimed.","’Floor 20.’","The doors slid open.","The elevator doors opened on the twentieth floor, and Dexter stepped out into a wide, elegantly furnished corridor.","A middle-aged man was standing directly in front of the elevator, waiting. He was dressed in a sharp grey suit, his hair neatly combed, his posture straight and professional. He smiled warmly as Dexter stepped forward.","\"Mr. Dexter?\"","Dexter nodded.","The man immediately extended his hand. \"It’s a pleasure to finally meet you. My name is Simon. I’m one of the administrative supervisors here.\"","Dexter shook his hand. \"The pleasure is mine.\"","Simon’s smile widened. \"Supervisor Stan has spoken very highly of you.\"","Dexter’s brows furrowed slightly as he searched his memory. Stan... then it clicked.","Supervisor Stan the senior official who had accompanied Rachel during the dungeon outbreak investigation and had quietly arranged for Dexter to receive a substantial payout.","\"Ah, Supervisor Stan,\" Dexter said, nodding. \"I remember him.\"","Simon gestured down the corridor. \"Please follow me.\"","He led Dexter to a massive corner office nearby.","The room was impressive floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the entire Hero Association compound, a polished mahogany desk, leather chairs, and bookshelves.","Simon gestured for Dexter to sit. Dexter settled into a comfortable leather chair opposite the desk while Simon took his own seat on the other side.","Simon folded his hands on the desk and leaned forward slightly.","\"First of all,\" he began, his tone formal but warm, \"on behalf of the Hero Association, I’d like to sincerely thank you for your contribution during the monster outbreak at Stonebridge Market District.\"","Dexter gave a small nod. \"It was my duty.\"","Simon continued. \"When the dimensional gate first appeared, it was classified as an E-Rank Gate. However, after further investigation, we have officially upgraded the incident to a C-Rank Monster Outbreak.\"","He paused, letting the weight of that classification settle.","\"Initially, we considered classifying it as a B-Rank outbreak. However, the total number of Ultra-Class monsters that emerged was fewer than ten. According to Hero Association regulations, that places the incident within the C-Rank category.\"","He slid a document across the desk. Dexter glanced at it—a detailed after-action report with his name, contribution summary, and combat assessment.","\"Taking your performance into account,\" Simon said, \"the Association has unanimously approved your promotion. You will be promoted from F-Rank directly to D-Rank Hero.\"","He paused again, a faint smile touching his lips.","\"In addition... you will retain your Gold Privilege status.\"","Dexter’s eyebrows rose. \"Since it’s a C rank outbreak which I participated in, should I not receive a C rank License?\"","Simon nodded, clearly anticipating the question. \"Ordinarily, yes. You would have received a C-Rank license, given that you participated in clearing a C-Rank outbreak. However, there’s a complication.\"","He leaned back in his chair.","\"Your Gold Privilege is extremely valuable. It’s a status reserved for rookies whose evaluated potential places them in the top percentile of their registration cohort. If we promoted you directly to C-Rank, your privilege tier would automatically reset under Association regulations. You would lose your Gold status and revert to Iron Privilege until you rebuilt your record through additional C-Rank dungeon clears.\"","Simon spread his hands.","\"We felt that would unduly penalize you and undervalue your actual combat ability. The board engaged in considerable discussion before reaching a consensus. It was decided that maintaining your Gold Privilege as a D-Rank Hero would serve you and the Association far better than a standard C-Rank license with Iron Privilege.\"","He tapped the document.","\"A Gold D-Rank Hero receives significantly more benefits than an ordinary C-Rank Hero. Higher mission priority, better dungeon invitations, access to premium equipment stores, increased stipend, and priority for emergency response opportunities.\"","Dexter considered this for a moment. It doesn’t sound half bad. As long as the pay and benefits were better, he didn’t particularly care what letter was printed on his card.","He nodded. \"That’s acceptable.\"","Simon smiled. \"Good.\" He then asked, \"May I have your current license card, please?\"","Dexter reached into his pocket and produced his golden F-Rank Hero identification card. He handed it across the desk.","Simon examined the card briefly, then snapped his fingers. A side door opened, and a young, very pretty woman stepped into the office.",",She carried a tablet and smiled pleasantly.","\"What can I do for you, Mr. Simon?\""]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145 | Rachel!","paragraphs":["A side door opened, and a young and incredibly beautiful woman stepped in, carrying a tablet and smiled.","\"What can I do for you, Mr. Simon?\"","Simon glanced at her indifferently and handed her the card. \"Please upgrade this card to D-Rank. Maintain Gold Privilege status.\"","\"Certainly.\" The secretary took the card, smiled at Simon and then swayed her hips as she disappeared back through the side door.","Simon turned back to Dexter. \"Now, regarding the monster corpses from the outbreak...\"","Dexter’s ears perked up. This was the part he cared about most.","\"Sadly,\" Simon continued, his expression apologetic, \"most of the resources recovered from the monster corpses have already been allocated. The funds earned from processing the carcasses have been directed toward repairing and renovating the Stonebridge Market District, which suffered extensive structural damage during the outbreak.\"","Dexter’s expression remained neutral, though he rolled his eyes.","’ He should be talking about the mall Aurora and the Six-arm goblin king had destroyed.’","\"Also, some had been distributed towards falling heroes families and also civilians families too.\"","\"However,\" Simon added, raising a finger, \"you are not leaving empty-handed.\"","Dexter’s eyes lit up.","\"The Association will transfer your combat bonus directly to your registered bank account. This includes your standard outbreak participation pay, your per-kill bounty for each verified monster you eliminated, and a special hazard bonus for engaging Ultra-Class opponents above your registered rank.\"","Simon consulted a document on his desk.","\"Additionally, your monthly salary has been adjusted to reflect your new D-Rank status. Although you’ve already received this month’s salary at your previous rate, the difference will be calculated and added to your next payment. Your benefits package has also been upgraded—you now have access to the Association’s premium medical coverage, discounted equipment purchases, and priority dungeon scheduling.\"","Dexter nodded, mentally calculating.","Between the combat bonus, the kill bounties, the hazard pay, and the salary adjustment, he was looking at a substantial influx of dollars.","\"One more thing,\" Simon said, leaning forward with a more personal expression.","\"Yesterday, several heroes who participated in the outbreak came forward. They pointed out some things to my attention.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","\"They said you saved them,\" Simon said simply. \"They said you are the reason they are still alive. Some of them wished to get your contact information—your phone number, your address. I informed them that I cannot distribute a hero’s personal information without their explicit permission.\"","He paused.","\"But they were quite... adamant... about thanking you. One of them was the hero named Plasmatic. He was particularly insistent.\"","Simon smiled.","\"So I would like your permission. May I share your contact information with the heroes who requested it? I will screen the list and only provide it to verified, licensed heroes with clean records.\"","Dexter thought about it for a moment.","Having contacts within the hero community could be useful—both for future dungeon raids and for potential emergencies.","Plasmatic, in particular, was someone worth staying in touch with. His long-range firepower complemented Dexter’s close-combat style perfectly.","\"Yes,\" Dexter said. \"You can give them only my number. But only those i fought with in the battlefield .\"","Simon nodded, making a note. \"I’ll have the list sent to your phone by end of day. You’ll be able to review it and approve each individual.\"","Then Simon paused. He stroked his beard thoughtfully and leaned back in his chair.","\"There was... one more person who asked for your contact information.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"Who?\"","Simon met his gaze as he looked at him strangely. There was an hint of surprise in his face as he spoke.","\"Aurora.\"","Dexter frowned.","Aurora. The S-rank hero. The woman with the Sky Manipulation talent who had single-handedly killed the Six-Armed Goblin King and destroyed the dungeon core.","\"Aurora?\" Dexter repeated slowly.","Simon nodded with a smile, as if he couldn’t quite believe it himself.","Dexter’s frown deepened. \"Why does she want my contact information?\"","Simon shrugged, spreading his hands. \"Beats me. I have no idea. She simply gave no reason and asked.\"","Dexter continued frowning. Aurora was an S-rank hero, one of the most powerful and influential young heroes in the entire city.","Having a connection with someone at that level could be good but it could also lead to complications.","And frankly, he hadn’t forgotten the way she had looked at him.","The cold, dismissive gaze didn’t exactly inspire a desire to exchange phone numbers.","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"There’s no need for that.\"","Simon blinked. \"I’m sorry?\"","\"I don’t want you to give out my contact information to Aurora,\" Dexter said flatly.","Simon stared at him with a stunned look.","\"I’m certain I’m not hearing that right.\"","Simon said carefully, leaning forward. \"I said... ’Aurora’ wants your contact information. Aurora. The current generation S-rank hero.\"","Dexter nodded calmly. \"I know. I heard you. But I don’t want you to give out my contact information to her.\"","Simon sat back in his chair, genuinely stunned.","Aurora has always kept to herself. The fact that she had proactively, asked ’Dexter’s’ contact information meant she had deemed him important or worth her time.","And now Dexter was rejecting her.","It was really shocking.","Simon opened his mouth to say something but the look in Dexter’s eyes stopped him.","Simon closed his mouth. He nodded slowly, making a final note on his document.","\"Very well,\" he said, his voice carefully neutral. \"I will inform Hero Aurora that her request was declined.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Thank you.\"","At that moment, the side door opened, and the secretary walked in.","She carried a small velvet tray with a sleek golden card resting on top, along with a folder of documents. She presented them to Simon with a professional smile.","\"Your card and documents, sir.\"","Simon took the tray and turned to Dexter. He picked up the golden card and held it out across the desk.","\"Here is your new license. D-Rank, Gold Privilege.\"","Dexter took the card. It was heavier than his previous one.","Simon also handed him the folder. \"These are your upgraded documents, your new rights, responsibilities, codes of conduct, and operational guidelines. Please read through them carefully. As a D-Rank Hero, you represent the Hero Association in a more visible capacity than before. Your actions will be scrutinized more closely, and your responsibilities will increase accordingly.\"","Dexter nodded, tucking the card into his pocket and the folder under his arm. \"All right.\"","Simon stood, extending his hand across the desk. Dexter rose and shook it.","\"Take care, Mr. Dexter,\" Simon said. \"And congratulations again.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Take care as well.\"","Dexter left the office and walked down the corridor, toward the elevator.","The doors opened and he stepped inside and pressed the ground floor.","As the elevator descended, Dexter pulled out his new D-Rank card one more time, turning it over in his fingers. It looked more premium than last one.","\"Ding!\"","He slipped the card back into his pocket as the elevator chimed, announcing his arrival at the ground floor.","The doors slid open.","Dexter stepped out... he froze.","Outside, an incredibly beautiful woman was standing directly in front of the elevator, smiling at him.","She wore a fitted white blazer over a dark blouse and her posture was confident, and her smile was astonishingly striking to say the least.","The woman was Rachel..."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146 | Just Friends, Nothing Else...","paragraphs":["Dexter blinked, momentarily caught off guard. \"Rachel?\"","Her smile widened briefly—then shifted into an exaggerated pout.","\"Dexter,\" she said, her voice carrying a teasing edge. \"You came to the Hero Association and didn’t inform me?\" She placed a hand on her chest. \"I’m slightly hurt by that.\"","Dexter scratched the back of his head awkwardly. \"I wasn’t coming here for anything related to your department. I only came to receive my promotion. That’s why I didn’t visit.\"","Rachel’s pout softened into a genuine smile. \"Yes, I heard about your feat. They said you fought alongside Aurora, Kinetic Man, and Bullet Spear Man during the outbreak.\" Her green eyes widened with interest. \"It must have been quite the scene, right?\"","Dexter nodded modestly. \"It was quite all right. I only assisted a bit.\"","Rachel laughed softly, shaking her head. \"Don’t be modest. I heard you saved more than ten heroes’ lives during the monster outbreak. You should be quite proud of yourself.\"","She fell into step beside him as they walked toward the main exit. The corridor was busy with heroes and staff moving between departments.","\"Almost everyone is starting to learn about the hero who saves other heroes,\" she continued, her voice carrying a note of genuine admiration. \"That’s quite the title, you know.\"","Dexter was quite stunned.","’The hero who saves other heroes?’","He hadn’t thought of it that way.","But the title was different than \"the bastard son of the Ashford family\" or \"the man who married three cripples.\"","Dexter smiled faintly but said nothing.","They reached the main entrance. The massive glass doors slid open, letting in the afternoon sunlight and the distant sounds of the city.","A brief silence settled between them as they walked.","Rachel broke the silence first.","\"So,\" she said, tilting her head slightly. \"Where are you heading? Are you going home right now?\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yeah, I just need to pick up a couple of things at the mall before heading home.\"","Rachel’s green eyes brightened. \"Why don’t I take you for lunch? I’m on my break anyway.\" She smiled warmly. \"I know a restaurant nearby.\"","Dexter was stunned.","’ Why do women feel the need to take me for lunch?’","He was supposed to be the one asking women for lunch. But now, for the second time, a woman was asking ’him’ out for a meal. First Violette, now Rachel.","Dexter shook his head. \"No, I have quite a lot of things to do at home.\"","Rachel nodded, her smile dimming slightly. \"Oh, your wives. How are they?\" She forced a smile. \"How are they? I hope the house renovation was up to their standards?\"","Dexter nodded. \"It’s holding quite all right.\"","He paused. He had been about to mention the cabinet incident—how the wall-mounted cabinet had nearly crushed Selene’s skull. But something stopped him.","If he told Rachel about the cabinet, she would immediately offer to inspect the house. She would use it as a reason to visit—citing safety concerns, Association protocols, or follow-up evaluations. And once she was inside the bungalow, Mira, Lyra, and Selene would not let it go.","The first time Rachel had visited, when she hugged him on the porch and mentioned their kiss at the hotel bar, the girls had nearly destroyed the living room.","A second visit would be worse. Especially now that the girls were cultivating again, their powers were growing, and their tolerance for perceived threats to their household had not improved.","And Rachel worked for the Hero Association.","So Dexter said nothing about the cabinet.","\"The house is holding quite all right,\" he repeated. \"The renovation was okay.\"","Rachel nodded. \"All right.\"","She was quiet for a moment, then glanced at him sideways. \"I’m assuming if I offer to drive you home, you would also decline.\"","Her tone was bitter, carrying an edge of accusation.","Dexter replied awkwardly. \"I’m sorry about that, but I’m afraid I have to decline.\"","Then Rachel spoke again in a much quieter tone.","\"So... am I really that difficult to be around?\"","Dexter blinked. He turned to look at her. Her eyes were focused straight ahead, her jaw tight, her posture stiff.","The playful, confident woman who had greeted him at the elevator was gone, replaced by someone more vulnerable—someone who was genuinely asking.","\"What?\" Dexter said.","\"Every time I offer to help, you politely refuse. Lunch, a ride, even a simple conversation.\" She sighed softly, the sound carrying a weight that surprised him. \"It makes me wonder if I’m doing something wrong.\"","Dexter shook his head immediately. \"You’re not.\"","\"Then what is it?\"","He scratched the back of his head awkwardly. The honest answer was complicated, and he wasn’t sure how to deliver it without sounding either arrogant or insulting. But something about Rachel’s expression—the genuine confusion and hurt in her eyes—made him choose honesty over deflection.","\"Because I already have three wives waiting for me at home.\"","Rachel stared at him, her brow creasing. \"What?\"","Dexter continued, his voice measured but firm. \"I don’t want to create misunderstandings.\"","\"Misunderstandings?\"","He nodded. Rachel was silent.","Dexter looked up at the sky. The afternoon sun hung high above the Association compound, casting long shadows across the polished courtyard. He watched a distant hero streak across the sky, leaving a faint trail of light.","\"They’ve already been through enough,\" he said quietly. \"The last thing I want is to make them feel insecure.\"","Rachel frowned. The silence between them stretched for several paces.","Then she spoke, her voice carrying a note of frustration.","\"I just want to be friends,\" she said. \"Simply friends with no strings attached. You’re a good person. You took in three strangers without complaining. Making you one of the rarest men out there with a good heart.\"","She sighed and continued. \" I just want to be friends with a good person like you.\" She turned to face him, her green eyes earnest.","\"How is that going to create a misunderstanding?\"","Dexter frowned as he studied her face carefully, searching for any trace of hidden intent.","\"Just friends?\" he asked. \"Nothing else?\"","Rachel nodded her head confidently. \"Yes. Just friends. Nothing else.\""]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147 | Friends & Purchases","paragraphs":["\"Friends?\"","Dexter eyed her suspiciously. He had a feeling that Rachel’s interest wasn’t purely platonic and why was her cheeks a bit flushed?","But then again, he couldn’t control how others felt. He could only control his own actions.","\"Okay,\" he said finally. \"Just friends then.\"","Rachel’s face lit up with a brilliant smile. \"All right, friend.\"","Then she blinked her eyes innocently. \"Since we’re just friends, can I get your contact information?\" She held up her phone.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","\"My number?\"","Rachel nodded naturally.","\"Friends exchange phone numbers, don’t they? Besides, if anything changes within the Hero Association, I can let you know immediately. And... I can also ask how you’re doing every now and then.\"","Dexter looked at her.","Rachel puffed out her cheeks.","\"It’s just your phone number.\"","He stared at her for another second before finally giving a helpless shrug.","\"...Fine.\"","He recited his phone number. Rachel typed it into her device double-checking each digit before saving.","\"Got it,\" she said, sliding her phone back into her blazer pocket. She looked up at him with a warm smile. \"I’ll text you later, friend.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Goodbye, Rachel.\"","\"Goodbye, Dexter.\"","He turned and walked away to his car.","•••","As Dexter exited the Hero Association’s main gate, the guards saluted him once more. He nodded rode out.","He didn’t head home immediately.","Instead, he pulled up his phone’s GPS and searched for the nearest commercial district. He needed to purchase renovation supplies like paint, tools, fixtures, and building materials. He also needed a few things too.","The GPS displayed a large shopping mall about ten minutes from the Association. Dexter set the route in his vehicle screen as he pressed the pedal.","As he drove, his phone buzzed.","He glanced at the screen.","’[New Message from: Rachel]’","> ’Hey, friend. Drive safe. 😊’","Dexter stared at the message for a long moment. Then he shook his head, pocketed the phone, and focused on the road.","He had lots of things to do, the last thing he needed was another complication.","But as he drove toward the mall, a small, involuntary smile tugged at the corner of his lips.","’ Friends.’","He’d believe it when he saw it.","...","Dexter drove to one of the city’s largest commercial mall.","He parked the ordinary looking SUV in the parking lot.","Then as he entered he saw a few trolleys. He calculated then grabbed two of them.","Then he blinked his eyes, recalculated and then went to grab two more, making four and then began his shopping.","He started with the hardware section.","The house needed extensive work. Mira had cracked the bathroom wall tiles during her spectral arm mishap, so replacement tiles were first on the list. He selected premium ceramic tiles in a soft, neutral tone that would complement the bathroom’s existing color scheme.","From there, the list grew rapidly. He loaded the first trolley with multiple buckets of premium interior wall paint, warm cream for the living room, light gray for the bedrooms, and pure white for the ceilings. He also selected exterior weather-resistant paint in a clean, modern color for the outside walls.","To complete the painting work, he picked up paint rollers, brushes of various sizes, extension poles, paint trays, painter’s tape, protective plastic sheets, sandpaper, scrapers, a folding ladder, gloves, and safety goggles.","Since the wallpaper in several rooms had begun peeling with age, he selected several nice rolls of wallpaper with simple, modern patterns, clean, tasteful designs. He also grabbed wallpaper adhesive and trimming tools.","He moved to the electrical and plumbing section next. Replacement light bulbs, new electrical switches, new curtains, curtain rods, screws, nails, wall anchors, wood filler, silicone sealant, a heavy-duty drill set, screwdrivers, hammers, measuring tape, levels, wrenches, and replacement plumbing fittings all went into the second trolley.","For the backyard, he picked up several pieces of treated lumber to repair the old swing chair that Selene loved.","The chains were corroded, the wooden slats were splintering, and the frame itself was beginning to bow.","He also bought replacement chains, bolts, and weather-resistant wood stain.","Remembering the leaking kitchen roof, he purchased roofing sealant, replacement roofing sheets, insulation material, and waterproof coating.","Dexter sighed as he walked back to admire the various tools here. he washed he could take them all back home and test them and also figure out their uses!","Sadly he couldn’t afford to spend so much money.","The garden section was closed so he thought for a bit and picked up a few flower pots, bags of garden soil, and several flowering plants, marigolds, lavender, and a small hydrangea bush to make the front yard feel more welcoming. The bungalow’s exterior was dull and unwelcoming. A few plants wouldn’t transform it into a mansion, but they would at least make it look nice.","The third trolley was for necessities.","The massage oil he had been using on Mira was almost finished. He picked up two new bottles of premium grade massage oil, soothing, and can easily transmit mana from finger tips to the muscles.","Then his eyes caught something on a nearby shelf.","’Massage Glove 3000 Pro.’","Dexter picked up the box and read the description.","The glove was a device designed for deep tissue massage, with multiple intensity settings and vibration modes.","It claimed to be 300% more efficient than ordinary hands at penetrating deep into muscle tissue, stimulating blood flow, and accelerating nerve recovery. It was expensive—$8,000—but the potential benefit for Mira’s physical therapy was significant.","He added it to the trolley.","He also picked up extra electric toothbrushes, a new set for the girls and a replacement for himself.","He grabbed shaving cream and a high-quality shaving kit for his growing beard and mustache, which had begun to itch annoyingly.","’That should be all right?’","Dexter pondered and shrugged as he walked towards the checkout. But then, he passed the food section and he immediately thought of Lyra.","’I should probably get a few things for her.’"]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148 | I’m Back!","paragraphs":["’I should probably get a few snacks for her.’","Dexter packed an assortment of snacks—chips, cookies, dried fruit, crackers, several tubs of premium ice cream in various flavors, and also, soda cans.","Lyra’s appetite was bottomless, and having quick snacks available would keep her satisfied between meals without requiring him to cook every time she got hungry.","The girls were all cultivating a Tier-7 technique now, which meant their bodies could process and expel impurities and excess calories through their cultivation. The energy of the Grand Cosmos Scripture would naturally cleanse their systems, so the junk food wouldn’t negatively affect their health or their figures. Dexter wasn’t worried about that.","He also picked up cooking ingredients for the bakery business, ordinary ingredients only. He was not going to use his precious Heavenly Treasures or Diamond Spirit Rice for commercial meals.","It would simply be an astronomical waste.","The meals he sold to customers would be made with standard, high-quality market ingredients, enhanced by his Great Grandmaster Foodsmith skills.","Even with ordinary ingredients, his cooking would produce Grade-One, Grade-Two meals or even Grade-three meals.","He purchased large quantities of vegetables, rice, cooking oil, spices, seasonings, and several large cooking pots for commercial-scale preparation.","By the time he was done, he had filled four trolleys to the brim.","He pushed all four to the checkout counter, where a bored clerk began scanning items.","The total appeared on the display.","$40,419.99","Dexter paid with his phone, received the receipt, and then flipped his right hand.","Golden light flashed, and all four trolleys’ worth of items vanished into his storage ring in a flash.","\"W-what?\"","The cashier froze. Her scanner hovered mid-air over the last item. The couple behind Dexter in line was stunned.","A storage ring. was an artifact only high level heroes possess!","Which meant that the man in the plain dark shirt and joggers was also a high level hero!","Dexter ignored the stunned stares, pocketed his receipt, and walked out to the parking lot.","•••","He pulled up his phone and searched for exotic beast meat suppliers. Then he selected one close by. It was a massive, warehouse-style establishment about fifteen minutes from the mall.","[Primordial Harvest: Exotic Beast Meat & Dungeon Resources]","Dexter drove there and arrived within twenty minutes. The building was enormous, it looked like a proper company instead of a butchers place.","He walked inside.","The inside was cold but clean and the place was painted stainless white too, looking eerily like an horror movie company.","Massive refrigerated display cases lined the walls, each one containing cuts of meat that ranged from ordinary-looking beef to flesh that glowed.","A receptionist who was a young man in a clean white coat greeted him from behind a polished counter.","\"Welcome to Primordial Harvest. How can I assist you?\"","\"I want to buy Mutated Class beast meat,\" Dexter nodded and replied.","The receptionist nodded professionally. \"Certainly, sir. We sell Mutated Class beast meat by the kilogram. Our current inventory ranges from Level 1 to Level 12, with prices scaling accordingly.\"","He pulled up a holographic catalog, displaying rows of available cuts with images, classifications, and prices.","Mutated Class Beast Meat (Standard Grade):","- Level 1 — $1,000/kg","- Level 2 — $2,000/kg","- Level 3 — $3,000/kg","- Level 12 — $12,000/kg","Premium Mutated Class Beast Meat (Exceptional Nutrition/Rare Bloodline):","- Level 1 — $2,000/kg","- Level 2 — $4,000/kg","- Level 12 — $24,000/kg","Dexter studied the prices as he calculated in his mind. Mutated Class beast meat was the most affordable tier—the meat of monsters from the lowest classification of dimensional gates. Even at these prices, it was still incredibly expensive compared to ordinary meat. A single kilogram of Level 1 meat cost as much as a month’s groceries for a normal family.","No wonder killing monsters and selling their corpses was the most lucrative business in the hero world. Well, apart from the Only Heroes website. (^o^)","Their bodies alone were worth fortunes. A single Level 3 goblin corpse—of which Dexter had killed dozens during the outbreak—would have been worth thousands in meat alone, not counting the nexus core.","\"What about Fiend Class?\" Dexter asked.","The receptionist smiled, clearly expecting the question. He scrolled to a different section of the catalog.","Fiend Class Beast Meat (Standard Grade):","- Level 1 — $3,000/kg","- Level 2 — $6,000/kg","- Level 3 — $9,000/kg","- Level 12 — $36,000/kg","Fiend Class meat was three times more expensive than Mutated Class. The meat was denser, richer in mana, and possessed significantly greater nutritional and restorative properties.","Dexter made his selections quickly.","\"Twenty kilograms of Level 1 Mutated Class Berserk Muscular Cow Meat,\" he said. The Berserk Muscular Cow was a common Mutated Class beast essentially a mutated bison with enhanced muscle density. Its meat was lean, protein-rich, and carried a mild mana signature that was easy to work with.","\"Twenty kilograms of Level 1 Fiend Class Twin-Headed Turkey Meat,\" he added. The Twin-Headed Turkey was a Fiend Class creature whose meat was renowned for its restorative properties—particularly its ability to nourish damaged meridians and accelerate nerve regeneration.","This was for the girls. He had been feeding them ordinary market meat. If he incorporated Fiend Class meat into their daily meals, the grade of his cooking would increase significantly, and the nutritional benefits would accelerate their healing.","The receptionist processed the order.","20 kg × $1,000/kg = $20,000 (Mutated Class)","20 kg × $3,000/kg = $60,000 (Fiend Class)","Total: $80,000","Dexter felt a paid in his heart as he paid the money.","A year ago, that sum would have been more money than he had earned in his entire life combined. Now, it was an investment that would return a 100 fold.","He stored the meat in his spatial ring alongside the renovation supplies and walked out of Primordial Harvest.","’If I stayed in the market any longer, I might start buying things neither the girls nor I actually need,’","•••","The drive back was uneventful.","He arrived at Fenmore Street twenty minutes later and parked the Vehicle in front of his bungalow. As he stepped out of the vehicle, his eyes caught movement across the street.","Tessa’s father, Henry, was also just returning home, carrying several large bags of flour on each shoulder with ease.","He had probably just returned from a supply run for the bakery.","The two men’s eyes met and Dexter nodded politely.","Henry returned the nod with a small smile. Then he turned and carried his flour bags inside the bakery.","Dexter wanted to actually walk over and discuss the food business, finalize the details, and coordinate the timeline for their trial run. But seeing the bags of flour and the fatigue on Henry’s face, he decided against interrupting him.","’Maybe later.’","Dexter opened the small gate and walked to up to the door.","The bungalow was quiet but he could hear Mira’s breathing from the living room, Lyra’s soft purring from the bedroom, and Selene’s breath from the backyard.","\"I’m back!\"","[A/N: Special thanks to reader MICHA_LOEWENSTEIN for the gift!!!❤️‍🔥❤️‍🔥❤️‍🔥]","[I genuinely think this book might stand a chance at getting third place in the competition at the end of this month!😊]","[Thanks you once more!]"]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149 | Fixing The House","paragraphs":["Mira was sitting in her wheelchair by the living room window, exactly where he had left her. Her head was tilted slightly toward the glass, her crimson eyes watching nothing in particular.","At the sound of his voice, she briefly glanced in his direction before closing her eyes again and returning to her own world without a single word.","Dexter shook his head slightly. ’ Same as always.’","He walked further inside and found Lyra standing in the doorway of her room. Her AI smart glasses blinked slightly. The moment she saw him, her dark eyes brightened.","’ You’re back.’","She said in his mind but she was looking at him with wide eyed and with an expectant gaze as her body leaned er body forward just a fraction, as though she were waiting for something.","Dexter understood what she meant but he simply smiled and said nothing.","He had indeed bought snacks of various varieties for her but he wasn’t going to give it to her just yet.","’ Let her wait a little. It’ll make it sweeter.’","He turned away from Lyra’s hopeful stare and walked through the hallway toward the backyard to check up on Selene. He open the rear door, he found Selene.","Her silver-white hair hung loose over her shoulders as she sat on the swing cultivation with her palms on her laps and upwards.","She turned her head toward the sound and nodded slightly.","\"Welcome back.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Thanks.\"","before nodding once and heading back inside.","He walked to the storage room near the back of the house and began unloading everything he had purchased. One by one, he pulled each item from his spatial storage and arranged them neatly against the wall, cataloguing everything in his mind.","Then he got to work.","He started with the tiles.","The kitchen floor had several cracked and loose tiles that had been bothering him since the first day they moved in. He pried them up carefully, scraped away the old adhesive, and laid down fresh grout before pressing the new tiles into place one by one.","From the kitchen, he moved to the bathroom. The wall above the shower fixture had a section where the old tiles had completely fallen away, leaving an ugly patch of exposed concrete. He measured the gap, cut the replacement tiles to size, and fitted them snugly into the wall. He grouted the seams, wiped away the excess, and stepped back to inspect his work.","It was clean and looked professional.","Dexter wasn’t a trained contractor, but he was no stranger to manual labor. Growing up in the Ashford estate as little more than a servant, he had been forced to perform nearly every odd job imaginable. Serving food, washing floors, scrubbing dishes, mending fences, repairing roofs and yes, construction work.","Whenever something in the estate needed fixing, the Head Servants pocket the money to call professionals and give the job to the servants to fix instead.","Over the years, he had learned to work with his hands out of pure necessity and that experience had made him versatile. Tiling, painting, carpentry, basic plumbing — he could do all of it. Not perfectly, but well enough.","After finishing the bathroom, he moved on to the wallpaper. He carefully stripped the damaged sections, applied fresh adhesive, and pressed the new wallpaper flat against the walls, smoothing out every air bubble with a clean cloth. Then he moved to the bedroom and repeated the process.","Once the wallpaper was done, he opened the cans of paint. A soft, warm white for the kitchen to make the small space feel brighter. A light grey for the bathroom.","Slowly, the rooms began to transform, becoming neater and cleaner.","Just like that, two hours passed.","\"Riiiiing!\"","Dexter checked his phone.","[Alarm; Make lunch for ’Wives?’]","Dexter set down the paint roller and wiped his hands on a rag. It was time to make lunch.","He washed up in the backyard tap, changed into a clean shirt, and walked into the kitchen. Lyra was already there. She had followed him from the moment he entered the kitchen and now sat on a small stool near the counter, watching him with sharp, unblinking eyes.","Dexter glanced at her. \"You’re going to watch me the entire time?\"","She nodded without a shred of shame.","He sighed and pulled out the ingredients.","Today’s lunch was going to be special.","Fiend-Class meat was rich in mana and possessed a naturally savory, deeply complex flavor that ordinary beef or pork could never match.","Dexter seasoned the meat carefully, using a blend of herbs and spices then seared it in the Type-II Cooking Pot until the surface caramelized beautifully, then reduced the heat and let it simmer in its own juices alongside fresh vegetables and a portion of Diamond Rice.","The kitchen filled with an incredible aroma and the smell was so intense that even Mira, sitting in the living room with her eyes closed, unconsciously turned her head toward the kitchen.","Dexter plated the meals. Four bowls of steaming rice, each topped with thick slices of the seared Fiend-Class meat and a ladle of the rich cooking broth.","He paused, studying the food carefully.","[Grade 4 Meal]","He had expected the Fiend-Class meat to push the meal’s grade higher. Perhaps even to Grade Five. If it had reached Grade Five, then there might have been tribulation lightning.","But nothing happened.","Dexter blinked in mild disappointment, then simply shrugged.","’Grade Four is still excellent. I’ll try again another time.’","He carried the bowls to the dining table and called the girls.","They gathered quickly. Lyra was already in her seat before Dexter had finished setting the last bowl down.","Mira wheeled herself to the table with the help of her Spectral Arms, Selene walked in last.","Then they all ate in silence.","Lyra of course was intensely focused on her food.","Selene ate slowly but somehow consumed the meal quickly as her pale face has a tint of red in them.","And, Mira was also eating speedily despite the fact that she was using her spectral arm.","Dexter watched them from across the table, a quiet pride swelling in his chest. As a cook, there was no greater compliment than seeing someone lose themselves entirely in a meal he had prepared.","\"I have something to tell you,\" Dexter said.","Mira eyed him while Selene tilted her head upwards and Lyra continued focusing on her food.","\"I’ve arranged a business partnership with Tessa and her father,\" Dexter said. \"They own the bakery on the corner. I’ll be preparing a few portions of my meals each day, and they’ll sell them at the bakery on a trial basis.\"","He paused.","\"If it sells, great. If it doesn’t, then that’s it for my plan.\"","The room was quiet for a moment.","Then Lyra’s brows furrowed as she pouted.","’You want to cook for other people?’","Dexter smiled.","\"Not particularly. I’m exchanging my services for money. Selling Enchanted Meals is a lucrative business, Lyra. And since I can cook, I decided to try it.\"","Lyra’s blinked her eyes as her deepened and she focused in her food but she was slower this time.","Mira, on the other hand spoke in her usual flat tone.","\"Do what you want.\"","Selene nodded slowly. \"That’s a nice idea, Dexter. I’m sure you’ll do well.\"","Dexter smiled. \"Thank you, Selene.\"","The girls gradually dispersed after their meal.","But Lyra remained in the kitchen doorway, her arms crossed, her pout still firmly in place.","Dexter looked at her then, with a flick of his wrist, a bag of snack materialized in his hands.","Lyra’s eyes widened and the pout vanished instantly as her hands shot forward with speed.","Then she looked up at him, and for the briefest moment, a faint smile tugged at the corner of her lips.","’Thank you Dexter. Good luck on your business.’","Then she turned and hurried toward the living room couch, already tearing open the bag of chips before she even sat down.","Dexter watched her go, shaking his head with a quiet chuckle.","’That girl and her food.’","[A/N: Y’all continue to stun me with your gifts. I’m really grateful for the gifts, everyone. It’s a really great boost. Especially SKYLER_WILLIAMS. Many thanks! Will dedicate a few Chapters for each of you. Look forward to it!]"]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150 | Deep Tissue Massage","paragraphs":["After finishing the dishes, Dexter dried his hands and walked into the living room, directly towards Mira. He stopped behind her wheelchair and unlocked the brakes.","Mira’s eyes snapped open. She turned her head and glared at him with slight irritation.","\"I’m beginning to think you look forward to this every day.\"","Dexter snorted lightly. \"I’ve touched better.\"","Mira glare intensified as she her eyes narrowed into a dangerous slit. \"What are you trying to say.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and sneered. \"You know what I mean, brat.\"","Mira clenched her teeth. \"I’m older than you...\"","Dexter shrugged. \"Yet you act like a naughty kid.\"","Her eyes were practically blazing with flames as she huffed and stared at Dexter.","Dexter had long since grown immune to her death glares. He gripped the handles of her wheelchair and steered her away from the window and into her bedroom.","He parked the wheelchair beside the bed, then carefully lifted her in his arms and gently lowered onto the center of the mattress, then reached into his spatial storage.","He brought out the new massage oil today and also the a specialized massaging glove.","The glove was incredibly thin and flexible. When he wore it, they fit snugly over his hands.","The glove had multiple vibration settings, At its lowest setting, it produced a gentle hum barely stronger than a phone’s notification.","At its highest, it could deliver deep, penetrating vibrations that reached all the way to the bone.","Combined with his Tier-2 36 Styles Massage Technique, the glove would immediately amplify the effectiveness of the massage.","Dexter reached for the hem of Mira’s shirt, lifted her torso just enough to pull the shirt over her head, then removed her skirt, leaving her in a plain sports bra and sport briefs.","Her skin was pale and smooth, almost looking as though it hadn’t been in the sun at all. Afterwards, he positioned her face-down on the bed with her arms resting at her sides and her face turned to one side against the pillow.","He poured a measure of warm massage oil into his palm and then he began, starting with her shoulders.","Since he was using it for the first time, he set the gloves to its lowest vibration, pressing his oiled fingers into the dense muscle where her neck met her shoulders.","Activating the 36 Styles Technique, mana surged through his finger tips as he followed the pattern of the technique.","At first, the vibration was so subtle that Mira wasnt able to feel it.","Seeing that she wasn’t complaining, Dexter gradually increased the intensity.","The humming grew a bit louder as the vibrations penetrated deeper into her tissue.","At that moment, Mira felt something and her eyes immediately flew open as she muttered.","\"What are you doing?\" she muttered.","Dexter didn’t look at her and continued with his work.","\"I bought a massaging glove. It increases the effectiveness of the massage by roughly 300 percent.\"","He paused, then added without thinking, \"You’ll feel more comfortable and relaxed than before.\"","The tips of Mira’s ears turned a faint shade of pink.","But Dexter noticed it and he blinked.","’Her blood circulation is certainly improving.’","His hands moved from her shoulders down to her upper back. As he worked the muscles along her spine, her shoulder blades and her lower back.","Mana seeped into every section, stimulating weakened nerves while gently encouraging circulation throughout her body.","He moved to her neck and cradled her head gently in one hand and worked the muscles at the base of her skull with the other.","These were the most sensitive areas, the ones closest to the site of her spinal injury. He increased the vibration slightly and channeled a thin thread of mana through his fingertips, letting it seep into the damaged nerve endings.","Dexter continued down her spine.","From the middle of her back, he carefully worked lower before returning to the muscles surrounding her waist, making sure not to apply unnecessary force directly onto the spine itself.","Without realizing it, Mira’s breathing had become quieter than before.","He worked vertebra by vertebra, pressing and rolling and vibrating the muscles on either side of her spinal column.","The 36 Styles Technique guided his mana into the damaged pathways, gently coaxing the severed nerve endings to remember what it felt like to carry a signal.","He reached the dimples at the base of her spine, where her lower back met her hips. He pressed deep, using the heel of his palm combined with the glove’s vibration to work the thick muscle tissue there.","Once he finished with her back, Dexter moved to her arms.","He stretched each finger individually before working through her palms, wrists, forearms, elbows, and upper arms, ensuring every muscle received equal attention.","Only after finishing both arms did he continue to her legs.","Beginning with her feet, he gently massaged each toe before moving across the soles of her feet. The vibration from the glove combined with the flowing mana to relax muscles that had remained inactive for years.","Slowly, he worked upward through her calves before reaching her thighs, then her upper thigh as the gloves vibrated, hitting deep within her tissue.","\"Hmm...\"","Mira unconsciously let out a soft breath.","Dexter frowned slightly.","\"Too much vibration?\"","\"...No.\"","Taking that as confirmation, he continued until both legs had been thoroughly treated.","Finally, he wiped away the excess massage oil with a warm towel before carefully helping Mira turn onto her back.","The moment she faced him, Dexter blinked.","Her cheeks were completely red.","Even the tips of her ears and her neck had turned a noticeable shade of crimson.","She stared directly at him.","\"...\"","\"...\"","Dexter tilted his head in confusion.","\"What’s wrong?\" he asked, his brow furrowing with concern. \"Are you running a fever? Your face is completely red.\"","Mira’s glare intensified.","\"You’re asking ’me’ if something is wrong?\" she hissed through clenched teeth.","Dexter blinked. \"Yes? Because your face is—\"","\"Nothing. Just continue.\"","[A/N: Many thanks once more to those who supported with gifts. I truly appreciate! And those with golden tickets and powerstones, Thank You!!!]"]}]);
